      *> Generated by Rosetta: COBOL bindings for the C++ module
      *>   datamunge. COPY this copybook into WORKING-STORAGE; COPY
      *>   "datamunge-callbacks.cpy" into the LINKAGE SECTION of
      *>   programs that C++ calls back.
      *> Each call has a parameter record: fill its fields, then CALL
      *>   its entry USING the record and DM-STATUS. RETURN-CODE and
      *>   DM-STATUS-CODE receive 0 or the error kind; DM-STATUS-MESSAGE
      *>   says what failed. STOP RUN exits with RETURN-CODE, so MOVE 0
      *>   TO RETURN-CODE after an expected failure.
      *> Fields have their C++ types' exact sizes. Strings are PIC
      *>   X(256) fields with a -LENGTH: -1 sends the text without
      *>   trailing spaces, 0 to 256 sends that many bytes; results set
      *>   it (a call's string results are PIC X(16384)). Calls with C++
      *>   defaults have a -GIVEN count of the arguments to send.
      *>   Objects and containers are handles (BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED, 0
      *>   for null): close each with CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE
      *>   DM-STATUS.
      *> Doc comments (*>>) carry the C++ documentation: the first lines
      *>   of a record's block are its C++ signature and its CALL
      *>   statements.

      *>> The status of the last call. Every call sets it (pass OMITTED
      *>>   to skip it).
       01 DM-STATUS.
      *>> 0 after a successful call; otherwise the error kind.
          05 DM-STATUS-CODE USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
             88 DM-STATUS-OK VALUE 0.
             88 DM-STATUS-ALLOCATION VALUE 1.
             88 DM-STATUS-RANGE VALUE 2.
             88 DM-STATUS-INDEX VALUE 3.
             88 DM-STATUS-ARGUMENT VALUE 4.
             88 DM-STATUS-NATIVE VALUE 5.
             88 DM-STATUS-CLOSED VALUE 6.
             88 DM-STATUS-CALLBACK VALUE 7.
      *>> The kind in lower case: allocation, range, index, argument,
      *>>   native, closed or callback.
          05 DM-STATUS-KIND PIC X(10) VALUE SPACES.
      *>> Bytes of -MESSAGE used.
          05 DM-STATUS-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> The error message: the call and what went wrong.
          05 DM-STATUS-MESSAGE PIC X(512) VALUE SPACES.

      *>> Any handle: object, container or function.
      *>> CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS (destroys its
      *>>   object; closing twice is harmless)
      *>> CALL "dm_handle_type" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS (sets -TYPE)
      *>> CALL "dm_handle_open" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS (sets -OPEN)
       01 DM-HANDLE.
      *>> The handle.
          05 DM-HANDLE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Its type (from the type call).
          05 DM-HANDLE-TYPE PIC X(256).
          05 DM-HANDLE-TYPE-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> 1 while the handle is open (from the open call).
          05 DM-HANDLE-OPEN USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.

      *>> C++ enum datamunge::algebra::MonomialOrder (MONOMIAL-ORDER
      *>>   fields).
      *>>
      *>> Monomial orderings supported for multivariate polynomial
      *>>   leading-term selection.
      *>> Lex: pure lexicographic (variable 0 dominates). Grlex: total
      *>>   degree first, then
      *>> lexicographic to break ties. Grevlex: total degree first, then
      *>>   REVERSE
      *>> lexicographic (smallest trailing-variable exponent wins) to
      *>>   break ties -- the usual
      *>> default for Groebner basis computations since it tends to keep
      *>>   intermediate
      *>> polynomials smaller than Grlex.
       78 DM-MONOMIAL-ORDER-LEX VALUE 0.
       78 DM-MONOMIAL-ORDER-GRLEX VALUE 1.
       78 DM-MONOMIAL-ORDER-GREVLEX VALUE 2.

      *>> C++ enum datamunge::cv::StructuringElement
      *>>   (STRUCTURING-ELEMENT fields).
      *>>
      *>> The neighborhood shape morphological operations probe around
      *>>   each pixel.
       78 DM-STRUCTURING-ELEMENT-SQUARE VALUE 0.
       78 DM-STRUCTURING-ELEMENT-CROSS VALUE 1.

      *>> C++ enum datamunge::fda::SplineSolver (SPLINE-SOLVER fields).
      *>>
      *>> Linear-system method used by the spline least-squares fits.
      *>>
      *>> Every fit forms symmetric normal equations (B^T B + P) c = B^T
      *>>   y. Cholesky is exact but
      *>> costs O(K^3) for K unknowns; conjugate gradient on the sparse
      *>>   system costs roughly
      *>> O(nnz) per iteration and suits large, well-conditioned
      *>>   (usually penalized) systems.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::SplineSolveOptions
      *>>   options{dm::fda::SplineSolver::ConjugateGradient};
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: SplineSolveOptions
       78 DM-SPLINE-SOLVER-AUTOMATIC VALUE 0.
       78 DM-SPLINE-SOLVER-CHOLESKY VALUE 1.
       78 DM-SPLINE-SOLVER-CONJUGATE-GRADIENT VALUE 2.

      *>> C++ enum datamunge::fem::BCType (BC-TYPE fields).
      *>>
      *>> Select an endpoint value or an outward-conormal natural
      *>>   boundary condition.
      *>> The conormal p*du/dn uses -u' at the left and +u' at the
      *>>   right. Physical
      *>> diffusive outward flux is its negative; these are different
      *>>   sign conventions.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> std::print("{}\n",dm::fem::BCType::Neumann); // Neumann
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: BoundaryCondition1D
       78 DM-BC-TYPE-DIRICHLET VALUE 0.
       78 DM-BC-TYPE-NEUMANN VALUE 1.
       78 DM-BC-TYPE-ROBIN VALUE 2.

      *>> C++ enum datamunge::geometry::DTWPredecessor (DTW-PREDECESSOR
      *>>   fields).
      *>>
      *>> Selected predecessor of an actual positive DTW cell.
      *>> advance_a changes the first coordinate, advance_b the second.
      *>>   Finite ties
      *>> prefer diagonal, then advance_a, then advance_b.
      *>>   Unrepresentable accumulated
      *>> costs have no finite predecessor witness; successful traceback
      *>>   never uses them.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   t=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_trace({1},{1});
      *>> std::print("{}\n",t.predecessors[0]==dm::geometry::DTWPredecessor::origin);
      *>>   // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: DTWTrace
       78 DM-DTW-PREDECESSOR-ORIGIN VALUE 0.
       78 DM-DTW-PREDECESSOR-DIAGONAL VALUE 1.
       78 DM-DTW-PREDECESSOR-ADVANCE-A VALUE 2.
       78 DM-DTW-PREDECESSOR-ADVANCE-B VALUE 3.
       78 DM-DTW-PREDECESSOR-UNREPRESENTABLE VALUE 4.

      *>> C++ enum datamunge::geometry::HullAction (HULL-ACTION fields).
      *>>
      *>> Actual constant-size stack event; no full stack snapshots are
      *>>   copied.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> std::cout <<
      *>>   (dm::geometry::HullAction::pop==dm::geometry::HullAction::pop);
      *>>   // 1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: HullEvent
       78 DM-HULL-ACTION-TEST VALUE 0.
       78 DM-HULL-ACTION-POP VALUE 1.
       78 DM-HULL-ACTION-PUSH VALUE 2.

      *>> C++ enum datamunge::geometry::HullPass (HULL-PASS fields).
