      *>> C++ enum datamunge::sim::Task (TASK fields).
      *>>
      *>> Built-in native rigid-body control task, using SI units and
      *>>   Y-up coordinates.
      *>> These are datamunge task definitions, not numerical replicas
      *>>   of another simulator.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto task=dm::sim::Task::InvertedPendulum;
      *>> ```
       78 DM-TASK-INVERTED-PENDULUM VALUE 0.
       78 DM-TASK-HOPPER VALUE 1.

      *>> C++ enum datamunge::stats::Alternative (ALTERNATIVE fields).
      *>>
      *>> Prespecified tail of a test's null reference, like R's
      *>>   alternative argument.
      *>> Location/proportion alternatives refer to the signed effect;
      *>>   KS alternatives refer
      *>> to empirical CDF ordering and consequently reverse the
      *>>   stochastic-location direction.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto a=dm::stats::Alternative::Less;
      *>> const auto t=dm::stats::t_test_one_sample({1,2,3,4},0,a);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",t.alternative==a); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> -
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/t.test.html
      *>>
      *>> See also: HypothesisTestResult
       78 DM-ALTERNATIVE-TWO-SIDED VALUE 0.
       78 DM-ALTERNATIVE-LESS VALUE 1.
       78 DM-ALTERNATIVE-GREATER VALUE 2.

      *>> C++ enum datamunge::stats::PAdjustMethod (P-ADJUST-METHOD
      *>>   fields).
      *>>
      *>> Multiple-comparison p-value adjustment methods, matching R's
      *>>   p.adjust.methods.
      *>> Bonferroni/Holm/Hochberg/Hommel control the family-wise error
      *>>   rate (FWER); BH/BY
      *>> control the false discovery rate (FDR); None returns the
      *>>   p-values unchanged.
       78 DM-P-ADJUST-METHOD-BONFERRONI VALUE 0.
       78 DM-P-ADJUST-METHOD-HOLM VALUE 1.
       78 DM-P-ADJUST-METHOD-HOCHBERG VALUE 2.
       78 DM-P-ADJUST-METHOD-HOMMEL VALUE 3.
       78 DM-P-ADJUST-METHOD-BH VALUE 4.
       78 DM-P-ADJUST-METHOD-BY VALUE 5.
       78 DM-P-ADJUST-METHOD-NONE VALUE 6.

