      *>> datamunge::algebra::Expr::Expr() -> EXPR handle
      *>> CALL "dm_expr_new" USING DM-EXPR-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::algebra::Expr. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A symbolic expression tree over +, -, *, /, ^ (power) and
      *>>   sin/cos/exp/log, supporting
      *>> symbolic differentiation, basic algebraic simplification, and
      *>>   numeric evaluation.
      *>> Value type wrapping a shared, immutable node tree -- copies
      *>>   are cheap and structural
      *>> sharing across copies is always safe since nodes are never
      *>>   mutated after
      *>> construction.
       01 DM-EXPR-NEW.
      *>> Result: EXPR handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-EXPR-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::algebra::Expr::Expr(double value) -> EXPR handle
      *>> CALL "dm_expr_new_double" USING DM-EXPR-NEW-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::algebra::Expr. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A symbolic expression tree over +, -, *, /, ^ (power) and
      *>>   sin/cos/exp/log, supporting
      *>> symbolic differentiation, basic algebraic simplification, and
      *>>   numeric evaluation.
      *>> Value type wrapping a shared, immutable node tree -- copies
      *>>   are cheap and structural
      *>> sharing across copies is always safe since nodes are never
      *>>   mutated after
      *>> construction.
      *>>
      *>> Construct a symbolic constant from a C++ numeric value,
      *>>   including implicit conversion.
      *>>
      *>> Numeric arguments convert to double, matching constant();
      *>>   integers larger than double's
      *>> exact integer range may round. Infinity and NaN are accepted.
      *>>   The new immutable node
      *>> owns its value. Enables literals on either side of expression
      *>>   operators and assignment
      *>> such as Expr f = 1. Does not add a conversion from Expr back
      *>>   to a number; use evaluate().
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::algebra::Expr value = 2.5;
      *>> std::print("{}\n", value.evaluate({}, {})); // 2.5
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::bad_alloc: If the constant node cannot be allocated.
      *>>
      *>> See also: constant(), evaluate()
       01 DM-EXPR-NEW-DOUBLE.
      *>> Value (double): double. Numeric constant, stored as a double
      *>>   without evaluation or simplification.
          05 DM-EXPR-NEW-DOUBLE-VALUE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result: EXPR handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-EXPR-NEW-DOUBLE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

