      *>> datamunge::algebra::Expr::differentiate(const std::string &
      *>>   var) const -> Expr
      *>> CALL "dm_expr_differentiate" USING DM-EXPR-DIFFERENTIATE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The symbolic derivative with respect to `var` (any other
      *>>   variable name is
      *>> treated as a constant).
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: if the expression contains `base ^
      *>>   exponent` where `exponent` is not a constant (only the
      *>>   constant-exponent power rule is supported).
       01 DM-EXPR-DIFFERENTIATE.
      *>> Self: the EXPR handle.
          05 DM-EXPR-DIFFERENTIATE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> var (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-EXPR-DIFFERENTIATE-VAR PIC X(256).
          05 DM-EXPR-DIFFERENTIATE-VAR-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> Result (Expr): EXPR handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-EXPR-DIFFERENTIATE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::algebra::Expr::integrate(const std::string & var)
      *>>   const -> Expr
      *>> CALL "dm_expr_integrate" USING DM-EXPR-INTEGRATE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The symbolic antiderivative with respect to `var` (any other
      *>>   variable name is
      *>> treated as a constant, matching differentiate()). Supports:
      *>>   the sum/difference
      *>> and constant-multiple rules; the power rule x^c (any real c !=
      *>>   -1) and its log
      *>> special case (c == -1); sin/cos/exp/log of any expression that
      *>>   is affine
      *>> (a*var + b) in var, via the standard substitution result for
      *>>   each; a constant
      *>> divided by an affine expression (reduces to the log rule);
      *>>   and, for a product of
      *>> two var-dependent factors, generic tabular integration by
      *>>   parts -- reusing
      *>> differentiate() to peel one factor down to the constant 0
      *>>   across at most 15
      *>> repeated derivatives (terminates for any genuine polynomial
      *>>   factor), paired with
      *>> repeated antiderivatives of the other factor. Not a full
      *>>   computer-algebra
      *>> integrator: general rational functions (a non-constant
      *>>   denominator that isn't
      *>> affine), a variable exponent, and products/quotients outside
      *>>   the forms above
      *>> (e.g. sin(x)*cos(x), which never reduces to zero under
      *>>   repeated differentiation)
      *>> are not attempted.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: when no rule above applies.
       01 DM-EXPR-INTEGRATE.
      *>> Self: the EXPR handle.
          05 DM-EXPR-INTEGRATE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> var (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-EXPR-INTEGRATE-VAR PIC X(256).
          05 DM-EXPR-INTEGRATE-VAR-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> Result (Expr): EXPR handle (new; close it).
