      *>   IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING

      *>> datamunge::bayes::ImportanceSampling::ImportanceSampling(ImportanceSamplingOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING handle
      *>> CALL "dm_importance_sampling_new" USING
      *>>   DM-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::bayes::ImportanceSampling. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Importance sampling against a multivariate Gaussian proposal
      *>>   N(mean, covariance) --
      *>> a natural choice when a Laplace approximation is available and
      *>>   reasonably close to
      *>> the target's shape (e.g. bayes::MAP's mode paired with a
      *>>   numerically estimated
      *>> Hessian there). Produces a weighted i.i.d. sample in one shot
      *>>   rather than a Markov
      *>> chain -- no warmup, nothing to check for mixing -- but
      *>>   accuracy depends entirely on
      *>> how well the Gaussian proposal covers the target's mass;
      *>>   effective_sample_size is
      *>> the diagnostic to check before trusting the result.
      *>>
      *>> Stores the sampler settings.
       01 DM-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (ImportanceSamplingOptions = {}):
      *>>   IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING-OPTIONS handle. Sampler settings.
          05 DM-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::bayes::ImportanceSampling::sample(optim::ArbitraryFunction
      *>>   & log_target, const std::vector<double> & proposal_mean,
