      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   NUTS

      *>> datamunge::bayes::NUTS::NUTS(NUTSOptions options = {}) -> NUTS
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_nuts_new" USING DM-NUTS-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::bayes::NUTS. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> The No-U-Turn Sampler (Hoffman & Gelman 2014, the efficient
      *>>   slice-sampling
      *>> variant, Algorithm 3): Hamiltonian Monte Carlo with an
      *>>   automatically chosen
      *>> trajectory length -- the leapfrog trajectory is grown by
      *>>   repeated doubling until
      *>> it would start turning back on itself (a "U-turn"), removing
      *>>   the need to hand-tune
      *>> a fixed number of leapfrog steps. Step size is still adapted
      *>>   via the same
      *>> dual-averaging scheme as HMC. Uses an identity mass matrix.
      *>>
      *>> Stores the sampler settings.
       01 DM-NUTS-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-NUTS-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (NUTSOptions = {}): NUTS-OPTIONS handle. Sampler
      *>>   settings.
          05 DM-NUTS-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: NUTS handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-NUTS-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::bayes::NUTS::sample(optim::DifferentiableFunction &
      *>>   log_posterior, const std::vector<double> & initial_params)
      *>>   const -> NUTSResult
      *>> CALL "dm_nuts_sample" USING DM-NUTS-SAMPLE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Runs one chain: warmup with step-size adaptation, then
      *>>   num_samples draws.
       01 DM-NUTS-SAMPLE.
      *>> Self: the NUTS handle.
          05 DM-NUTS-SAMPLE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> log_posterior (optim::DifferentiableFunction &):
      *>>   DIFFERENTIABLE-FUNCTION handle. Log density (up to a
      *>>   constant) and its gradient.
          05 DM-NUTS-SAMPLE-LOG-POSTERIOR USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> initial_params (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Starting point on the unconstrained scale.
          05 DM-NUTS-SAMPLE-INITIAL-PARAMS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (NUTSResult): NUTS-RESULT handle (new; close it). Draws
      *>>   plus acceptance, step size and per-draw diagnostics.
          05 DM-NUTS-SAMPLE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

