      *>> bool datamunge::bayes::RWMOptions::adapt_covariance
      *>> CALL "dm_rwm_options_adapt_covariance_get" USING
      *>>   DM-RWM-OPTIONS-ADAPT-COVARIANCE DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_rwm_options_adapt_covariance_set" USING
      *>>   DM-RWM-OPTIONS-ADAPT-COVARIANCE DM-STATUS (writes -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Learn a proposal covariance during warmup (adaptive
      *>>   Metropolis, Haario et al.
      *>> 2001). The first half of warmup is isotropic; at its end the
      *>>   covariance
      *>>
      *>> `\hat\Sigma` of the second quarter's draws, shrunk slightly
      *>>   towards
      *>> `10^{-3}I`, becomes the proposal shape `x'=x+\varepsilon Lz`
      *>>   with
      *>> `LL^\top=\hat\Sigma`, and the step size is re-adapted from
      *>> `\varepsilon=2.38/\sqrt d` for the rest of warmup.
       01 DM-RWM-OPTIONS-ADAPT-COVARIANCE.
      *>> Self: the RWM-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-RWM-OPTIONS-ADAPT-COVARIANCE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (bool): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-RWM-OPTIONS-ADAPT-COVARIANCE-VALUE USAGE BINARY-CHAR
              UNSIGNED.

