      *>> datamunge::image::Image::Image() -> IMAGE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_image_new" USING DM-IMAGE-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::image::Image. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A 2D raster image: row-major, top-left origin, interleaved
      *>>   channel bytes (matching
      *>> the layout every common image codec uses on disk, so I/O needs
      *>>   no reshuffling).
      *>> Pixel data is always stored as the mode's exact channel count
      *>>   (1/2/3/4 bytes per
      *>> pixel) -- get_pixel()/set_pixel() are the only place
      *>>   mode-specific expansion happens.
       01 DM-IMAGE-NEW.
      *>> Result: IMAGE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-IMAGE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

