      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   IMAGE-LOADER

      *>> datamunge::datasets::ImageLoader::ImageLoader(const
      *>>   std::string & dataset, const std::string & split = "train",
      *>>   const std::string & directory = "") -> IMAGE-LOADER handle
      *>> CALL "dm_image_loader_new" USING DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::datasets::ImageLoader. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A configurable, disk-backed batch iterator over a standard
      *>>   image dataset.
      *>>
      *>> Datasets: "mnist" and "fashion_mnist" (28x28 grayscale, 10
      *>>   classes; 60000 train / 10000
      *>> test), "cifar10" (32x32 RGB, 10 classes; 50000 / 10000) and
      *>>   "cifar100" (32x32 RGB, 100 fine
      *>> or 20 coarse classes; 50000 / 10000).
      *>>
      *>> Iteration works in epochs. has_next()/next() walk the current
      *>>   epoch's order; reset() starts
      *>> the next epoch (with a fresh shuffle when shuffling is on).
      *>>   Every setter returns the loader
      *>> for chaining and rewinds the current epoch, so configure
      *>>   before iterating.
      *>>
      *>> Reading is const and opens files per call, so batch()/take()
      *>>   may be called from several
      *>> threads at once; next()/reset() and the setters mutate and
      *>>   must not race.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::datasets::ImageLoader test("cifar10", "test");
      *>> test.set_batch_size(500).set_layout("nchw").set_normalize(false);
      *>> const auto first = test.next(); // shape {500, 3, 32, 32},
      *>>   values 0..255
      *>> std::print("{}\n", test.class_names()[first.labels[0]]); //
      *>>   "cat"
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Opens a dataset split, downloading the files first if they are
      *>>   missing.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: for an unknown dataset or split.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: if the files are missing and cannot be
      *>>   downloaded, or are not valid files of that dataset.
       01 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> dataset (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. "mnist", "fashion_mnist", "cifar10"
      *>>   or "cifar100".
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW-DATASET PIC X(256).
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW-DATASET-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> split (const std::string & = "train"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. "train" or "test".
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW-SPLIT PIC X(256).
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW-SPLIT-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> directory (const std::string & = ""): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. Where the dataset's files
      *>>   are (or should be downloaded); empty means `data_home() +
      *>>   "/" + dataset`.
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW-DIRECTORY PIC X(256).
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW-DIRECTORY-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> Result: IMAGE-LOADER handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::datasets::ImageLoader::set_batch_size(int size) ->
      *>>   ImageLoader &
      *>> CALL "dm_image_loader_set_batch_size" USING
      *>>   DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-BATCH-SIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Images per batch (default 32).
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: if `size` is not positive.
       01 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-BATCH-SIZE.
      *>> Self: the IMAGE-LOADER handle.
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-BATCH-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> size (int): int.
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-BATCH-SIZE-SIZE USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED.
      *>> Result (ImageLoader &): IMAGE-LOADER handle (new; refers into
      *>>   its owner, which it keeps alive).
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-BATCH-SIZE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::datasets::ImageLoader::set_shuffle(bool shuffle) ->
      *>>   ImageLoader &
      *>> CALL "dm_image_loader_set_shuffle" USING
      *>>   DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-SHUFFLE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Turns shuffling on or off (default off). Epoch e's order is a
      *>>   permutation drawn
      *>> from (seed(), e), so the same seed always gives the same
      *>>   sequence of epochs.
       01 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-SHUFFLE.
      *>> Self: the IMAGE-LOADER handle.
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-SHUFFLE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> shuffle (bool): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-SHUFFLE-SHUFFLE USAGE BINARY-CHAR
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (ImageLoader &): IMAGE-LOADER handle (new; refers into
      *>>   its owner, which it keeps alive).
          05 DM-IMAGE-LOADER-SET-SHUFFLE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
