      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   MESH1D

      *>> datamunge::fem::Mesh1D::Mesh1D() -> MESH1D handle
      *>> CALL "dm_mesh1d_new" USING DM-MESH1D-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fem::Mesh1D. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A 1D finite-element mesh: a strictly increasing sequence of
      *>>   node coordinates.
      *>> Element i spans [nodes[i], nodes[i+1]] for i in [0,
      *>>   num_elements()) -- no separate
      *>> connectivity array is needed since consecutive nodes are
      *>>   always the two endpoints
      *>> of one linear (P1) element. `nodes` is a public field for
      *>>   direct C++ construction,
      *>> but (matching datamunge::ode::ODESolution's t/y fields -- a
      *>>   swig-jse R-backend
      *>> codegen bug hits plain vector<double> struct *field* getters)
      *>>   is not exposed to
      *>> language bindings; node_at()/num_nodes() are the
      *>>   cross-language-safe accessors.
       01 DM-MESH1D-NEW.
      *>> Result: MESH1D handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-MESH1D-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fem::Mesh1D::num_nodes() const -> std::size_t
      *>> CALL "dm_mesh1d_num_nodes" USING DM-MESH1D-NUM-NODES DM-STATUS
       01 DM-MESH1D-NUM-NODES.
      *>> Self: the MESH1D handle.
          05 DM-MESH1D-NUM-NODES-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::size_t): unsigned long.
          05 DM-MESH1D-NUM-NODES-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fem::Mesh1D::num_elements() const -> std::size_t
      *>> CALL "dm_mesh1d_num_elements" USING DM-MESH1D-NUM-ELEMENTS
      *>>   DM-STATUS
       01 DM-MESH1D-NUM-ELEMENTS.
      *>> Self: the MESH1D handle.
          05 DM-MESH1D-NUM-ELEMENTS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::size_t): unsigned long.
          05 DM-MESH1D-NUM-ELEMENTS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fem::Mesh1D::node_at(std::size_t index) const ->
      *>>   double
      *>> CALL "dm_mesh1d_node_at" USING DM-MESH1D-NODE-AT DM-STATUS
       01 DM-MESH1D-NODE-AT.
      *>> Self: the MESH1D handle.
          05 DM-MESH1D-NODE-AT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> index (std::size_t): unsigned long.
          05 DM-MESH1D-NODE-AT-INDEX USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double.
          05 DM-MESH1D-NODE-AT-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

