      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D

      *>> datamunge::fem::BoundaryCondition1D::BoundaryCondition1D() ->
      *>>   BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D handle
      *>> CALL "dm_boundary_condition1d_new" USING
      *>>   DM-BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fem::BoundaryCondition1D. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Owned endpoint data for Dirichlet, outward-conormal Neumann or
      *>>   Robin conditions.
      *>> Dirichlet uses value as u; Neumann uses it as p*du/dn; Robin
      *>>   uses it as the
      *>> reference value in p*du/dn+alpha*(u-value)=0. Alpha zero gives
      *>>   zero conormal.
      *>> For coercive diffusion/heat models use nonnegative Robin alpha
      *>>   and sufficient
      *>> constraints/reaction to remove the constant nullspace.
      *>>   Unsupported enum values
      *>> and nonfinite data are outside the solver's preconditions, not
      *>>   fully validated.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::fem::BoundaryCondition1D
      *>>   right{dm::fem::BCType::Robin,4,3};
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n",right.value,right.robin_coefficient); //
      *>>   4 3
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: FEM1D, BCType
       01 DM-BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D-NEW.
      *>> Result: BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> BCType datamunge::fem::BoundaryCondition1D::type
      *>> CALL "dm_boundary_condition1d_type_get" USING
