      *>> datamunge::fem::FEM1DResult::FEM1DResult() -> FEM1D-RESULT
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_fem1d_result_new" USING DM-FEM1D-RESULT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fem::FEM1DResult. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Owned nodal P1 steady solution, with checked scalar accessors
      *>>   for language bindings.
      *>> The continuous finite-element field is the piecewise-linear
      *>>   interpolant of
      *>> these values; nodal agreement alone does not imply agreement
      *>>   between nodes.
      *>> Copies own their arrays, with no mesh/callback alias. Public
      *>>   edits can break
      *>> array consistency; accessors check the actual requested vector
      *>>   bounds.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{});
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n",r.size(),r.value_at(1)); // 3 0.125
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: FEM1D::solve(), algorithms::linear_interpolate()
       01 DM-FEM1D-RESULT-NEW.
      *>> Result: FEM1D-RESULT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-FEM1D-RESULT-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

