      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   FEM1D-TIME-SERIES

      *>> datamunge::fem::FEM1DTimeSeries::FEM1DTimeSeries() ->
      *>>   FEM1D-TIME-SERIES handle
      *>> CALL "dm_fem1d_time_series_new" USING DM-FEM1D-TIME-SERIES-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fem::FEM1DTimeSeries. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Owned initial state and actual strictly advancing
      *>>   backward-Euler time slices.
      *>> Solver output has one u row per time and one value per spatial
      *>>   node. Initial
      *>> time zero/u0 are retained as supplied; later rows satisfy
      *>>   imposed boundary data.
      *>> Times retain rounded nominal-step products with a shortened
      *>>   final interval;
      *>> an already reached endpoint is not appended twice. Copies
      *>>   retain no mesh/source
      *>> alias. Public edits may break consistency; accessors check
      *>>   actual vector bounds.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   t=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{},{0,0,0},.5,.5);
      *>> std::print("{} {:.6f}\n",t.num_steps(),t.value_at(1,1)); // 2
      *>>   0.107143
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: FEM1D::solve_transient(),
      *>>   FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin()
       01 DM-FEM1D-TIME-SERIES-NEW.
      *>> Result: FEM1D-TIME-SERIES handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-FEM1D-TIME-SERIES-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

