      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   FEM1D

      *>> datamunge::fem::FEM1D::FEM1D() -> FEM1D handle
      *>> CALL "dm_fem1d_new" USING DM-FEM1D-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fem::FEM1D. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Solve steady or transient one-dimensional divergence-form
      *>>   problems with P1 Galerkin FEM.
      *>> Models -(p*u')'+q*u=f and u_t-(p*u')'+q*u=f on a
      *>>   caller-supplied mesh.
      *>> Requires at least two finite strictly increasing nodes, finite
      *>>   coefficient/
      *>> boundary/source data and finite assembled arithmetic with
      *>>   nonzero Thomas pivots;
      *>> those mathematical/geometry preconditions are not fully
      *>>   validated. Positive p,
      *>> nonnegative q/Robin data and adequate constraints give the
      *>>   usual coercive model.
      *>> Piecewise-constant p/q can be scalar or one per element.
      *>>   Results own their
      *>> values; input mesh/data are unchanged. Calls share no mutable
      *>>   global state,
      *>> while callback side effects/concurrency belong to the caller.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{});
      *>> std::print("{}\n",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - MFEM, Weak Formulations: https://mfem.org/fem_weak_form/ .
      *>>   This native implementation
      *>>   uses P1 intervals, three-point Gauss-Legendre loads and a
      *>>     tridiagonal direct solve.
      *>>
      *>> See also: Mesh1D, FEM1DResult, FEM1DTimeSeries
       01 DM-FEM1D-NEW.
      *>> Result: FEM1D handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-FEM1D-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve(const Mesh1D & mesh, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & p, const std::vector<double> & q,
      *>>   ScalarField1D & f, const BoundaryCondition1D & left, const
      *>>   BoundaryCondition1D & right) -> FEM1DResult
      *>> CALL "dm_fem1d_solve" USING DM-FEM1D-SOLVE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Solve the steady P1 system for -(p*u')'+q*u=f with endpoint
      *>>   boundary data.
      *>> Follows FEM1D's
      *>>   mesh/coefficient/finite-arithmetic/nonsingular-pivot
      *>>   preconditions.
      *>> Uses three-point Gauss-Legendre quadrature of f times each
      *>>   local basis, natural
      *>> boundary terms and symmetric Dirichlet elimination, then
      *>>   Thomas elimination.
      *>> O(N) work/storage for N nodes; invokes the source three times
      *>>   per element.
      *>> No callback pointer is retained. Independent calls share no
      *>>   mutable state.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> struct Unit final:dm::fem::ScalarField1D{double
      *>>   evaluate(double) override{return 1;}} source;
      *>> const auto
      *>>   r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},source,{},{});
      *>> std::print("{}\n",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - https://mfem.org/fem_weak_form/ ; native interval P1 and
      *>>   quadrature choices as FEM1D.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If p/q are empty or have the wrong
      *>>   lengths.
      *>> - std::bad_alloc: If assembly/result storage cannot be
      *>>   allocated; callback exceptions propagate.
      *>>
      *>> See also: solve_builtin(), solve_transient()
       01 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE.
      *>> mesh (const Mesh1D &): MESH1D handle. Borrowed mesh with at
      *>>   least two finite strictly increasing nodes.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-MESH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> p (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed diffusion coefficient: length1 or one per element.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-P USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> q (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed reaction coefficient: length1 or one per element.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-Q USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> f (ScalarField1D &): SCALAR-FIELD1D handle. Borrowed spatial
      *>>   source; evaluate() may have caller-owned side effects.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-F USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> left (const BoundaryCondition1D &): BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D
      *>>   handle. Left endpoint condition, with outward normal -1.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-LEFT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> right (const BoundaryCondition1D &): BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D
      *>>   handle. Right endpoint condition, with outward normal +1.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-RIGHT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (FEM1DResult): FEM1D-RESULT handle (new; close it).
      *>>   Owned original nodes and computed nodal values.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(const Mesh1D &
      *>>   mesh, const std::vector<double> & p, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & q, const std::string & source, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & source_params, const
      *>>   BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D &
      *>>   right) -> FEM1DResult
      *>> CALL "dm_fem1d_solve_builtin" USING DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Solve the steady system using an owned named spatial source,
      *>>   without a director callback.
      *>> Shares the live-source solver and its
      *>>   mathematical/precondition/storage contracts.
      *>> Sources: zero=0 (params unused); constant=c ({1});
      *>>   linear=m*x+c ({1,0});
      *>> polynomial=sum(params[i]*x^i) (empty gives0);
      *>>   sine=A*sin(w*x+phase) ({1,1,0}).
      *>> Missing trailing parameters use those defaults; extra
      *>>   parameters are ignored
      *>> except polynomial, which uses all entries. Name matching is
      *>>   exact/case-sensitive.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{},
      *>>   {},{});
      *>> std::print("{}\n",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - https://mfem.org/fem_weak_form/ ; source definitions are
      *>>   native convenience choices.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For an unknown source or malformed
      *>>   p/q lengths.
      *>> - std::bad_alloc: If owned parameter/assembly/result storage
      *>>   cannot be allocated.
      *>>
      *>> See also: solve(), solve_transient_builtin()
       01 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN.
      *>> mesh (const Mesh1D &): MESH1D handle. Borrowed valid finite
      *>>   interval mesh; unchanged.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-MESH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> p (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed scalar/per-element diffusion coefficient.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-P USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> q (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed scalar/per-element reaction coefficient.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-Q USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> source (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Exact name zero, constant, linear,
      *>>   polynomial or sine.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-SOURCE PIC X(256).
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-SOURCE-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> source_params (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Borrowed positional source parameters, with defaults
      *>>   described above.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-SOURCE-PARAMS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> left (const BoundaryCondition1D &): BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D
      *>>   handle. Left endpoint data using outward normal -1.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-LEFT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> right (const BoundaryCondition1D &): BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D
      *>>   handle. Right endpoint data using outward normal +1.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-RIGHT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (FEM1DResult): FEM1D-RESULT handle (new; close it).
      *>>   Owned computed nodal result, retaining no source or input
      *>>   reference.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient(const Mesh1D &
      *>>   mesh, const std::vector<double> & p, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & q, ScalarField1D & f, const
      *>>   BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D &
      *>>   right, const std::vector<double> & u0, double t_end, double
      *>>   dt) -> FEM1DTimeSeries
      *>> CALL "dm_fem1d_solve_transient" USING DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Integrate u_t-(p*u')'+q*u=f with P1 space and actual
      *>>   backward-Euler time intervals.
      *>> Shares FEM1D's spatial/finite-arithmetic/nonzero-pivot
      *>>   preconditions. Source
      *>> and boundary data represent a time-independent model; the live
      *>>   callback is
      *>> actually reevaluated three times per element at every time
      *>>   advance, not cached.
      *>> Stores initial u0 as supplied, then imposes boundary data at
      *>>   later solves.
      *>> Nominal step dt is shortened at t_end; actual positive time
      *>>   differences enter
      *>> the mass term. Stops once t_end is reached, avoiding a
      *>>   duplicate rounded last
      *>> time even when ceil(t_end/dt) overestimates the number of
      *>>   advances.
      *>> O(S*N) work/output storage for S advances/N nodes, O(N)
      *>>   assembly temporaries;
      *>> no optional trace or quota. Backward Euler is unconditionally
      *>>   stable for the
      *>> coercive semidiscrete model, not a guarantee of arbitrary-step
      *>>   accuracy or
      *>> finite arithmetic for arbitrary parameters. Input arrays
      *>>   remain unchanged;
      *>> callback exceptions/side effects/concurrent safety belong to
      *>>   caller.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> struct Zero final:dm::fem::ScalarField1D{double
      *>>   evaluate(double) override{return 0;}} source;
      *>> const auto
      *>>   t=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},source,{},{},{0,1,0},.5,.5);
      *>> std::print("{} {:.6f}\n",t.num_steps(),t.value_at(1,1)); // 2
      *>>   0.142857
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - Arnold (2012), Numerical Analysis of Partial Differential
      *>>   Equations, chapter5 section2.
      *>>   https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~arnold/8445.f12/notes.pdf .
      *>>     Native load quadrature,
      *>>   fixed data and rounded/shortened time grid are
      *>>     implementation choices.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For fewer than two nodes, wrong
      *>>   coefficient/u0 lengths or nonpositive/nonfinite time
      *>>   controls.
      *>> - std::length_error: If frame counts, vector capacities or
      *>>   total scalar count cannot be represented.
      *>> - std::overflow_error: If rounded time products cannot advance
      *>>   before t_end.
      *>> - std::bad_alloc: If output/assembly storage cannot be
      *>>   allocated; callback exceptions propagate.
      *>>
      *>> See also: solve_transient_builtin(), FEM1DTimeSeries
       01 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT.
      *>> mesh (const Mesh1D &): MESH1D handle. Borrowed valid mesh with
      *>>   at least two finite increasing nodes.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-MESH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> p (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed scalar/per-element diffusion coefficient.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-P USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> q (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed scalar/per-element reaction coefficient.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-Q USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> f (ScalarField1D &): SCALAR-FIELD1D handle. Borrowed spatial
      *>>   callback, reevaluated at every advance.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-F USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> left (const BoundaryCondition1D &): BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D
      *>>   handle. Fixed left condition, with outward normal -1.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-LEFT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> right (const BoundaryCondition1D &): BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D
      *>>   handle. Fixed right condition, with outward normal +1.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-RIGHT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> u0 (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed finite initial nodal values, exactly one per mesh
      *>>   node.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-U0 USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> t_end (double): double. Positive finite final time, in time
      *>>   units.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-T-END USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> dt (double): double. Positive finite nominal time step in the
      *>>   same units; may exceed t_end.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-DT USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result (FEM1DTimeSeries): FEM1D-TIME-SERIES handle (new; close
      *>>   it). Owned nodes, initial state and strictly advancing
      *>>   slices ending at t_end.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(const
      *>>   Mesh1D & mesh, const std::vector<double> & p, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & q, const std::string & source, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & source_params, const
      *>>   BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D &
      *>>   right, const std::vector<double> & u0, double t_end, double
      *>>   dt) -> FEM1DTimeSeries
      *>> CALL "dm_fem1d_solve_transient_builtin" USING
      *>>   DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Integrate the same backward-Euler model with a named source
      *>>   and no callback subclass.
      *>> Uses the same private source construction as solve_builtin()
      *>>   and the same
      *>> actual time loop as solve_transient(); no second solver or
      *>>   per-language glue.
      *>> Names/defaults: zero=0; constant=c ({1}); linear=m*x+c
      *>>   ({1,0});
      *>> polynomial=sum(params[i]*x^i) (empty0); sine=A*sin(w*x+phase)
      *>>   ({1,1,0}).
      *>> Extra entries ignored except polynomial; exact case-sensitive
      *>>   names. Source
      *>> objects are local and synchronous; results own values, not
      *>>   callback aliases.
      *>> All spatial/time/initial-state, complexity and stability
      *>>   contracts follow
      *>> solve_transient(); ordinary output has no optional
      *>>   history/quota.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   t=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{},{0,0,0},.5,.5);
      *>> std::print("{} {:.6f}\n",t.num_steps(),t.value_at(1,1)); // 2
      *>>   0.107143
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~arnold/8445.f12/notes.pdf ;
      *>>   same native discretization as solve_transient().
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For an unknown source, malformed
      *>>   coefficient/u0 lengths, fewer than two nodes or
      *>>   nonpositive/nonfinite time controls.
      *>> - std::length_error: If frame/container/total scalar counts
      *>>   cannot be represented.
      *>> - std::overflow_error: If rounded time products cannot
      *>>   advance.
      *>> - std::bad_alloc: If parameters, output or assembly storage
      *>>   cannot be allocated.
      *>>
      *>> See also: solve_builtin(), solve_transient()
       01 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN.
      *>> mesh (const Mesh1D &): MESH1D handle. Borrowed valid finite
      *>>   increasing mesh, with at least two nodes.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-MESH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> p (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed scalar/per-element diffusion coefficient.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-P USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> q (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed scalar/per-element reaction coefficient.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-Q USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> source (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Exact name zero, constant, linear,
      *>>   polynomial or sine.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-SOURCE PIC X(256).
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-SOURCE-LENGTH USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> source_params (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Borrowed positional parameters; omitted trailing
      *>>   values use the defaults above.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-SOURCE-PARAMS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> left (const BoundaryCondition1D &): BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D
      *>>   handle. Fixed left boundary condition using outward normal
      *>>   -1.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-LEFT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> right (const BoundaryCondition1D &): BOUNDARY-CONDITION1D
      *>>   handle. Fixed right boundary condition using outward normal
      *>>   +1.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-RIGHT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> u0 (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Borrowed finite initial values, exactly one per spatial
      *>>   node.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-U0 USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> t_end (double): double. Positive finite final time.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-T-END USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> dt (double): double. Positive finite nominal time step; final
      *>>   interval is shortened as needed.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-DT USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result (FEM1DTimeSeries): FEM1D-TIME-SERIES handle (new; close
      *>>   it). Owned initial state and actual strictly advancing
      *>>   backward-Euler slices.
          05 DM-FEM1D-SOLVE-TRANSIENT-BUILTIN-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   POINT2D

      *>> datamunge::geometry::Point2D::Point2D() -> POINT2D handle
      *>> CALL "dm_point2d_new" USING DM-POINT2D-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::Point2D. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A copied point or free vector with ordinary double
      *>>   coordinates.
      *>> Construction does not validate finiteness; checked algorithms
      *>>   document their
      *>> own input contracts. Default coordinates are zero. Equality is
      *>>   numeric, so
      *>> signed zeros compare equal and NaN coordinates do not compare
      *>>   equal.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::geometry::Point2D p{3,4};
      *>> std::cout << p.x << ' ' << p.y; // 3 4
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: squared_distance(), distance(), cross(),
      *>>   orientation_sign()
       01 DM-POINT2D-NEW.
      *>> Result: POINT2D handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-POINT2D-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::geometry::Point2D::operator==(const Point2D &
      *>>   other) const -> bool
      *>> CALL "dm_point2d_equal" USING DM-POINT2D-EQUAL DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Compare both coordinates with ordinary double equality.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> std::cout <<
      *>>   (dm::geometry::Point2D{0,1}==dm::geometry::Point2D{-0.,1});
      *>>   // 1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: operator!=()
       01 DM-POINT2D-EQUAL.
      *>> Self: the POINT2D handle.
          05 DM-POINT2D-EQUAL-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> other (const Point2D &): POINT2D handle. Point to compare
      *>>   without mutation.
          05 DM-POINT2D-EQUAL-OTHER USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (bool): 0 or 1. Both coordinate comparisons are true;
      *>>   signed zeros compare equal.
          05 DM-POINT2D-EQUAL-RESULT USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::geometry::Point2D::operator!=(const Point2D &
      *>>   other) const -> bool
      *>> CALL "dm_point2d_not_equal" USING DM-POINT2D-NOT-EQUAL
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Negate coordinate equality, including unequal NaN coordinates.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> std::cout <<
      *>>   (dm::geometry::Point2D{0,1}!=dm::geometry::Point2D{0,2}); //
      *>>   1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: operator==()
       01 DM-POINT2D-NOT-EQUAL.
      *>> Self: the POINT2D handle.
          05 DM-POINT2D-NOT-EQUAL-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> other (const Point2D &): POINT2D handle. Point to compare
      *>>   without mutation.
          05 DM-POINT2D-NOT-EQUAL-OTHER USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (bool): 0 or 1. Logical negation of operator==().
          05 DM-POINT2D-NOT-EQUAL-RESULT USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.

