      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   DELAUNAY-INSERTION

      *>> datamunge::geometry::DelaunayInsertion::DelaunayInsertion() ->
      *>>   DELAUNAY-INSERTION handle
      *>> CALL "dm_delaunay_insertion_new" USING
      *>>   DM-DELAUNAY-INSERTION-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::DelaunayInsertion. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Owned actual cavity removal, directed boundary and replacement
      *>>   for one site.
      *>> removed/added may contain ghosts, identified by c=the original
      *>>   input count.
      *>> boundary is ordered by canonical undirected endpoint key but
      *>>   retains the first
      *>> directed occurrence; shared interior edges are cancelled.
      *>>   Actual face scans
      *>> precede this event. No full before/after mesh snapshot or
      *>>   geometric replay is
      *>> retained. All vectors own their entries and have no input
      *>>   lifetime dependency.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   t=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace({{0,0},{4,0},{4,4},{0,4},{2,2}});
      *>> std::print("{} {}
      *>>   {}\n",t.steps.back().input_index,t.steps.back().removed.size(),t.steps.back().added.size());
      *>>   // 4 2 4
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: DelaunayTrace
       01 DM-DELAUNAY-INSERTION-NEW.
      *>> Result: DELAUNAY-INSERTION handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-DELAUNAY-INSERTION-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

