      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   DELAUNAY-TRACE

      *>> datamunge::geometry::DelaunayTrace::DelaunayTrace() ->
      *>>   DELAUNAY-TRACE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_delaunay_trace_new" USING DM-DELAUNAY-TRACE-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::DelaunayTrace. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Complete owned sites, earliest-identity mapping, finite mesh
      *>>   and actual events.
      *>> Numeric coordinate equality coalesces duplicates and signed
      *>>   zeros. Representatives
      *>> retain earliest input indices in input order. Seed is the
      *>>   first two distinct
      *>> sites and first later noncollinear site; remaining distinct
      *>>   sites are inserted
      *>> in input order. Strict positive incircle conflicts retain an
      *>>   existing diagonal
      *>> on an exact cocircular tie; permutations may therefore select
      *>>   another valid mesh.
      *>> Final finite triangles rotate their smallest id first and are
      *>>   lexicographically
      *>> sorted, independent of map/hash traversal. All-collinear/fewer
      *>>   than three
      *>> distinct sites have no seed, faces or insertion events. All
      *>>   fields own data;
      *>> public edits are unchecked and independent calls share no
      *>>   mutable state.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   t=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace({{0,0},{1,0},{0,1},{0,0}});
      *>> std::print("{} {}
      *>>   {}\n",t.representatives.size(),t.representative_for_input.back(),t.triangles.size());
      *>>   // 3 0 1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: delaunay_trace(), delaunay_triangulation()
       01 DM-DELAUNAY-TRACE-NEW.
      *>> Result: DELAUNAY-TRACE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-DELAUNAY-TRACE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

