      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   DELAUNAY-ANALYSIS

      *>> datamunge::geometry::DelaunayAnalysis::DelaunayAnalysis() ->
      *>>   DELAUNAY-ANALYSIS handle
      *>> CALL "dm_delaunay_analysis_new" USING DM-DELAUNAY-ANALYSIS-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::DelaunayAnalysis. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Coordinate-deduplicated topology counts and exact local
      *>>   empty-circle checks.
      *>> Counts are independent of triangle order. Duplicate-coordinate
      *>>   ids are mapped
      *>> to earliest originals. Triangle indices must be valid,
      *>>   distinct in coordinate,
      *>> exactly CCW, with no duplicate face and at most two incident
      *>>   faces per edge.
      *>> These checks do not certify global nonoverlap, hull coverage
      *>>   or planar embedding
      *>> of an arbitrary supplied mesh. minimum_angle_degrees is a
      *>>   scaled floating
      *>> diagnostic, NaN for no faces and potentially zero after
      *>>   extreme scale loss;
      *>> it never controls topology. Empty-circle signs are exact for
      *>>   stored binary64.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D>
      *>>   p{{0,0},{4,0},{4,4},{0,4},{2,2}};
      *>> const auto
      *>>   a=dm::geometry::delaunay_analyze(p,dm::geometry::delaunay_triangulation(p));
      *>> std::print("{} {} {}
      *>>   {}\n",a.distinct_points,a.triangles,a.boundary_edges,a.interior_violations);
      *>>   // 5 4 4 0
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: delaunay_analyze()
       01 DM-DELAUNAY-ANALYSIS-NEW.
