      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   FEM2D

      *>> datamunge::fem::FEM2D::FEM2D() -> FEM2D handle
      *>> CALL "dm_fem2d_new" USING DM-FEM2D-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fem::FEM2D. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Galerkin finite-element solver for the 2D Poisson equation
      *>> -k * (u_xx + u_yy) = f(x, y) on a triangular mesh, using
      *>>   piecewise-linear (P1)
      *>> Lagrange elements and Dirichlet boundary conditions only (this
      *>>   "basic" 2D solver
      *>> does not offer FEM1D's Neumann/Robin options). Internally
      *>>   assembles a sparse
      *>> stiffness system and solves it with the conjugate-gradient
      *>>   solver
      *>> (datamunge::linalg::cg) -- the assembled matrices themselves
      *>>   are never exposed,
      *>> matching this codebase's rule that linalg's sparse/dense
      *>>   matrix types are never
      *>> SWIG-bound.
       01 DM-FEM2D-NEW.
      *>> Result: FEM2D handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-FEM2D-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::fem::FEM2D::solve(const Mesh2D & mesh,
      *>>   double k, ScalarField2D & f, const std::vector<int> &
      *>>   dirichlet_nodes, const std::vector<double> &
      *>>   dirichlet_values) -> FEM2DResult
      *>> CALL "dm_fem2d_solve" USING DM-FEM2D-SOLVE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Solves -k * Laplacian(u) = f with Dirichlet data u =
      *>>   dirichlet_values[i] at node
      *>> dirichlet_nodes[i] (every other node is a free unknown); k is
      *>>   the constant,
      *>> isotropic diffusion coefficient. Throws std::invalid_argument
      *>>   if
      *>> dirichlet_nodes.size() != dirichlet_values.size(), if any
      *>>   index in
      *>> dirichlet_nodes is out of range, or if every node is
      *>>   constrained (nothing to
      *>> solve for).
       01 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE.
      *>> mesh (const Mesh2D &): MESH2D handle.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-MESH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> k (double): double.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-K USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> f (ScalarField2D &): SCALAR-FIELD2D handle.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-F USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> dirichlet_nodes (const std::vector<int> &): VECTOR-INT handle.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-DIRICHLET-NODES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> dirichlet_values (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-DIRICHLET-VALUES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (FEM2DResult): FEM2D-RESULT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::fem::FEM2D::solve_builtin(const Mesh2D &
      *>>   mesh, double k, const std::string & source, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & source_params, const std::vector<int>
      *>>   & dirichlet_nodes, const std::vector<double> &
      *>>   dirichlet_values) -> FEM2DResult
      *>> CALL "dm_fem2d_solve_builtin" USING DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Same as solve(), but f is one of a fixed set of named source
      *>>   terms instead of a
      *>> live user-supplied callback. source_params is interpreted
      *>>   positionally, with the
      *>> listed defaults used for any parameter past the end of
      *>>   source_params:
      *>> - "zero": f(x, y) = 0. source_params unused.
      *>> - "constant": f(x, y) = c. {c=1}.
      *>> - "sine": f(x, y) = amplitude*sin(fx*x)*sin(fy*y).
      *>>   {amplitude=1, fx=1, fy=1}.
      *>>   Throws std::invalid_argument for an unknown source name.
       01 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN.
      *>> mesh (const Mesh2D &): MESH2D handle.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-MESH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> k (double): double.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-K USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> source (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-SOURCE PIC X(256).
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-SOURCE-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> source_params (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-SOURCE-PARAMS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> dirichlet_nodes (const std::vector<int> &): VECTOR-INT handle.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-DIRICHLET-NODES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> dirichlet_values (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-DIRICHLET-VALUES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (FEM2DResult): FEM2D-RESULT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-FEM2D-SOLVE-BUILTIN-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

