      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   ALPHA-BETA-FILTER

      *>> datamunge::filter::AlphaBetaFilter::AlphaBetaFilter(double
      *>>   alpha, double beta, double dt, double x0 = 0.0, double v0 =
      *>>   0.0) -> ALPHA-BETA-FILTER handle
      *>> CALL "dm_alpha_beta_filter_new" USING DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::filter::AlphaBetaFilter. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> The constant-gain alpha-beta ("g-h") filter: a
      *>>   constant-velocity tracker that uses
      *>> the SAME predict/correct structure as KalmanFilter, but with
      *>>   fixed gains alpha
      *>> (position correction) and beta (velocity correction) instead
      *>>   of a covariance-driven
      *>> Kalman gain -- it is exactly the steady-state behavior a 1D
      *>>   constant-velocity
      *>> KalmanFilter converges to once its covariance stops changing,
      *>>   with the covariance
      *>> bookkeeping stripped out entirely. Far cheaper per step (no
      *>>   matrices at all) at the
      *>> cost of not adapting its gain to changing noise conditions the
      *>>   way a real Kalman
      *>> filter does.
       01 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 3 to 5 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 3.
          05 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 3.
      *>> alpha (double): double.
          05 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-NEW-ALPHA USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> beta (double): double.
          05 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-NEW-BETA USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> dt (double): double.
          05 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-NEW-DT USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> x0 (double = 0.0): double.
          05 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-NEW-X0 USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> v0 (double = 0.0): double.
          05 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-NEW-V0 USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result: ALPHA-BETA-FILTER handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::filter::AlphaBetaFilter::update(double z) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_alpha_beta_filter_update" USING
      *>>   DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-UPDATE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Predicts one step ahead, then corrects toward measurement `z`:
      *>>   x_pred = x +
      *>> v*dt; residual = z - x_pred; x = x_pred + alpha*residual; v +=
      *>>   (beta/dt)*residual.
       01 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-UPDATE.
      *>> Self: the ALPHA-BETA-FILTER handle.
          05 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-UPDATE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> z (double): double.
          05 DM-ALPHA-BETA-FILTER-UPDATE-Z USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::filter::AlphaBetaFilter::position() const -> double
