      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   INFORMATION-FILTER

      *>> datamunge::filter::InformationFilter::InformationFilter(std::vector<std::vector<double>>
      *>>   F, std::vector<std::vector<double>> H,
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> Q,
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> R, std::vector<double> x0,
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> P0) -> INFORMATION-FILTER
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_information_filter_new" USING
      *>>   DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::filter::InformationFilter. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> The Information Filter: the algebraic dual of KalmanFilter,
      *>>   tracking the information
      *>> matrix Y = P^-1 and information vector y = Y x instead of (x,
      *>>   P) directly. Its
      *>> measurement update is purely ADDITIVE (Y += H^T R^-1 H, y +=
      *>>   H^T R^-1 z) -- the
      *>> classical advantage of this form is that fusing several
      *>>   independent sensors, or
      *>> distributing a filter across nodes that each see part of the
      *>>   measurement stream, is
      *>> just summing information contributions, with no matrix
      *>>   inversion per sensor. The
      *>> time-update (predict) step has no equally simple additive form
      *>>   for general F, so
      *>> this implementation converts to covariance form, applies the
      *>>   ordinary
      *>> KalmanFilter-style predict, and converts back --
      *>>   mathematically exact, and produces
      *>> IDENTICAL results to KalmanFilter given the same model (the
      *>>   two are the same
      *>> estimator in a different parameterization, not an
      *>>   approximation of each other).
       01 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-NEW.
      *>> F (std::vector<std::vector<double>>): VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-NEW-F USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> H (std::vector<std::vector<double>>): VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-NEW-H USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Q (std::vector<std::vector<double>>): VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-NEW-Q USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> R (std::vector<std::vector<double>>): VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-NEW-R USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> x0 (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-NEW-X0 USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> P0 (std::vector<std::vector<double>>): VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-NEW-P0 USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: INFORMATION-FILTER handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::filter::InformationFilter::predict() -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_information_filter_predict" USING
      *>>   DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-PREDICT DM-STATUS
       01 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-PREDICT.
      *>> Self: the INFORMATION-FILTER handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-PREDICT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::filter::InformationFilter::update(const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & z) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_information_filter_update" USING
      *>>   DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-UPDATE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The additive information-form update: Y += H^T R^-1 H, y +=
      *>>   H^T R^-1 z.
       01 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-UPDATE.
      *>> Self: the INFORMATION-FILTER handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-UPDATE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> z (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-UPDATE-Z USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::filter::InformationFilter::state() const ->
      *>>   std::vector<double>
      *>> CALL "dm_information_filter_state" USING
      *>>   DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-STATE DM-STATUS
       01 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-STATE.
      *>> Self: the INFORMATION-FILTER handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-STATE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; close
      *>>   it).
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-STATE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::filter::InformationFilter::covariance() const ->
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>>
      *>> CALL "dm_information_filter_covariance" USING
      *>>   DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-COVARIANCE DM-STATUS
       01 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-COVARIANCE.
      *>> Self: the INFORMATION-FILTER handle.
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-COVARIANCE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<std::vector<double>>):
      *>>   VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-INFORMATION-FILTER-COVARIANCE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::filter::InformationFilter::filter(const
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> & measurements) ->
      *>>   std::vector<KalmanState>
