      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   CONVEX-HULL-WORK

      *>> datamunge::geometry::ConvexHullWork::ConvexHullWork() ->
      *>>   CONVEX-HULL-WORK handle
      *>> CALL "dm_convex_hull_work_new" USING DM-CONVEX-HULL-WORK-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::ConvexHullWork. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Actual sorting, deduplication and two-scan work, with checked
      *>>   counters.
      *>> Comparison counts depend on the standard-library sort and
      *>>   original order.
      *>> For at least two distinct points each pass pushes each point
      *>>   once. Tests
      *>> count exact orientation requests; every nonpositive test
      *>>   causes one pop.
      *>> max_stack is the greatest length of either separate chain, not
      *>>   their sum.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   a=dm::geometry::convex_hull_analyze({{0,0},{1,0},{0,1}});
      *>> std::cout << a.work.distinct_points << ' ' << a.work.pushes;
      *>>   // 3 6
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: ConvexHullAnalysis
       01 DM-CONVEX-HULL-WORK-NEW.
      *>> Result: CONVEX-HULL-WORK handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-CONVEX-HULL-WORK-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

