      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   HULL-EVENT

      *>> datamunge::geometry::HullEvent::HullEvent() -> HULL-EVENT
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_hull_event_new" USING DM-HULL-EVENT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::HullEvent. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Actual scan event, referring to indices in the trace's sorted
      *>>   unique points.
      *>> candidate is the pending point; point is the pushed/popped
      *>>   point, or candidate
      *>> for a test. a,b,turn are meaningful only for test events and
      *>>   otherwise zero.
      *>> stack_size is the actual size after the event (unchanged for
      *>>   tests). Together
      *>> these compact edits describe every stack state without
      *>>   quadratic snapshots.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto t=dm::geometry::convex_hull_trace({{0,0},{1,0}});
      *>> std::cout << t.events[0].stack_size; // 1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: ConvexHullTrace, HullPass, HullAction
       01 DM-HULL-EVENT-NEW.
      *>> Result: HULL-EVENT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-HULL-EVENT-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

