      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   CONVEX-HULL-ANALYSIS

      *>> datamunge::geometry::ConvexHullAnalysis::ConvexHullAnalysis()
      *>>   -> CONVEX-HULL-ANALYSIS handle
      *>> CALL "dm_convex_hull_analysis_new" USING
      *>>   DM-CONVEX-HULL-ANALYSIS-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::ConvexHullAnalysis. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Owned strict hull, earliest original identities and actual
      *>>   work without history.
      *>> Vertices start at the lexicographic minimum and run
      *>>   counterclockwise, without
      *>> repeating the first. Collinear edge points are omitted. Empty
      *>>   gives no points;
      *>> one distinct point gives one; a collinear set gives its sorted
      *>>   two endpoints.
      *>> Identity vector aligns one-for-one with hull vertices.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   a=dm::geometry::convex_hull_analyze({{1,0},{0,0},{0,1}});
      *>> std::cout << a.hull.size() << ' ' << a.input_indices[0]; // 3
      *>>   1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: convex_hull_analyze()
       01 DM-CONVEX-HULL-ANALYSIS-NEW.
      *>> Result: CONVEX-HULL-ANALYSIS handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-CONVEX-HULL-ANALYSIS-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

