      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   CONVEX-HULL-TRACE

      *>> datamunge::geometry::ConvexHullTrace::ConvexHullTrace() ->
      *>>   CONVEX-HULL-TRACE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_convex_hull_trace_new" USING DM-CONVEX-HULL-TRACE-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::ConvexHullTrace. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Owned actual sorted identities, compact stack edits and
      *>>   completed scan chains.
      *>> lower/upper contain indices into sorted and include their
      *>>   endpoints. Inputs
      *>> with fewer than two distinct points take no scans and have
      *>>   empty chains/events.
      *>> Trace capture performs no extra sorting or orientation replay.
      *>>   All storage is
      *>> independent of the caller, result and other snapshots; O(n)
      *>>   extra space.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto t=dm::geometry::convex_hull_trace({{0,0},{1,0}});
      *>> std::cout << t.lower.size() << ' ' << t.upper.size(); // 2 2
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: convex_hull_trace()
       01 DM-CONVEX-HULL-TRACE-NEW.
      *>> Result: CONVEX-HULL-TRACE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-CONVEX-HULL-TRACE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

