      *>>   dm::Vector<dm::RGB>
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: dm::RGBA, dm::Plot::set_col(), dm::points()
      *>>
      *>> Implicitly parse a color name, #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA string.
      *>> Names and hexadecimal digits are case-insensitive. Hex alpha
      *>>   is the final
      *>> byte divided by 255; omitted alpha is 1. Whitespace is not
      *>>   stripped. Named
      *>> green is (0, 128, 0); transparent is black with alpha zero.
      *>>   The input is copied
      *>> while parsing and is never borrowed by a plot or palette.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::RGBA glass = std::string("#ff44ff55");
      *>> const auto plt = dm::plot(dm::c(0, 1), dm::c(1, 2), "data",
      *>>   "#ff44ff55");
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n", glass.r, dm::round(glass.alpha, 3)); //
      *>>   255 0.333
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For empty text, unknown names or
      *>>   malformed hex.
       01 DM-RGB-NEW-STRING.
      *>> color (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Color text; supported names are
      *>>   listed in the class description.
          05 DM-RGB-NEW-STRING-COLOR PIC X(256).
          05 DM-RGB-NEW-STRING-COLOR-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> Result: RGB handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-RGB-NEW-STRING-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

