      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   DATA-SERIES

      *>> datamunge::graphics::DataSeries::DataSeries() -> DATA-SERIES
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_data_series_new" USING DM-DATA-SERIES-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::graphics::DataSeries. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> One drawn layer of a plot (points, a line, bars, a box, a
      *>>   polygon, a label, or
      *>> segments), as stored by RPlot's layer verbs and read back
      *>>   through Plot::series().
      *>>
      *>> A plain aggregate holding data coordinates and styling. Which
      *>>   fields matter depends on
      *>> kind; each Kind value documents how it reads x, y, and the
      *>>   other fields. Layers are drawn
      *>> in insertion order, after the reference lines, and every
      *>>   layer's coordinates widen the
      *>> automatic axis ranges (bars also pull the y range down or up
      *>>   to 0). A nonempty label puts
      *>> the layer in the automatic legend unless it is a Text layer.
      *>>   User code normally creates
      *>> layers through RPlot verbs (points(), lines(), bars(), ...)
      *>>   and only reads this struct.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot().points(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(3.0, 4.0),
      *>>   "pts");
      *>> const dm::graphics::DataSeries& s = plt.series()[0];
      *>> std::print("{} {} {} {}\n", s.kind ==
      *>>   dm::graphics::DataSeries::Kind::Scatter, s.x.size(),
      *>>            s.label, s.marker_size); // true 2 pts 4
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: Plot::series(), RPlot::points(), RPlot::lines()
       01 DM-DATA-SERIES-NEW.
      *>> Result: DATA-SERIES handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-DATA-SERIES-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

