      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   AB-LINE

      *>> datamunge::graphics::ABLine::ABLine() -> AB-LINE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_ab_line_new" USING DM-AB-LINE-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::graphics::ABLine. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A straight reference line across the whole plotting area, as
      *>>   drawn by R's
      *>> `abline(a, b)`, `abline(h =)` and `abline(v =)`.
      *>>
      *>> A sloped or horizontal line is y = value + slope * x evaluated
      *>>   at both ends of the visible
      *>> x range; a vertical line sits at x = value and ignores slope.
      *>>   Reference lines are drawn
      *>> beneath every DataSeries. Vertical lines widen the automatic x
      *>>   range to include them;
      *>> sloped and horizontal lines never change the axis ranges.
      *>>   Created by RPlot::abline(),
      *>> abline_h(), abline_v(), and qqline(); read back through
      *>>   Plot::reference_lines().
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot(dm::c(0.0, 1.0), dm::c(0.0,
      *>>   2.0)).abline(0.5, 2.0).abline_v(0.25);
      *>> const auto& lines = plt.reference_lines();
      *>> std::print("{} {} {}\n", lines[0].slope, lines[1].vertical,
      *>>   lines[1].value); // 2 true 0.25
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `abline()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/abline.html
      *>>
      *>> See also: RPlot::abline(), Plot::reference_lines()
       01 DM-AB-LINE-NEW.
      *>> Result: AB-LINE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-AB-LINE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

