      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   LEGEND-ENTRY

      *>> datamunge::graphics::LegendEntry::LegendEntry() ->
      *>>   LEGEND-ENTRY handle
      *>> CALL "dm_legend_entry_new" USING DM-LEGEND-ENTRY-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::graphics::LegendEntry. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> One manually specified legend row, as drawn by R's `legend()`.
      *>>
      *>> When a plot has any manual entries, they replace the default
      *>>   auto-generated
      *>> (one-row-per-labeled-series) legend. Each row is a color
      *>>   swatch followed by the label,
      *>> stacked from the top-right corner of the plotting area in
      *>>   insertion order.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(1.0,
      *>>   2.0)).legend({"data"}, {dm::RGB{0, 0, 255}});
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n", plt.legend_entries()[0].label,
      *>>   plt.legend_entries()[0].color.b); // data 255
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `legend()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/legend.html
      *>>
      *>> See also: RPlot::legend(), dm::legend(),
      *>>   Plot::legend_entries()
       01 DM-LEGEND-ENTRY-NEW.
      *>> Result: LEGEND-ENTRY handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-LEGEND-ENTRY-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

