      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   PLOT

      *>> datamunge::graphics::Plot::Plot() -> PLOT handle
      *>> CALL "dm_plot_new" USING DM-PLOT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::graphics::Plot. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Renderer-facing state shared by every 2-D plot: canvas,
      *>>   labels, axes, and series.
      *>>
      *>> User code works with the derived RPlot (spelled `dm::Plot`),
      *>>   whose setters return `RPlot&`;
      *>> this base holds the data, the read-only accessors, and the
      *>>   output functions to_svg(),
      *>> save(), and show(). The base-class setters below return
      *>>   `Plot&` and are what RPlot's
      *>> same-named setters forward to; call the RPlot forms in user
      *>>   code so chains keep the RPlot
      *>> type. A `const Plot&` is also what RLayout::add() accepts and
      *>>   RLayout::panel() returns.
      *>>
      *>> Every output function renders from the stored state, so it
      *>>   throws std::runtime_error for a
      *>> plot with no data series (reference lines and legend rows
      *>>   alone are not enough) or a canvas
      *>> too small for its margins. Plots are copyable values with no
      *>>   shared state; distinct plots may
      *>> be used from different threads, but one plot must not be
      *>>   mutated while it is rendered.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::graphics::Plot& base = dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0),
      *>>   dm::c(1.0, 4.0)).set_title("Base");
      *>> std::print("{} {}x{}\n", base.title_text(), base.width(),
      *>>   base.height()); // Base 960x640
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: RPlot, RLayout
       01 DM-PLOT-NEW.
      *>> Result: PLOT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-PLOT-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::Plot::size(std::size_t width, std::size_t
      *>>   height) -> Plot &
      *>> CALL "dm_plot_size" USING DM-PLOT-SIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Base-class form of RPlot::size(): sets the canvas size in
      *>>   pixels (default 960x640).
      *>>
      *>> See also: RPlot::size()
       01 DM-PLOT-SIZE.
      *>> Self: the PLOT handle.
          05 DM-PLOT-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> width (std::size_t): unsigned long. Canvas width in pixels.
          05 DM-PLOT-SIZE-WIDTH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> height (std::size_t): unsigned long. Canvas height in pixels.
          05 DM-PLOT-SIZE-HEIGHT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (Plot &): PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-PLOT-SIZE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::Plot::title(std::string value) -> Plot &
