      *>> datamunge::graphics::Plot::to_svg() const -> std::string
      *>> CALL "dm_plot_to_svg" USING DM-PLOT-TO-SVG DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Renders the plot as a standalone SVG document and returns it
      *>>   as a string.
      *>>
      *>> The document starts with an XML declaration and draws text as
      *>>   embedded Computer Modern
      *>> glyph outlines, so it displays identically in any SVG viewer,
      *>>   with or without web fonts. The plot is not modified, and no
      *>>   file or display is used.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto svg = dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(2.0,
      *>>   1.0)).set_title("Tiny").to_svg();
      *>> std::print("{}\n", svg.starts_with("<?xml")); // true
      *>> std::print("{}\n", svg.contains("Tiny")); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the plot has no data series, or the
      *>>   canvas is smaller than its margins.
      *>>
      *>> See also: save(), show()
       01 DM-PLOT-TO-SVG.
      *>> Self: the PLOT handle.
          05 DM-PLOT-TO-SVG-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::string): text in PIC X(16384); -LENGTH is its
      *>>   length in bytes. The complete SVG text.
          05 DM-PLOT-TO-SVG-RESULT PIC X(16384).
          05 DM-PLOT-TO-SVG-RESULT-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              0.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::Plot::save(const std::string & path)
      *>>   const -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_plot_save" USING DM-PLOT-SAVE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Writes the plot to `path`, choosing the format from the file
      *>>   extension
      *>> (R's `svg()`/`png()`/`pdf()` devices followed by `dev.off()`,
      *>>   in one call).
      *>>
      *>> `.svg` or no extension writes the same text as to_svg();
      *>>   `.png` writes the raster image
      *>> the X11 viewer displays; `.pdf` wraps that raster in a
      *>>   single-page PDF. The extension is
      *>> case-sensitive. An existing file is overwritten. Needs no
      *>>   display.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0, 3.0), dm::c(1.0, 4.0,
      *>>   9.0)).set_title("Squares");
      *>> plt.save("squares.svg"); // vector
      *>> plt.save("squares.png"); // raster
      *>> plt.save("squares.pdf"); // raster in a one-page PDF
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For any other extension (e.g.
      *>>   `.jpg`).
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the file cannot be opened for
      *>>   writing, the plot has no data series, or the canvas is
      *>>   smaller than its margins.
      *>>
      *>> See also: save_svg(), to_svg(), show()
       01 DM-PLOT-SAVE.
      *>> Self: the PLOT handle.
          05 DM-PLOT-SAVE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> path (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Destination file; relative paths
      *>>   resolve against the working directory.
          05 DM-PLOT-SAVE-PATH PIC X(256).
          05 DM-PLOT-SAVE-PATH-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::Plot::save_svg(const std::string & path)
      *>>   const -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_plot_save_svg" USING DM-PLOT-SAVE-SVG DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Writes to_svg() to `path` regardless of its extension.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(1.0,
      *>>   2.0)).save_svg("diagonal.txt"); // SVG text
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the file cannot be opened for
      *>>   writing, or rendering fails as described for to_svg().
      *>>
      *>> See also: save()
       01 DM-PLOT-SAVE-SVG.
      *>> Self: the PLOT handle.
          05 DM-PLOT-SAVE-SVG-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> path (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Destination file; an existing file is
      *>>   overwritten.
          05 DM-PLOT-SAVE-SVG-PATH PIC X(256).
          05 DM-PLOT-SAVE-SVG-PATH-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::Plot::to_png() const ->
      *>>   std::vector<std::uint8_t>
      *>> CALL "dm_plot_to_png" USING DM-PLOT-TO-PNG DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Renders the plot as PNG image bytes (the same raster save()
      *>>   writes for `.png`).
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto png = dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(2.0,
      *>>   1.0)).to_png();
      *>> std::print("{}\n", png[1] == 'P'); // true: PNG signature
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If rendering fails as described for
      *>>   to_svg().
      *>>
      *>> See also: save_png(), to_pdf(), to_svg()
       01 DM-PLOT-TO-PNG.
      *>> Self: the PLOT handle.
          05 DM-PLOT-TO-PNG-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<std::uint8_t>): VECTOR-UCHAR handle (new;
      *>>   close it). The complete PNG file contents.
          05 DM-PLOT-TO-PNG-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::Plot::to_pdf() const ->
      *>>   std::vector<std::uint8_t>
      *>> CALL "dm_plot_to_pdf" USING DM-PLOT-TO-PDF DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Renders the plot as a one-page PDF holding the raster image.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If rendering fails as described for
      *>>   to_svg().
      *>>
      *>> See also: save_pdf(), to_png()
       01 DM-PLOT-TO-PDF.
      *>> Self: the PLOT handle.
          05 DM-PLOT-TO-PDF-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<std::uint8_t>): VECTOR-UCHAR handle (new;
      *>>   close it). The complete PDF file contents.
          05 DM-PLOT-TO-PDF-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::Plot::save_png(const std::string & path)
