      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::size(std::size_t width,
      *>>   std::size_t height) -> RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_size" USING DM-R-PLOT-SIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Sets the canvas size in pixels (default 960 by 640), like the
      *>>   `width`/`height`
      *>> of R's `png()` or `svg()` device.
      *>>
      *>> Not validated here: rendering throws std::runtime_error when
      *>>   the canvas leaves no room
      *>> inside the margins (by default the canvas must exceed 114 by
      *>>   156 pixels).
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(1.0,
      *>>   2.0)).size(400, 300);
      *>> std::print("{}x{}\n", plt.width(), plt.height()); // 400x300
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: margins()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-SIZE.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> width (std::size_t): unsigned long. Canvas width in pixels.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-SIZE-WIDTH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> height (std::size_t): unsigned long. Canvas height in pixels.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-SIZE-HEIGHT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-SIZE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

