      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::hide_axes(bool enabled = true) ->
      *>>   RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_hide_axes" USING DM-R-PLOT-HIDE-AXES DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Hides the axis lines, tick labels, grid, and axis labels, like
      *>>   R's `axes = FALSE,
      *>> ann = FALSE` (the title and subtitle are still drawn).
      *>>
      *>> pie() turns this on. Margins are unchanged, so call margins()
      *>>   as well to let the data use
      *>> the freed space.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(1.0,
      *>>   2.0)).hide_axes();
      *>> std::print("{}\n", plt.axes_hidden()); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `plot.default()` (`axes`, `ann`):
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/plot.default.html
      *>>
      *>> See also: show_grid(), margins()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-HIDE-AXES.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIDE-AXES-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIDE-AXES-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> enabled (bool = true): 0 or 1. True (the default) hides them;
      *>>   false shows them again.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIDE-AXES-ENABLED USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIDE-AXES-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::x_tick_labels(std::vector<std::string>
      *>>   labels) -> RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_x_tick_labels" USING DM-R-PLOT-X-TICK-LABELS
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Replaces the numeric x ticks with `labels` at x = 0, 1, 2,
      *>>   ..., like R's
      *>> `axis(1, at = 0:(n - 1), labels = labels)`.
      *>>
      *>> Matches the bar positions of barplot() and boxplot(). Clears
      *>>   any positions set by
      *>> x_ticks(); an empty vector restores the numeric ticks.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot(dm::c(0.0, 1.0, 2.0), dm::c(5.0, 3.0,
      *>>   4.0))
      *>>                .x_tick_labels({"low", "mid", "high"});
      *>> std::print("{}\n", plt.x_tick_label_list()[2]); // high
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `axis()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/axis.html
      *>>
      *>> See also: x_ticks(), y_tick_labels()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-X-TICK-LABELS.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-X-TICK-LABELS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> labels (std::vector<std::string>): VECTOR-STRING handle. Tick
      *>>   texts, in order.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-X-TICK-LABELS-LABELS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-X-TICK-LABELS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::x_ticks(std::vector<double>
      *>>   positions, std::vector<std::string> labels) -> RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_x_ticks" USING DM-R-PLOT-X-TICKS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Replaces the numeric x ticks with `labels` drawn at data
      *>>   positions `positions`,
      *>> like R's `axis(1, at = positions, labels = labels)`.
      *>>
      *>> Positions need not be sorted or inside the visible range. Two
      *>>   empty vectors restore the
      *>> numeric ticks.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto x = dm::seql(0.0, 6.283, 50);
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot(x, dm::sin(x))
      *>>                .x_ticks({0.0, 3.1416, 6.2832}, {"0", "pi", "2
      *>>                  pi"})
      *>>                .y_ticks({-1.0, 0.0, 1.0}, {"min", "0",
      *>>                  "max"});
      *>> std::print("{}\n", plt.x_tick_position_list()[1]); // 3.1416
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `axis()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/axis.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the two vectors differ in length;
      *>>   the plot is unchanged.
      *>>
      *>> See also: x_tick_labels(), y_ticks()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-X-TICKS.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-X-TICKS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> positions (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. x data
      *>>   coordinates of the ticks.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-X-TICKS-POSITIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> labels (std::vector<std::string>): VECTOR-STRING handle. Tick
      *>>   texts, one per position.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-X-TICKS-LABELS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-X-TICKS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::y_tick_labels(std::vector<std::string>
      *>>   labels) -> RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_y_tick_labels" USING DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICK-LABELS
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Replaces the numeric y ticks with `labels` at y = 0, 1, 2,
      *>>   ..., like R's
      *>> `axis(2, at = 0:(n - 1), labels = labels)`.
      *>>
      *>> Clears any positions set by y_ticks(); an empty vector
      *>>   restores the numeric ticks.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot(dm::c(3.0, 5.0), dm::c(0.0,
      *>>   1.0)).y_tick_labels({"no", "yes"});
      *>> std::print("{}\n", plt.y_tick_label_list().size()); // 2
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `axis()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/axis.html
      *>>
      *>> See also: y_ticks(), x_tick_labels()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICK-LABELS.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICK-LABELS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> labels (std::vector<std::string>): VECTOR-STRING handle. Tick
      *>>   texts, in order.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICK-LABELS-LABELS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICK-LABELS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::y_ticks(std::vector<double>
      *>>   positions, std::vector<std::string> labels) -> RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_y_ticks" USING DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICKS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Replaces the numeric y ticks with `labels` drawn at data
      *>>   positions `positions`,
      *>> like R's `axis(2, at = positions, labels = labels)`.
      *>>
      *>> Two empty vectors restore the numeric ticks.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> See x_ticks(), which sets both axes.
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `axis()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/axis.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the two vectors differ in length;
      *>>   the plot is unchanged.
      *>>
      *>> See also: y_tick_labels(), x_ticks()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICKS.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICKS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> positions (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. y data
      *>>   coordinates of the ticks.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICKS-POSITIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> labels (std::vector<std::string>): VECTOR-STRING handle. Tick
      *>>   texts, one per position.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICKS-LABELS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-Y-TICKS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::margins(double left, double right,
      *>>   double top, double bottom) -> RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_margins" USING DM-R-PLOT-MARGINS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Overrides the automatic outer margins around the plotting
      *>>   area, in pixels, like
      *>> R's `par(mai =)` (which uses inches and orders bottom, left,
      *>>   top, right).
      *>>
      *>> The automatic margins are left 90, right 24, top 72 (96 when a
      *>>   subtitle is set), and
      *>> bottom 84; they leave room for the title, axis labels, and
      *>>   ticks. Explicit margins are used
      *>> as given, with no extra room for a subtitle. Tight margins
      *>>   suit small multi-panel tiles
      *>> whose title and axis labels are empty. Rendering throws
      *>>   std::runtime_error if the margins
      *>> leave no plotting area.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto tile = dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(2.0, 1.0))
      *>>                 .set_title("").set_xlab("").set_ylab("")
      *>>                 .margins(30, 10, 10, 20)
      *>>                 .tick_font_size(9);
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n", tile.has_custom_margins(),
      *>>   tile.margin_left()); // true 30
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `par()` (`mai`, `mar`):
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/par.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If any margin is negative or
      *>>   non-finite; the plot is unchanged.
      *>>
      *>> See also: size(), tick_font_size(), RLayout
       01 DM-R-PLOT-MARGINS.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-MARGINS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> left (double): double. Left margin in pixels.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-MARGINS-LEFT USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> right (double): double. Right margin in pixels.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-MARGINS-RIGHT USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> top (double): double. Top margin in pixels.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-MARGINS-TOP USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> bottom (double): double. Bottom margin in pixels.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-MARGINS-BOTTOM USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-MARGINS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::tick_font_size(double pixels) ->
      *>>   RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_tick_font_size" USING DM-R-PLOT-TICK-FONT-SIZE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Sets the tick-label font size in pixels (default 12), like R's
      *>>   `cex.axis`.
      *>>
      *>> In SVG output the size is used as given. The raster outputs
      *>>   (PNG, PDF, show()) draw tick
      *>> labels with half-size glyphs when the size is below 12.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> See margins(), which shrinks the ticks for a small tile.
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `par()` (`cex.axis`):
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/par.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If `pixels` is not positive and
      *>>   finite; the plot is unchanged.
      *>>
      *>> See also: margins()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-TICK-FONT-SIZE.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-TICK-FONT-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> pixels (double): double. Font size in pixels.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-TICK-FONT-SIZE-PIXELS USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-TICK-FONT-SIZE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::pretty_ticks(bool enabled = true)
      *>>   -> RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_pretty_ticks" USING DM-R-PLOT-PRETTY-TICKS
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Places numeric ticks at round values (default on) instead of
      *>>   six evenly spaced
      *>> ticks across the range, in the spirit of R's `pretty()`.
      *>>
      *>> The step is 1, 2, or 5 times a power of ten, chosen as the
      *>>   "nice number" nearest a fifth
      *>> of the visible range (Heckbert's rule), and ticks are its
      *>>   multiples inside the range.
      *>> That gives about four to seven ticks, close to R's `pretty()`:
      *>>   a padded range of -0.365
      *>> to 7.665 gets ticks at 0, 2, 4 and 6. Custom tick labels take
      *>>   precedence. The background
      *>> grid follows the ticks.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot(dm::c(0.0, 100.0), dm::c(0.0,
      *>>   1.0)).pretty_ticks();
      *>> std::print("{}\n", plt.to_svg().contains(">40</text>")); //
      *>>   true: ticks 0, 20, ..., 100
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `pretty()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/base/html/pretty.html
      *>> - P. S. Heckbert (1990). "Nice Numbers for Graph Labels". In
      *>>   Graphics Gems, 61-63.
      *>>   Academic Press. doi:10.1016/B978-0-08-050753-8.50020-8
      *>>
      *>> See also: x_ticks(), show_grid()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-PRETTY-TICKS.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PRETTY-TICKS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PRETTY-TICKS-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              0.
      *>> enabled (bool = true): 0 or 1. True turns round ticks on;
      *>>   false restores six even ticks.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PRETTY-TICKS-ENABLED USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PRETTY-TICKS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::graphics::RPlot::plot(std::vector<double> x,
      *>>   std::vector<double> y, std::string type = "p", std::string
      *>>   label = "", RGBA color = ...) -> RPlot
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_plot" USING DM-R-PLOT-PLOT DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Builds a scatter, line, or line-plus-points plot of `y`
      *>>   against `x`, like R's
      *>> `plot(x, y, type = "p" | "l" | "b")`.
      *>>
      *>> `"p"` (the default) adds one scatter series with 4-pixel
      *>>   markers; `"l"` adds one 2-pixel
      *>> line joining the points in input order; `"b"` adds the line
      *>>   and then unlabeled points on
      *>> top (R's `"b"` leaves gaps in the line around each point; this
      *>>   draws it through them). The
      *>> title and axis labels keep their defaults. `RPlot(x, y)` is
      *>>   `plot(x, y)`.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto x = dm::seql(0.0, 4.0, 5);
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot::plot(x, x * x, "b", "x squared");
      *>> std::print("{} series\n", plt.series().size()); // 2 series
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `plot.default()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/plot.default.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the coordinates are empty or
      *>>   differ in length, or `type` is not one of the three codes.
      *>>
      *>> See also: RPlot(std::vector<double>, std::vector<double>),
      *>>   points(), lines()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 5 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> x (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Horizontal
      *>>   coordinates, one per point.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT-X USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> y (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Vertical
      *>>   coordinates, paired with `x` by position.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT-Y USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> type (std::string = "p"): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims
      *>>   trailing spaces. `"p"` (default), `"l"`, or `"b"`;
      *>>   case-sensitive.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT-TYPE PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT-TYPE-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> label (std::string = ""): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims
      *>>   trailing spaces. Legend text; empty (the default) keeps the
      *>>   plot out of the automatic legend. With `"b"` only the line
      *>>   carries it.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT-LABEL PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT-LABEL-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> color (RGBA): RGB handle. Color of the points and line
      *>>   (default blue `{37, 99, 235}`).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT-COLOR USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot): R-PLOT handle (new; close it). A new plot
      *>>   holding the series.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PLOT-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::graphics::RPlot::hist(std::vector<double>
      *>>   data, std::size_t bins = 10, std::string label = "", RGBA
      *>>   color = ...) -> RPlot
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_hist" USING DM-R-PLOT-HIST DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Builds a frequency histogram of `data` with `bins` equal-width
      *>>   bins, like R's
      *>> `hist(x, breaks = bins)`.
      *>>
      *>> The bins split [min, max] of the data into equal widths (R
      *>>   instead treats `breaks` as a
      *>> suggestion and uses `pretty()` boundaries). Bins include their
      *>>   left edge and exclude their
      *>> right edge, except that the maximum goes in the final bin; R's
      *>>   default (`right = TRUE`) is
      *>> the opposite, so a value on an inner boundary is counted one
      *>>   bin higher here. Constant
      *>> data uses the range [value, value + 1]. Each bin is one bar of
      *>>   height equal to its count,
      *>> centered on the bin with width equal to the bin width. The
      *>>   title is "Histogram", the x
      *>> label "x", and the y label "Frequency". The data is consumed;
      *>>   the plot keeps only counts.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot::hist({1.0, 2.0, 2.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 4.0},
      *>>   3);
      *>> const auto& bars = plt.series()[0]; // bins [1,2) [2,3) [3,4]
      *>> std::print("{} {} {}\n", bars.y[0], bars.y[1], bars.y[2]); //
      *>>   1 2 4
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `hist()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/hist.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For empty/non-finite data, zero bins,
      *>>   or a range/bin width that cannot be represented as a finite
      *>>   positive double.
      *>>
      *>> See also: dm::Histogram, bars()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-HIST.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIST-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> data (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Observations; all must be finite.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIST-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> bins (std::size_t = 10): unsigned long. Number of bins
      *>>   (default 10).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIST-BINS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> label (std::string = ""): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims
      *>>   trailing spaces. Legend text; empty (the default) shows no
      *>>   legend.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIST-LABEL PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIST-LABEL-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> color (RGBA): RGB handle. Bar color (default light blue `{96,
      *>>   165, 250}`).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIST-COLOR USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot): R-PLOT handle (new; close it). A new plot
      *>>   holding one Bar series.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-HIST-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::graphics::RPlot::barplot(std::vector<double>
      *>>   heights, std::vector<std::string> names = {}, std::string
      *>>   label = "", RGBA color = ...) -> RPlot
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_barplot" USING DM-R-PLOT-BARPLOT DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Builds a bar chart with one bar per height, like R's
      *>> `barplot(heights, names.arg = names)`.
      *>>
      *>> Bar i is centered at x = i (0, 1, 2, ...) and is 0.8 units
      *>>   wide (R puts default bars at
      *>> 0.7, 1.9, 3.1, ...). Bars rise from 0, so negative heights
      *>>   point down, and the y range
      *>> always includes 0. Nonempty `names` become x tick labels under
      *>>   the bars. The title and
      *>> axis labels keep their defaults.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot::barplot({3.0, 5.0, 2.0}, {"a", "b",
      *>>   "c"}).set_title("Counts");
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n", plt.series()[0].x[2],
      *>>   plt.x_tick_label_list()[2]); // 2 c
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `barplot()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/barplot.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If `heights` is empty or `names` is
      *>>   nonempty with a different length.
      *>>
      *>> See also: bars(), x_tick_labels()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-BARPLOT.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BARPLOT-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> heights (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Bar
      *>>   heights, in display order.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BARPLOT-HEIGHTS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> names (std::vector<std::string> = {}): VECTOR-STRING handle.
      *>>   Tick labels, one per bar; empty (the default) keeps numeric
      *>>   ticks.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BARPLOT-NAMES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> label (std::string = ""): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims
      *>>   trailing spaces. Legend text; empty (the default) shows no
      *>>   legend.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BARPLOT-LABEL PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BARPLOT-LABEL-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> color (RGBA): RGB handle. Bar color (default green `{22, 163,
      *>>   74}`).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BARPLOT-COLOR USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot): R-PLOT handle (new; close it). A new plot
      *>>   holding one Bar series.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BARPLOT-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static
      *>>   datamunge::graphics::RPlot::boxplot(std::vector<std::vector<double>>
      *>>   groups, std::vector<std::string> names = {}, RGBA color =
      *>>   ...) -> RPlot
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_boxplot" USING DM-R-PLOT-BOXPLOT DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Builds side-by-side box-and-whisker plots, one per group, like
      *>>   R's
      *>> `boxplot(list(...), names = names)`.
      *>>
      *>> Group g is drawn at x = g (0, 1, 2, ...) as a 0.6-unit-wide
      *>>   box from the first to the
      *>> third quartile with a line at the median. Quartiles are R's
      *>>   default "type 7" sample
      *>> quantiles. Whiskers reach the most extreme values within 1.5
      *>>   IQR of the box (Tukey's
      *>> rule), and values beyond are drawn as outlier points. R's
      *>>   `boxplot()` instead uses
      *>> Tukey's hinges (`fivenum()`), so for some sample sizes the box
      *>>   edges and the fences differ
      *>> slightly from R: for 1, ..., 9, 40 this gives quartiles 3.25
      *>>   and 7.75 where R draws
      *>> hinges at 3 and 8. All boxes share `color`; the title and axis
      *>>   labels keep their defaults.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot::boxplot({{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 40},
      *>>   {2, 4, 6}}, {"a", "b"});
      *>> const auto& y = plt.series()[0].y; // whisker_lo, q1, median,
      *>>   q3, whisker_hi, outliers...
      *>> std::print("{} {} {} {} {} | {}\n", y[0], y[1], y[2], y[3],
      *>>   y[4], y[5]);
      *>> // 1 3.25 5.5 7.75 9 | 40
      *>> plt.save("boxes.svg");
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - J. W. Tukey (1977). Exploratory Data Analysis.
      *>>   Addison-Wesley. (Box plot and the 1.5 IQR fences.)
      *>> - R. McGill, J. W. Tukey, W. A. Larsen (1978). "Variations of
      *>>   Box Plots". The American
      *>>   Statistician 32(1), 12-16.
      *>>     doi:10.1080/00031305.1978.10479236
      *>> - R. J. Hyndman, Y. Fan (1996). "Sample Quantiles in
      *>>   Statistical Packages". The American
      *>>   Statistician 50(4), 361-365.
      *>>     doi:10.1080/00031305.1996.10473566 (quantile type 7.)
      *>> - R `boxplot()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/boxplot.html
      *>> - R `boxplot.stats()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/grDevices/html/boxplot.stats.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If `groups` or any group is empty, or
      *>>   `names` is nonempty with a different length.
      *>>
      *>> See also: box(), x_tick_labels()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-BOXPLOT.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BOXPLOT-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> groups (std::vector<std::vector<double>>):
      *>>   VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. One vector of observations per
      *>>   box; each must be nonempty.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BOXPLOT-GROUPS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> names (std::vector<std::string> = {}): VECTOR-STRING handle.
      *>>   Tick labels under the boxes; empty (the default) keeps
      *>>   numeric ticks.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BOXPLOT-NAMES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> color (RGBA): RGB handle. Box, whisker, and outlier color
      *>>   (default light blue `{96, 165, 250}`).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BOXPLOT-COLOR USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot): R-PLOT handle (new; close it). A new plot
      *>>   holding one Box series per group (see DataSeries::Kind::Box
      *>>   for its layout).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-BOXPLOT-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static
      *>>   datamunge::graphics::RPlot::boxplot(std::vector<std::vector<double>>
      *>>   groups, std::vector<std::string> names, std::vector<RGBA>
      *>>   colors) -> RPlot
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plt_bxplt_vctr_vctr_dbl_vector_string_vector_rgb"
      *>>   USING DM-R-PLT-BXPLT-VCTR-VCTR-DBL-VECTOR-STRING-VECTOR-RGB
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> boxplot() with one color per box, like R's `boxplot(..., col =
      *>>   colors)`.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::graphics::RPlot::boxplot({{1, 2, 3}, {2, 4,
      *>>   6}}, {"a", "b"},
      *>>                                     std::vector<dm::RGB>{{78,
      *>>                                       121, 167}, {242, 142,
      *>>                                       43}});
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: As boxplot(), or if `colors` is
      *>>   empty.
      *>>
      *>> See also: boxplot(std::vector<std::vector<double>>,
      *>>   std::vector<std::string>, RGB)
       01 DM-R-PLT-BXPLT-VCTR-VCTR-DBL-VECTOR-STRING-VECTOR-RGB.
      *>> groups (std::vector<std::vector<double>>):
      *>>   VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. One vector of observations per
      *>>   box; each must be nonempty.
          05 DM-R-PLT-BXPLT-VCTR-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-STRNG-VCTR-RGB-GROUPS
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> names (std::vector<std::string>): VECTOR-STRING handle. Tick
      *>>   labels under the boxes; empty keeps numeric ticks.
          05 DM-R-PLT-BXPLT-VCTR-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-STRNG-VCTR-RGB-NAMES
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> colors (std::vector<RGBA>): VECTOR-RGB handle. Box colors,
      *>>   recycled when shorter than `groups`; must be nonempty.
          05 DM-R-PLT-BXPLT-VCTR-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-STRNG-VCTR-RGB-COLORS
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot): R-PLOT handle (new; close it). A new plot
      *>>   holding one Box series per group.
          05 DM-R-PLT-BXPLT-VCTR-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-STRNG-VCTR-RGB-RESULT
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::graphics::RPlot::pie(std::vector<double>
      *>>   values, std::vector<std::string> names = {},
      *>>   std::vector<RGBA> colors = {}) -> RPlot
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_pie" USING DM-R-PLOT-PIE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Builds a pie chart with one wedge per value, like R's
      *>> `pie(x, labels = names, col = colors, clockwise = TRUE)`.
      *>>
      *>> Wedge i spans the fraction values[i] / sum(values) of the
      *>>   circle. Wedges start at 12
      *>> o'clock and run clockwise (R's default starts at 3 o'clock and
      *>>   runs counter-clockwise).
      *>> Each wedge is a filled unit-radius polygon with 24 arc
      *>>   segments. Names, when given, are
      *>> drawn at radius 1.15 beside the middle of each wedge's arc and
      *>>   also label the wedges, so the
      *>> automatic legend lists them. Colors are recycled; empty uses
      *>>   an 8-color built-in palette
      *>> starting blue, red, green. The axes and grid are hidden and
      *>>   both ranges are fixed at
      *>> [-1.4, 1.4]. The pie is drawn in data units, so it is round
      *>>   only when the plotting area is
      *>> square, e.g. `.size(598, 640)` with the default margins; the
      *>>   default 960x640 canvas draws an
      *>> ellipse.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot::pie({3.0, 2.0, 1.0}, {"rent", "food",
      *>>   "fun"}).size(598, 640);
      *>> std::print("{}\n", plt.series().size()); // 6
      *>> plt.save("budget.svg");
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `pie()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/pie.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If `values` is empty, has a negative
      *>>   entry, or sums to 0, or `names` is nonempty with a different
      *>>   length.
      *>>
      *>> See also: polygon(), text()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-PIE.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PIE-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> values (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Wedge
      *>>   sizes; nonnegative, with a positive sum.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PIE-VALUES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> names (std::vector<std::string> = {}): VECTOR-STRING handle.
      *>>   Wedge labels; empty (the default) draws none.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PIE-NAMES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> colors (std::vector<RGBA> = {}): VECTOR-RGB handle. Wedge
      *>>   colors, recycled; empty (the default) uses the built-in
      *>>   palette.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PIE-COLORS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot): R-PLOT handle (new; close it). A new plot
      *>>   holding one Polygon series per wedge plus one Text series
      *>>   per name.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-PIE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::graphics::RPlot::curve(datamunge::Callback &
      *>>   f, double from, double to, std::size_t n = 101, std::string
      *>>   label = "", RGBA color = ...) -> RPlot
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_curve" USING DM-R-PLOT-CURVE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Plots a function over [`from`, `to`] as a line, like R's
      *>>   `curve(expr, from, to, n)`.
      *>>
      *>> Evaluates `f.call(x)` at `n` evenly spaced points including
      *>>   both ends, in increasing
      *>> order, and joins them with a 2-pixel line. `f` is used only
      *>>   during this call and is not
      *>> retained. Non-finite results are stored as-is. Exceptions
      *>>   thrown by `f.call()` propagate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> struct Square : dm::Callback {
      *>>   double call(double x) override { return x * x; }
      *>> };
      *>> Square square;
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot::curve(square, -1.0, 1.0, 5);
      *>> std::print("{}\n", plt.series()[0].y); // [1, 0.25, 0, 0.25,
      *>>   1]
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `curve()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/curve.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If `n` is below 2 or `to` is not
      *>>   greater than `from`.
      *>>
      *>> See also: lines()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE.
      *>> Arguments to send: 3 to 6 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 3.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 3.
      *>> f (datamunge::Callback &): CALLBACK handle. The function to
      *>>   draw: a dm::Callback subclass overriding `call(double)`.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE-F USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> from (double): double. Left end of the range.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE-FROM USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> to (double): double. Right end; must be greater than `from`.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE-TO USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> n (std::size_t = 101): unsigned long. Number of sample points,
      *>>   at least 2 (default 101, as in R).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE-N USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> label (std::string = ""): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims
      *>>   trailing spaces. Legend text; empty (the default) shows no
      *>>   legend.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE-LABEL PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE-LABEL-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> color (RGBA): RGB handle. Line color (default red `{220, 38,
      *>>   38}`).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE-COLOR USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot): R-PLOT handle (new; close it). A new plot
      *>>   holding one Line series.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-CURVE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::graphics::RPlot::qqnorm(std::vector<double>
      *>>   data, std::string label = "sample", RGBA color = ...) ->
      *>>   RPlot
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_qqnorm" USING DM-R-PLOT-QQNORM DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Builds a normal Q-Q plot: the sorted `data` against
      *>>   standard-normal quantiles,
      *>> like R's `qqnorm(y)`.
      *>>
      *>> The i-th smallest value (i = 1..n) is plotted against the
      *>>   normal quantile of the plotting
      *>> position (i - 0.5) / n. R's `ppoints()` uses that rule only
      *>>   for n > 10 and
      *>> (i - 3/8) / (n + 1/4) for n <= 10, so the x coordinates differ
      *>>   from R for small samples.
      *>> Points that fall on a straight line indicate normally
      *>>   distributed data; add the reference
      *>> line with qqline(). The title is "Normal Q-Q", the axis labels
      *>>   "Theoretical Quantiles"
      *>> and "Sample Quantiles".
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const std::vector<double> sample{3.0, 1.0, 2.0, 5.0, 4.0};
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot::qqnorm(sample).qqline(sample);
      *>> std::print("{:.4f}\n", plt.series()[0].x[0]); // -1.2816
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - M. B. Wilk, R. Gnanadesikan (1968). "Probability plotting
      *>>   methods for the analysis of
      *>>   data". Biometrika 55(1), 1-17. doi:10.1093/biomet/55.1.1
      *>> - R `qqnorm()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/qqnorm.html
      *>> - R `ppoints()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/ppoints.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If `data` has fewer than two values.
      *>>
      *>> See also: qqline()
       01 DM-R-PLOT-QQNORM.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-QQNORM-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> data (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. The sample;
      *>>   at least two values. Consumed (sorted in place).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-QQNORM-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> label (std::string = "sample"): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Legend text (default "sample", so the
      *>>   automatic legend shows one row; pass "" to hide it).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-QQNORM-LABEL PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-QQNORM-LABEL-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> color (RGBA): RGB handle. Point color (default blue `{37, 99,
      *>>   235}`).
          05 DM-R-PLOT-QQNORM-COLOR USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RPlot): R-PLOT handle (new; close it). A new plot
      *>>   holding one Scatter series.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-QQNORM-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::points(std::vector<double> x,
      *>>   std::vector<double> y, std::string label = "", RGBA color =
      *>>   ..., double marker_size = 4.0) -> RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plt_pnts_vctr_dbl_vector_double_string_rgb_double"
      *>>   USING DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VECTOR-DOUBLE-STRING-RGB-DOUBLE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Adds a scatter series to this plot, like R's `points(x, y, col
      *>>   = color)`.
      *>>
      *>> The coordinates are copied (or moved from rvalues) into a new
      *>>   series drawn above the
      *>> existing ones; axis ranges grow to include it. A nonempty
      *>>   `label` adds a row to the
      *>> automatic legend (shown only while no manual legend() entries
      *>>   exist).
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto x = dm::seql(0.0, 6.0, 13);
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot().set_title("sin and cos");
      *>> plt.points(x, dm::sin(x), "sin", dm::RGB{37, 99, 235})
      *>>    .points(x, dm::cos(x), "cos", dm::RGB{220, 38, 38}, 6.0);
      *>> plt.save("trig.svg"); // automatic legend lists "sin" and
      *>>   "cos"
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `points()`:
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/points.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the coordinates are empty or have
      *>>   different lengths.
      *>>
      *>> See also: points_colored(), dm::points(), set_col()
       01 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VECTOR-DOUBLE-STRING-RGB-DOUBLE.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-DBL-STRING-RGB-DOUBLE-SELF
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 5 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-DBL-STRING-RGB-DOUBLE-GIVEN
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> x (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Horizontal
      *>>   coordinates, one per point.
          05 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-DOUBLE-STRING-RGB-DOUBLE-X
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> y (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Vertical
      *>>   coordinates, paired with `x` by position.
          05 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-DOUBLE-STRING-RGB-DOUBLE-Y
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> label (std::string = ""): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims
      *>>   trailing spaces. Legend text for this series; empty (the
      *>>   default) keeps it out of the legend.
          05 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-DBL-STRING-RGB-DOUBLE-LABEL PIC
              X(256).
          05 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-DBL-STRNG-RGB-DBL-LBL-LNGTH
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> color (RGBA): RGB handle. Marker color for every point
      *>>   (default blue `{37, 99, 235}`).
          05 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-DBL-STRING-RGB-DOUBLE-COLOR
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> marker_size (double = 4.0): double. Marker radius in pixels
      *>>   (default 4).
          05 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-DBL-STRNG-RGB-DBL-MRKR-SIZE
              USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result (RPlot &): R-PLOT handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This plot, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-PLT-PNTS-VCTR-DBL-VCTR-DBL-STRNG-RGB-DOUBLE-RESULT
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RPlot::points_colored(std::vector<double>
      *>>   x, std::vector<double> y, std::vector<RGBA> colors, double
      *>>   marker_size = 4.0) -> RPlot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_plot_points_colored" USING DM-R-PLOT-POINTS-COLORED
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Appends scatter points with a recycled per-point RGB(A)
      *>>   palette.
      *>> Coordinates must have equal nonzero lengths; colors must not
      *>>   be empty.
      *>> A partial palette cycle is allowed without a warning. Colors
      *>>   retain their own alpha.
      *>> The series is unlabeled, so it never appears in the automatic
      *>>   legend.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto palette = dm::c(dm::RGB{255, 0, 0}, dm::RGB{0, 0,
      *>>   255});
      *>> auto plt = dm::Plot().points_colored(dm::c(1.0, 2.0, 3.0),
      *>>   dm::c(3.0, 2.0, 1.0), palette);
      *>> std::print("{}\n", plt.series()[0].point_colors.size()); // 2
      *>>   (red, blue, red)
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R `points()` (vector `col`):
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/points.html
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the coordinate lengths or palette
      *>>   are invalid.
      *>>
      *>> See also: dm::points() and Points::set_col(), the
      *>>   pipe-friendly form of this call.
       01 DM-R-PLOT-POINTS-COLORED.
      *>> Self: the R-PLOT handle.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-POINTS-COLORED-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 3 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 3.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-POINTS-COLORED-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 3.
      *>> x (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Horizontal
      *>>   coordinates.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-POINTS-COLORED-X USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> y (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Vertical
      *>>   coordinates, paired with `x`.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-POINTS-COLORED-Y USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> colors (std::vector<RGBA>): VECTOR-RGB handle. Palette; point
      *>>   i uses `colors[i % colors.size()]`.
          05 DM-R-PLOT-POINTS-COLORED-COLORS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> marker_size (double = 4.0): double. Marker radius in pixels
