      *>> datamunge::graphics::RLayout::title_text() const -> const
      *>>   std::string &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_title_text" USING DM-R-LAYOUT-TITLE-TEXT
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrows the figure-level heading for the lifetime of this
      *>>   layout.
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-TITLE-TEXT.
      *>> Self: the R-LAYOUT handle.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-TITLE-TEXT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const std::string &): text in PIC X(16384); -LENGTH is
      *>>   its length in bytes. The title; empty (the default) when
      *>>   none is drawn.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-TITLE-TEXT-RESULT PIC X(16384).
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-TITLE-TEXT-RESULT-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE 0.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RLayout::panel(std::size_t index) const
      *>>   -> const Plot &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_panel" USING DM-R-LAYOUT-PANEL DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrows the copy of the `index-th` added panel.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto fig = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,
      *>>   2).add(dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0), dm::c(1.0)).set_title("A"));
      *>> std::print("{}\n", fig.panel(0).title_text()); // A
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: If `index` is not below panel_count().
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-PANEL.
      *>> Self: the R-LAYOUT handle.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-PANEL-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> index (std::size_t): unsigned long. Zero-based panel index, in
      *>>   the order panels were added.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-PANEL-INDEX USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const Plot &): PLOT handle (new; refers into its
      *>>   owner, which it keeps alive). The stored copy, valid until
      *>>   the next add() or the layout's destruction.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-PANEL-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RLayout::to_svg() const -> std::string
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_to_svg" USING DM-R-LAYOUT-TO-SVG DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Renders the multi-panel figure as a standalone SVG document
      *>>   and returns it as a string.
      *>>
      *>> Each panel becomes a nested `<svg>` scaled into its cell. A
      *>>   layout with no panels renders
      *>> as an empty white figure. The layout is not modified.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto fig = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2,
      *>>   1).add(dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(1.0, 2.0)));
      *>> std::print("{}\n", fig.to_svg().starts_with("<?xml")); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: save()
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-TO-SVG.
      *>> Self: the R-LAYOUT handle.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-TO-SVG-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::string): text in PIC X(16384); -LENGTH is its
      *>>   length in bytes. The complete SVG text.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-TO-SVG-RESULT PIC X(16384).
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-TO-SVG-RESULT-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RLayout::save(const std::string & path)
      *>>   const -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_save" USING DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Saves the figure, choosing the format from the extension:
      *>>   `.svg` (or none) writes
      *>> SVG, `.png` / `.pdf` write the same tiled raster the X11
      *>>   viewer shows.
      *>>
      *>> The extension is case-sensitive and an existing file is
      *>>   overwritten. Raster panels are
      *>> re-rendered from the stored copies and scaled into their
      *>>   cells.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> See RLayout.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For any other extension.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the file cannot be written.
      *>>
      *>> See also: save_svg(), to_svg(), show()
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE.
      *>> Self: the R-LAYOUT handle.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> path (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Destination file.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE-PATH PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE-PATH-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RLayout::save_svg(const std::string &
      *>>   path) const -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_save_svg" USING DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE-SVG
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Writes to_svg() to `path` regardless of its extension.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the file cannot be opened for
      *>>   writing.
      *>>
      *>> See also: save()
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE-SVG.
      *>> Self: the R-LAYOUT handle.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE-SVG-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> path (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Destination file; an existing file is
      *>>   overwritten.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE-SVG-PATH PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SAVE-SVG-PATH-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RLayout::to_png() const ->
      *>>   std::vector<std::uint8_t>
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_to_png" USING DM-R-LAYOUT-TO-PNG DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Renders the tiled figure as PNG image bytes (the raster save()
      *>>   writes for `.png`).
