      *>> datamunge::graphics::RLayout::fit_panels() -> RLayout &
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_fit_panels" USING DM-R-LAYOUT-FIT-PANELS
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Resizes every stored panel's canvas to its cell, so text keeps
      *>>   its pixel size
      *>> instead of being scaled with the panel.
      *>>
      *>> Call it after size() and title() (the title band changes the
      *>>   cell height). Panels added
      *>> later keep their own size until fit_panels() is called again.
      *>>   A cell whose shorter side is
      *>> under min_panel_px gets a canvas scaled up to that side (same
      *>>   aspect ratio), so its text is
      *>> drawn proportionally smaller instead of the margins
      *>>   overflowing the panel.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto fig = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      *>>                .add(dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(2.0,
      *>>                  1.0)))
      *>>                .add(dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(1.0,
      *>>                  2.0)))
      *>>                .size(1000, 400)
      *>>                .fit_panels();
      *>> std::print("{}x{}\n", fig.panel(0).width(),
      *>>   fig.panel(0).height()); // 500x400
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: size()
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-FIT-PANELS.
      *>> Self: the R-LAYOUT handle.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-FIT-PANELS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (RLayout &): R-LAYOUT handle (new; refers into its
      *>>   owner, which it keeps alive). This layout, for chaining.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-FIT-PANELS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RLayout::show(const std::string &
      *>>   title_hint = "") const -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_show" USING DM-R-LAYOUT-SHOW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Opens the tiled figure in the interactive X11 viewer; the
      *>>   toolbar zoom/pan buttons
      *>> act on every panel's data bounds at once, keyboard zoom/pan
      *>>   scales the whole image.
      *>>
      *>> Blocks until the window is closed (q or Escape). Use save() in
      *>>   headless code.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto x = dm::seql(0.0, 6.0, 30);
      *>> dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      *>>     .add(dm::Plot(x, dm::sin(x)))
      *>>     .add(dm::Plot(x, dm::cos(x)))
      *>>     .show("Trig");
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If X11 support was not enabled at build
      *>>   time or no display is available.
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If no panel was added.
      *>>
      *>> See also: save(), Plot::show()
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-SHOW.
      *>> Self: the R-LAYOUT handle.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SHOW-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SHOW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> title_hint (const std::string & = ""): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. Window title; empty (the
      *>>   default) uses title_text().
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SHOW-TITLE-HINT PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-SHOW-TITLE-HINT-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.

      *>> datamunge::graphics::RLayout::view(const std::string &
      *>>   title_hint = "") const -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_view" USING DM-R-LAYOUT-VIEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Same as show(); kept as an alias for older code.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::runtime_error: As for show().
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If no panel was added.
      *>>
      *>> See also: show()
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-VIEW.
      *>> Self: the R-LAYOUT handle.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-VIEW-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-VIEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> title_hint (const std::string & = ""): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. Window title; empty (the
      *>>   default) uses title_text().
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-VIEW-TITLE-HINT PIC X(256).
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-VIEW-TITLE-HINT-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.

      *>> static const std::size_t
      *>>   datamunge::graphics::RLayout::title_band_px
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_title_band_px_get" USING
      *>>   DM-R-LAYOUT-TITLE-BAND-PX DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Height in pixels of the heading band reserved above the panels
      *>>   when a title is set.
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-TITLE-BAND-PX.
      *>> Value (const std::size_t): unsigned long.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-TITLE-BAND-PX-VALUE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> static const std::size_t
      *>>   datamunge::graphics::RLayout::min_panel_px
      *>> CALL "dm_r_layout_min_panel_px_get" USING
      *>>   DM-R-LAYOUT-MIN-PANEL-PX DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Smallest canvas side fit_panels() gives a panel; smaller cells
      *>>   get a larger canvas
      *>> with the cell's aspect ratio, scaled down when drawn, so the
      *>>   margins still fit.
       01 DM-R-LAYOUT-MIN-PANEL-PX.
      *>> Value (const std::size_t): unsigned long.
          05 DM-R-LAYOUT-MIN-PANEL-PX-VALUE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   DTW-RESULT

      *>> datamunge::geometry::DTWResult::DTWResult() -> DTW-RESULT
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_result_new" USING DM-DTW-RESULT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::DTWResult. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Owned unrestricted scalar DTW result, preserving the original
      *>>   three-field layout.
      *>> Distance is the unnormalized sum of absolute differences along
      *>>   the returned
      *>> inclusive path. Default construction is an uncomputed
      *>>   placeholder. Copies own
      *>> independent buffers. Positive lengths fit int; steps advance
      *>>   a, b or both by one.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   r=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping({1,2,3},{1,1,2,3});
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n",r.distance,r.path_a.size()); // 0 4
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: dynamic_time_warping(), dtw_path_cost()
       01 DM-DTW-RESULT-NEW.
      *>> Result: DTW-RESULT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-DTW-RESULT-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> double datamunge::geometry::DTWResult::distance
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_result_distance_get" USING DM-DTW-RESULT-DISTANCE
      *>>   DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_result_distance_set" USING DM-DTW-RESULT-DISTANCE
      *>>   DM-STATUS (writes -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Finite nonnegative summed absolute loss for a computed result.
       01 DM-DTW-RESULT-DISTANCE.
      *>> Self: the DTW-RESULT handle.
          05 DM-DTW-RESULT-DISTANCE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (double): double.
          05 DM-DTW-RESULT-DISTANCE-VALUE USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> std::vector<int> datamunge::geometry::DTWResult::path_a
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_result_path_a_get" USING DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-A
      *>>   DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_result_path_a_set" USING DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-A
      *>>   DM-STATUS (writes -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Owned zero-based a indices, from zero to a.size()-1.
       01 DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-A.
      *>> Self: the DTW-RESULT handle.
          05 DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-A-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (std::vector<int>): VECTOR-INT handle (new; refers into
      *>>   its owner, which it keeps alive).
          05 DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-A-VALUE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> std::vector<int> datamunge::geometry::DTWResult::path_b
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_result_path_b_get" USING DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-B
      *>>   DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_result_path_b_set" USING DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-B
      *>>   DM-STATUS (writes -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Owned parallel b indices, from zero to b.size()-1.
       01 DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-B.
      *>> Self: the DTW-RESULT handle.
          05 DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-B-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (std::vector<int>): VECTOR-INT handle (new; refers into
      *>>   its owner, which it keeps alive).
          05 DM-DTW-RESULT-PATH-B-VALUE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   DTW-WORK

      *>> datamunge::geometry::DTWWork::DTWWork() -> DTW-WORK handle
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_work_new" USING DM-DTW-WORK-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::DTWWork. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Logical work of the shared DTW recurrence and actual
      *>>   traceback.
      *>> These are counts, not time. Validation, allocation, copies,
      *>>   comparisons and
      *>> rendering are excluded. Each positive cell reads three
      *>>   predecessor slots,
      *>> including infinite boundary slots. Every returned pair counts
      *>>   one traceback step.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto r=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_work({2},{5});
      *>> std::print("{} {}
      *>>   {}\n",r.work.cells,r.work.predecessor_reads,r.work.traceback_steps);
      *>>   // 1 3 1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: DTWComputation
       01 DM-DTW-WORK-NEW.
      *>> Result: DTW-WORK handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-DTW-WORK-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> std::uint64_t datamunge::geometry::DTWWork::cells
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_work_cells_get" USING DM-DTW-WORK-CELLS DM-STATUS
      *>>   (reads -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_work_cells_set" USING DM-DTW-WORK-CELLS DM-STATUS
      *>>   (writes -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Exactly a.size()*b.size() recurrence evaluations.
       01 DM-DTW-WORK-CELLS.
      *>> Self: the DTW-WORK handle.
          05 DM-DTW-WORK-CELLS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
