      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   DTW-TRACE

      *>> datamunge::geometry::DTWTrace::DTWTrace() -> DTW-TRACE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_trace_new" USING DM-DTW-TRACE-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::geometry::DTWTrace. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Owned input, actual accumulated costs and chosen predecessors
      *>>   from one DTW run.
      *>> Positive cells are row-major at i*b.size()+j; sentinel border
      *>>   is implicit.
      *>> Costs and predecessor codes are captured during the original
      *>>   recurrence,
      *>> not reconstructed afterward. Infinite cells mark
      *>>   unrepresentable costs.
      *>> Logical capture entries are
      *>>   a.size()+b.size()+2*a.size()*b.size(): one
      *>> per input scalar, cost and direction. Result paths, rolling
      *>>   scratch rows,
      *>> scalar metadata and allocator bytes are excluded. Copies are
      *>>   independent.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto
      *>>   t=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_trace({1},{4});
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n",t.cumulative[0],t.captured_entries); // 3
      *>>   4
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: dynamic_time_warping_trace(), dtw_trace_entries()
       01 DM-DTW-TRACE-NEW.
      *>> Result: DTW-TRACE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-DTW-TRACE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> std::vector<double> datamunge::geometry::DTWTrace::a
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_trace_a_get" USING DM-DTW-TRACE-A DM-STATUS
      *>>   (reads -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_dtw_trace_a_set" USING DM-DTW-TRACE-A DM-STATUS
      *>>   (writes -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Owned first input, unchanged by alignment.
       01 DM-DTW-TRACE-A.
