      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   RHS

      *>> datamunge::ode::RHS::RHS() -> RHS handle with COBOL overrides
      *>> CALL "dm_rhs_extend" USING DM-RHS-EXTEND DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::ode::RHS. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A COBOL subclass: each PROGRAM-POINTER names the COBOL program
      *>>   that overrides that virtual method. The program receives its
      *>>   -ARGS record (in the callbacks copybook) and the callback
      *>>   status.
      *>>
      *>> Must override: EVALUATE.
      *>>
      *>> Right-hand side of a first-order ODE system dy/dt = f(t, y): R
      *>>   x R^n -> R^n.
      *>> Director-enabled only in the Python binding, matching
      *>>   datamunge::filter::VectorFunction
      *>> (the closest existing precedent -- a vector<double>-returning
      *>>   pure-virtual director):
      *>> every other SWIG backend either has no director support at
      *>>   all, or -- confirmed by a
      *>> real compile failure while wiring this class up in R -- cannot
      *>>   generate a working
      *>> director wrapper for a virtual method that returns
      *>>   std::vector<double>. Every other
      *>> binding can only use ODESolver::solve_builtin()'s fixed set of
      *>>   named systems, since a
      *>> live user-supplied RHS requires exactly that subclassing.
       01 DM-RHS-EXTEND.
      *>> Override of datamunge::ode::RHS::evaluate(double t, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & y) -> std::vector<double>: SET it TO
      *>>   ENTRY "PROGRAM-ID", or leave it NULL (required: pure
      *>>   virtual).
          05 DM-RHS-EXTEND-EVALUATE USAGE PROGRAM-POINTER.
      *>> Result: RHS handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-RHS-EXTEND-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::ode::RHS::evaluate(double t, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & y) -> std::vector<double>
      *>> CALL "dm_rhs_evaluate" USING DM-RHS-EVALUATE DM-STATUS
       01 DM-RHS-EVALUATE.
      *>> Self: the RHS handle.
          05 DM-RHS-EVALUATE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> t (double): double.
          05 DM-RHS-EVALUATE-T USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> y (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
          05 DM-RHS-EVALUATE-Y USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; close
      *>>   it).
          05 DM-RHS-EVALUATE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

