      *>> datamunge::ode::ODESolution::ODESolution() -> ODE-SOLUTION
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_ode_solution_new" USING DM-ODE-SOLUTION-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::ode::ODESolution. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> One numerically integrated trajectory: t[i] paired with y[i]
      *>>   (the full state vector
      *>> at that time), in increasing-time order, always including both
      *>>   endpoints. `t` and `y`
      *>> are public fields for direct C++ use, but are not exposed to
      *>>   language bindings (a
      *>> container-typed struct *field getter* -- even a plain
      *>>   vector<double>, not just a
      *>> nested vector<vector<double>> -- hits a swig-jse R-backend
      *>>   codegen bug that a
      *>> same-shaped plain *method* return does not) --
      *>>   time_at()/state_at()/size() are the
      *>> cross-language-safe way to read it.
       01 DM-ODE-SOLUTION-NEW.
      *>> Result: ODE-SOLUTION handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-ODE-SOLUTION-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

