      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   ACOR

      *>> datamunge::optim::ACOR::ACOR(ACOROptions options = {}) -> ACOR
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_acor_new" USING DM-ACOR-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::ACOR. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Ant Colony Optimization for continuous domains (ACOR), Socha &
      *>>   Dorigo (2008). A
      *>> solution archive of size k is maintained; each iteration, new
      *>>   ants are sampled from a
      *>> Gaussian kernel mixture built from the archive (ranked by
      *>>   quality, so better solutions
      *>> attract denser sampling), then the archive is truncated back
      *>>   to its k best members
      *>> merged with the new ants. Derivative-free, box-constrained.
       01 DM-ACOR-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-ACOR-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (ACOROptions = {}): ACOR-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-ACOR-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: ACOR handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-ACOR-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::ACOR::optimize(ArbitraryFunction & function,
      *>>   std::vector<double> & coordinates, const std::vector<double>
      *>>   & lower_bound, const std::vector<double> & upper_bound)
      *>>   const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_acor_optimize" USING DM-ACOR-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Minimizes `function` within [`lower_bound`, `upper_bound`],
      *>>   updating
      *>> `coordinates` in place to the best point found, and returns
      *>>   its value. The
      *>> initial `coordinates` (clamped into bounds) seed one member of
      *>>   the archive.
       01 DM-ACOR-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the ACOR handle.
          05 DM-ACOR-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
          05 DM-ACOR-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
          05 DM-ACOR-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> lower_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-ACOR-OPTIMIZE-LOWER-BOUND USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> upper_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-ACOR-OPTIMIZE-UPPER-BOUND USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double.
          05 DM-ACOR-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

