      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   ADAM

      *>> datamunge::optim::Adam::Adam(AdamOptions options = {}) -> ADAM
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_adam_new" USING DM-ADAM-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::Adam. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Adam on the DifferentiableFunction callback interface.
      *>> Bias-corrected full-batch first and second moments,
      *>>   denominator sqrt(vhat)+epsilon. Tests the pre-update
      *>>   gradient norm after applying its update. No line search or
      *>>   general nonconvex convergence guarantee; O(p) reset local
      *>>   state.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::Adam optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - D. P. Kingma and J. Ba (2015), Adam: A Method for Stochastic
      *>>   Optimization, https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.6980
      *>>
      *>> See also: AdamOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::Adam optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-ADAM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-ADAM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (AdamOptions = {}): ADAM-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   AdamOptions.
          05 DM-ADAM-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: ADAM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-ADAM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::Adam::optimize(DifferentiableFunction &
      *>>   function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_adam_optimize" USING DM-ADAM-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run Adam from the supplied point using the configured finite
      *>>   budget.
      *>> Bias-corrected full-batch first and second moments,
      *>>   denominator sqrt(vhat)+epsilon. Tests the pre-update
      *>>   gradient norm after applying its update. No line search or
      *>>   general nonconvex convergence guarantee; O(p) reset local
      *>>   state.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::AdamOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto value=dm::optim::Adam(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), AdamOptions
       01 DM-ADAM-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the ADAM handle.
          05 DM-ADAM-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (DifferentiableFunction &): DIFFERENTIABLE-FUNCTION
      *>>   handle. Borrowed DifferentiableFunction with matching finite
      *>>   output shapes.
          05 DM-ADAM-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-ADAM-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-ADAM-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::Adam::options() const -> const AdamOptions &
      *>> CALL "dm_adam_options" USING DM-ADAM-OPTIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
       01 DM-ADAM-OPTIONS.
      *>> Self: the ADAM handle.
          05 DM-ADAM-OPTIONS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const AdamOptions &): ADAM-OPTIONS handle (new; refers
      *>>   into its owner, which it keeps alive). Const option
      *>>   reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
          05 DM-ADAM-OPTIONS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

