      *>   ADA-DELTA

      *>> datamunge::optim::AdaDelta::AdaDelta(AdaDeltaOptions options =
      *>>   {}) -> ADA-DELTA handle
      *>> CALL "dm_ada_delta_new" USING DM-ADA-DELTA-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::AdaDelta. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> AdaDelta on the DifferentiableFunction callback interface.
      *>> Uses squared-gradient and squared-update exponential averages.
      *>>   The update multiplies the gradient by
      *>>   sqrt(previous_update_average+epsilon)/sqrt(current_gradient_average+epsilon).
      *>>   No separate learning-rate option. Tests the gradient used
      *>>   after applying its update; O(p) reset local state.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::AdaDelta optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - M. D. Zeiler (2012), ADADELTA: An Adaptive Learning Rate
      *>>   Method, https://arxiv.org/abs/1212.5701
      *>>
      *>> See also: AdaDeltaOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::AdaDelta optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-ADA-DELTA-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-ADA-DELTA-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (AdaDeltaOptions = {}): ADA-DELTA-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   AdaDeltaOptions.
          05 DM-ADA-DELTA-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: ADA-DELTA handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-ADA-DELTA-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::AdaDelta::optimize(DifferentiableFunction &
      *>>   function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_ada_delta_optimize" USING DM-ADA-DELTA-OPTIMIZE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run AdaDelta from the supplied point using the configured
      *>>   finite budget.
      *>> Uses squared-gradient and squared-update exponential averages.
      *>>   The update multiplies the gradient by
      *>>   sqrt(previous_update_average+epsilon)/sqrt(current_gradient_average+epsilon).
      *>>   No separate learning-rate option. Tests the gradient used
      *>>   after applying its update; O(p) reset local state.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::AdaDeltaOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto value=dm::optim::AdaDelta(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: AdaDelta: decay_rate must be in [0,
      *>>   1); AdaDelta: epsilon must be positive; AdaDelta: tolerance
      *>>   must be non-negative.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), AdaDeltaOptions
       01 DM-ADA-DELTA-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the ADA-DELTA handle.
          05 DM-ADA-DELTA-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (DifferentiableFunction &): DIFFERENTIABLE-FUNCTION
      *>>   handle. Borrowed DifferentiableFunction with matching finite
      *>>   output shapes.
          05 DM-ADA-DELTA-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-ADA-DELTA-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-ADA-DELTA-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::AdaDelta::options() const -> const
