      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN

      *>> datamunge::optim::AugmentedLagrangian::AugmentedLagrangian(AugmentedLagrangianOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN handle
      *>> CALL "dm_augmented_lagrangian_new" USING
      *>>   DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::AugmentedLagrangian. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> AugmentedLagrangian on the EqualityConstrainedFunction
      *>>   callback interface.
      *>> Uses fixed inner gradient steps on f+lambda*c+rho*||c||^2/2,
      *>>   capped so each displacement norm is at most one. Updates
      *>>   multipliers after each inner budget and doubles rho until
      *>>   feasibility tolerance or outer budget. No dual-stationarity
      *>>   test is exposed. Objective return alone is not a KKT
      *>>   certificate.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::AugmentedLagrangian optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_outer_iterations);
      *>>   // 50
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - J. Nocedal and S. J. Wright (2006), Numerical Optimization,
      *>>   second edition, https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-387-40065-5.
      *>>   The implemented variant and stopping rules are specified
      *>>   above.
      *>>
      *>> See also: AugmentedLagrangianOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::AugmentedLagrangian optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_outer_iterations);
      *>>   // 50
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (AugmentedLagrangianOptions = {}):
      *>>   AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIONS handle. Method-specific
      *>>   controls; defaults are listed by AugmentedLagrangianOptions.
          05 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::AugmentedLagrangian::optimize(EqualityConstrainedFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const ->
      *>>   double
      *>> CALL "dm_augmented_lagrangian_optimize" USING
      *>>   DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run AugmentedLagrangian from the supplied point using the
      *>>   configured finite budget.
      *>> Uses fixed inner gradient steps on f+lambda*c+rho*||c||^2/2,
      *>>   capped so each displacement norm is at most one. Updates
      *>>   multipliers after each inner budget and doubles rho until
      *>>   feasibility tolerance or outer budget. No dual-stationarity
      *>>   test is exposed. Objective return alone is not a KKT
      *>>   certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::EqualityQuadratic f({2,0},1);
      *>> dm::optim::AugmentedLagrangianOptions
      *>>   controls;controls.max_outer_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto
      *>>   value=dm::optim::AugmentedLagrangian(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: AugmentedLagrangian: positive
      *>>   step_size and penalty required.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), AugmentedLagrangianOptions
       01 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN handle.
          05 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (EqualityConstrainedFunction &):
      *>>   EQUALITY-CONSTRAINED-FUNCTION handle. Borrowed
      *>>   EqualityConstrainedFunction with matching finite output
      *>>   shapes.
          05 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::AugmentedLagrangian::options() const ->
      *>>   const AugmentedLagrangianOptions &
      *>> CALL "dm_augmented_lagrangian_options" USING
      *>>   DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
       01 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIONS.
      *>> Self: the AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN handle.
          05 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIONS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const AugmentedLagrangianOptions &):
      *>>   AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIONS handle (new; refers into its
      *>>   owner, which it keeps alive). Const option reference, valid
      *>>   during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
          05 DM-AUGMENTED-LAGRANGIAN-OPTIONS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   BAYESIAN-SURROGATE

      *>> datamunge::optim::BayesianSurrogate::BayesianSurrogate() ->
      *>>   BAYESIAN-SURROGATE handle with COBOL overrides
      *>> CALL "dm_bayesian_surrogate_extend" USING
      *>>   DM-BAYESIAN-SURROGATE-EXTEND DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::BayesianSurrogate. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A COBOL subclass: each PROGRAM-POINTER names the COBOL program
      *>>   that overrides that virtual method. The program receives its
      *>>   -ARGS record (in the callbacks copybook) and the callback
      *>>   status.
      *>>
      *>> Must override: FIT, ACQUISITION.
      *>>
      *>> Surrogate/acquisition extension point for
      *>>   BayesianOptimization.
      *>>
      *>> A surrogate is refitted to all observations before every
      *>>   proposal. acquisition() scores a
      *>> candidate point; the optimizer evaluates the objective where
      *>>   the score is largest.
      *>> RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate is the built-in implementation.
       01 DM-BAYESIAN-SURROGATE-EXTEND.
      *>> Override of datamunge::optim::BayesianSurrogate::fit(const
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & values) -> void: SET it TO ENTRY
      *>>   "PROGRAM-ID", or leave it NULL (required: pure virtual).
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-SURROGATE-EXTEND-FIT USAGE PROGRAM-POINTER.
      *>> Override of
      *>>   datamunge::optim::BayesianSurrogate::acquisition(const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & point, double incumbent) -> double:
      *>>   SET it TO ENTRY "PROGRAM-ID", or leave it NULL (required:
      *>>   pure virtual).
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-SURROGATE-EXTEND-ACQUISITION USAGE
              PROGRAM-POINTER.
      *>> Result: BAYESIAN-SURROGATE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-SURROGATE-EXTEND-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::BayesianSurrogate::fit(const
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const
