      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION

      *>> datamunge::optim::BayesianOptimization::BayesianOptimization(BayesianOptimizationOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION handle
      *>> CALL "dm_bayesian_optimization_new" USING
      *>>   DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::BayesianOptimization. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Minimises an expensive black-box function on a box with few
      *>>   evaluations.
      *>>
      *>> The loop is:
      *>> 1. evaluate `initial_samples` points drawn uniformly in
      *>>   `[lower, upper]`;
      *>> 2. repeat `max_iterations` times: fit the surrogate to all
      *>>   observations, score `candidates`
      *>>   uniform random points with BayesianSurrogate::acquisition()
      *>>     (the incumbent being the
      *>>   smallest value so far), polish the best one by compass
      *>>     search on the acquisition (steps
      *>>   of 10% of each side, halved `refine_iterations` times,
      *>>     clipped to the box), and evaluate
      *>>   the objective there.
      *>>
      *>> Only point evaluations of the objective are used, so it suits
      *>>   expensive simulations,
      *>> experiments and hyperparameter tuning where each evaluation
      *>>   costs far more than the
      *>> surrogate fit.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> struct Bowl : dm::optim::ArbitraryFunction {
      *>>     double evaluate(const std::vector<double>& x) override {
      *>>       return (x[0] - 1.0) * (x[0] - 1.0); }
      *>> } bowl;
      *>> dm::optim::RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate
      *>>   gp({.fit_hyperparameters = true});
      *>> const auto result =
      *>>   dm::optim::BayesianOptimization({.initial_samples = 4,
      *>>   .max_iterations = 10})
      *>>                         .run(bowl, {-3.0}, {3.0}, gp);
      *>> std::print("{:.3f} after {} evaluations\n",
      *>>   result.best_point[0], result.values.size()); // 1.002 after
      *>>   14 evaluations
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - D. R. Jones, M. Schonlau and W. J. Welch (1998). "Efficient
      *>>   global optimization of expensive
      *>>   black-box functions". Journal of Global Optimization 13,
      *>>     455–492.
      *>> - B. Shahriari et al. (2016). "Taking the human out of the
      *>>   loop: a review of Bayesian
      *>>   optimization". Proceedings of the IEEE 104(1), 148–175.
      *>>
      *>> See also: RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate, expected_improvement()
      *>>
      *>> Creates the optimizer.
       01 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (BayesianOptimizationOptions = {}):
      *>>   BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIONS handle. Design size, iteration
      *>>   count, seed and acquisition search settings.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::BayesianOptimization::run(ArbitraryFunction
      *>>   & function, const std::vector<double> & lower, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & upper, BayesianSurrogate & surrogate)
      *>>   const -> BayesianOptimizationResult
      *>> CALL "dm_bayesian_optimization_run" USING
      *>>   DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-RUN DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Runs the loop and records every evaluation.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the bounds are empty, differ in
      *>>   length or are not increasing.
       01 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-RUN.
      *>> Self: the BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION handle.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-RUN-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
      *>>   Objective to minimise.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-RUN-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> lower (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Lower corner of the box.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-RUN-LOWER USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> upper (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Upper corner of the box (each entry larger than in `lower`).
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-RUN-UPPER USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> surrogate (BayesianSurrogate &): BAYESIAN-SURROGATE handle.
      *>>   Surrogate refitted before every proposal.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-RUN-SURROGATE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (BayesianOptimizationResult):
      *>>   BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-RESULT handle (new; close it). The
      *>>   evaluations and the best point.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-RUN-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::BayesianOptimization::optimize(ArbitraryFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & lower, const std::vector<double> &
      *>>   upper, BayesianSurrogate & surrogate) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_bayesian_optimization_optimize" USING
      *>>   DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Runs the loop and returns only the best value.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the bounds do not match
      *>>   `coordinates` or are not increasing.
       01 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION handle.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
      *>>   Objective to minimise.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Output: the best point (its length must equal the bounds').
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> lower (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Lower corner of the box.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIMIZE-LOWER USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> upper (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Upper corner of the box.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIMIZE-UPPER USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> surrogate (BayesianSurrogate &): BAYESIAN-SURROGATE handle.
      *>>   Surrogate refitted before every proposal.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIMIZE-SURROGATE USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. The smallest observed value.
          05 DM-BAYESIAN-OPTIMIZATION-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

