      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   CMAES

      *>> datamunge::optim::CMAES::CMAES(CMAESOptions options = {}) ->
      *>>   CMAES handle
      *>> CALL "dm_cmaes_new" USING DM-CMAES-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::CMAES. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> CMAES on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface.
      *>> Unbounded covariance-adaptation evolution strategy with
      *>>   weighted elites, evolution paths and global step-size
      *>>   adaptation. Default offspring count is 4+floor(3*log(p)).
      *>>   Covariance eigensolve is dense with numerical eigenvalue
      *>>   floors. Stops on search-scale/axis tolerance or generation
      *>>   budget; stochastic results depend on seed and population,
      *>>   not a global certificate.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::CMAES optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - N. Hansen and A. Ostermeier (2001), Completely Derandomized
      *>>   Self-Adaptation in Evolution Strategies,
      *>>   https://doi.org/10.1162/106365601750190398
      *>>
      *>> See also: CMAESOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::CMAES optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-CMAES-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-CMAES-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (CMAESOptions = {}): CMAES-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   CMAESOptions.
          05 DM-CMAES-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: CMAES handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-CMAES-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::CMAES::optimize(ArbitraryFunction &
      *>>   function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_cmaes_optimize" USING DM-CMAES-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run CMAES from the supplied point using the configured finite
      *>>   budget.
      *>> Unbounded covariance-adaptation evolution strategy with
      *>>   weighted elites, evolution paths and global step-size
      *>>   adaptation. Default offspring count is 4+floor(3*log(p)).
      *>>   Covariance eigensolve is dense with numerical eigenvalue
      *>>   floors. Stops on search-scale/axis tolerance or generation
      *>>   budget; stochastic results depend on seed and population,
      *>>   not a global certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::CMAESOptions controls;controls.max_generations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto value=dm::optim::CMAES(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: CMAES: initial_step_size must be
      *>>   positive; CMAES: tolerance must be non-negative; CMAES:
      *>>   population_size must be at least 2.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), CMAESOptions
       01 DM-CMAES-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the CMAES handle.
          05 DM-CMAES-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
      *>>   Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output
      *>>   shapes.
          05 DM-CMAES-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-CMAES-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-CMAES-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::CMAES::options() const -> const CMAESOptions
      *>>   &
      *>> CALL "dm_cmaes_options" USING DM-CMAES-OPTIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
       01 DM-CMAES-OPTIONS.
      *>> Self: the CMAES handle.
          05 DM-CMAES-OPTIONS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const CMAESOptions &): CMAES-OPTIONS handle (new;
      *>>   refers into its owner, which it keeps alive). Const option
      *>>   reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
          05 DM-CMAES-OPTIONS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

