      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD

      *>> datamunge::optim::CrossEntropyMethod::CrossEntropyMethod(CrossEntropyMethodOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD handle
      *>> CALL "dm_cross_entropy_method_new" USING
      *>>   DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::CrossEntropyMethod. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> The Cross-Entropy Method (CEM) for derivative-free continuous
      *>>   optimization on an
      *>> ArbitraryFunction within a box constraint. A
      *>>   diagonal-covariance Gaussian search
      *>> distribution is repeatedly refit from the best ("elite")
      *>>   fraction of each generation's
      *>> samples, with the new distribution parameters exponentially
      *>>   smoothed against the
      *>> previous generation's for stability (Rubinstein 1997;
      *>>   Rubinstein & Kroese 2004).
       01 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (CrossEntropyMethodOptions = {}):
      *>>   CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::CrossEntropyMethod::optimize(ArbitraryFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double>
      *>>   & upper_bound) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_cross_entropy_method_optimize" USING
      *>>   DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Minimizes `function` within [`lower_bound`, `upper_bound`],
      *>>   updating
      *>> `coordinates` in place to the best point found, and returns
      *>>   its value. The
      *>> initial `coordinates` (clamped into bounds) seed the initial
      *>>   distribution mean.
       01 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD handle.
          05 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
          05 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
          05 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> lower_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-OPTIMIZE-LOWER-BOUND USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> upper_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-OPTIMIZE-UPPER-BOUND USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double.
          05 DM-CROSS-ENTROPY-METHOD-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

