      *>> double datamunge::optim::CuckooSearchOptions::discovery_rate
      *>> CALL "dm_cuckoo_search_options_discovery_rate_get" USING
      *>>   DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-OPTIONS-DISCOVERY-RATE DM-STATUS (reads
      *>>   -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_cuckoo_search_options_discovery_rate_set" USING
      *>>   DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-OPTIONS-DISCOVERY-RATE DM-STATUS (writes
      *>>   -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> pa: fraction of the worst nests discovered/abandoned each
      *>>   iteration. Yang & Deb's
      *>> original paper headlines 0.25, but this implementation's
      *>>   "replace a randomly
      *>> chosen comparison nest" Levy-flight rule (faithful to the
      *>>   paper) homogenizes the
      *>> population fast enough at pa=0.25 that convergence quality
      *>>   becomes sharply
      *>> seed-dependent on smooth objectives (verified: only 6/30 seeds
      *>>   converged well at
      *>> pa=0.25, population_size=25 on a simple 3D sphere). 0.4 --
      *>>   still within the
      *>> commonly-used literature range -- injects enough fresh
      *>>   diversity each iteration to
      *>> fix this at the default population size (verified: 30/30
      *>>   seeds).
       01 DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-OPTIONS-DISCOVERY-RATE.
      *>> Self: the CUCKOO-SEARCH-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-OPTIONS-DISCOVERY-RATE-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (double): double.
          05 DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-OPTIONS-DISCOVERY-RATE-VALUE USAGE COMP-2.

