      *>   CUCKOO-SEARCH

      *>> datamunge::optim::CuckooSearch::CuckooSearch(CuckooSearchOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> CUCKOO-SEARCH handle
      *>> CALL "dm_cuckoo_search_new" USING DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::CuckooSearch. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Cuckoo Search (Yang & Deb, 2009) on an ArbitraryFunction
      *>>   within a box constraint: a
      *>> population of nests is perturbed by heavy-tailed Levy flights
      *>>   (via Mantegna's
      *>> algorithm) and a fraction of the worst nests is abandoned and
      *>>   rebuilt each
      *>> iteration, mimicking brood parasitism. Derivative-free.
       01 DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              0.
      *>> options (CuckooSearchOptions = {}): CUCKOO-SEARCH-OPTIONS
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: CUCKOO-SEARCH handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-CUCKOO-SEARCH-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

