      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION

      *>> datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution::DifferentialEvolution(DEOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION handle
      *>> CALL "dm_differential_evolution_new" USING
      *>>   DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> DifferentialEvolution on the ArbitraryFunction callback
      *>>   interface.
      *>> Box-constrained differential mutation/crossover with greedy
      *>>   trial replacement. Supports the declared
      *>>   rand1/best1/current_to_best1/rand2 and binomial/exponential
      *>>   strategies. Coordinates seed one clamped member; more than
      *>>   twenty small-best-improvement generations can stop the run.
      *>>   O(population_size*p) storage; no global certificate.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R. Storn and K. Price (1997), Differential Evolution - A
      *>>   Simple and Efficient Heuristic for global Optimization over
      *>>   Continuous Spaces, https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1008202821328
      *>>
      *>> See also: DEOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (DEOptions = {}): DE-OPTIONS handle. Method-specific
      *>>   controls; defaults are listed by DEOptions.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution::optimize(ArbitraryFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double>
      *>>   & upper_bound) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_differential_evolution_optimize" USING
      *>>   DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run DifferentialEvolution from the supplied point using the
      *>>   configured finite budget.
      *>> Box-constrained differential mutation/crossover with greedy
      *>>   trial replacement. Supports the declared
      *>>   rand1/best1/current_to_best1/rand2 and binomial/exponential
      *>>   strategies. Coordinates seed one clamped member; more than
      *>>   twenty small-best-improvement generations can stop the run.
      *>>   O(population_size*p) storage; no global certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::DEOptions controls;controls.max_generations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto
      *>>   value=dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution(controls).optimize(f,x,std::vector<double>{-3,-3},std::vector<double>{3,3});
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: DifferentialEvolution::optimize:
      *>>   crossover_strategy must be 'binomial' or 'exponential'.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), DEOptions
       01 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION handle.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
      *>>   Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output
      *>>   shapes.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> lower_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Matching finite inclusive lower box limits.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIMIZE-LOWER-BOUND USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> upper_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Matching finite inclusive upper limits, greater than
      *>>   lower limits.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIMIZE-UPPER-BOUND USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution::options() const ->
      *>>   const DEOptions &
      *>> CALL "dm_differential_evolution_options" USING
      *>>   DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
       01 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIONS.
      *>> Self: the DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION handle.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIONS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const DEOptions &): DE-OPTIONS handle (new; refers
      *>>   into its owner, which it keeps alive). Const option
      *>>   reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
          05 DM-DIFFERENTIAL-EVOLUTION-OPTIONS-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

