      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION

      *>> datamunge::optim::EstimationOfDistribution::EstimationOfDistribution(EstimationOfDistributionOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION handle
      *>> CALL "dm_estimation_of_distribution_new" USING
      *>>   DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::EstimationOfDistribution. Close
      *>>   the handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Estimation of Distribution Algorithm (EMNA-style,
      *>>   full-covariance Gaussian) on an
      *>> ArbitraryFunction within a box constraint. Unlike
      *>>   explicit-operator methods (GA, DE)
      *>> or covariance-adapting methods (CMA-ES), EMNA builds an
      *>>   explicit multivariate Gaussian
      *>> model of where the good solutions are each generation --
      *>>   re-estimating its mean and
      *>> covariance from scratch as the empirical mean/covariance of
      *>>   the current generation's
      *>> elite, with no smoothing or evolution paths -- and samples the
      *>>   next generation directly
      *>> from that model. Derivative-free.
       01 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (EstimationOfDistributionOptions = {}):
      *>>   ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-NEW-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::EstimationOfDistribution::optimize(ArbitraryFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double>
      *>>   & upper_bound) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_estimation_of_distribution_optimize" USING
      *>>   DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Minimizes `function` within [`lower_bound`, `upper_bound`],
      *>>   updating
      *>> `coordinates` in place to the best point found, and returns
      *>>   its value. The
      *>> initial `coordinates` (clamped into bounds) seed the initial
      *>>   Gaussian mean.
       01 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION handle.
          05 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
          05 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
          05 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> lower_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-OPTIMIZE-LOWER-BOUND USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> upper_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle.
          05 DM-ESTIMATION-OF-DISTRIBUTION-OPTIMIZE-UPPER-BOUND USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
