      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   EVOLUTION-STRATEGY

      *>> datamunge::optim::EvolutionStrategy::EvolutionStrategy(EvolutionStrategyOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> EVOLUTION-STRATEGY handle
      *>> CALL "dm_evolution_strategy_new" USING
      *>>   DM-EVOLUTION-STRATEGY-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::EvolutionStrategy. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Classic self-adaptive (mu, lambda) / (mu+lambda) Evolution
      *>>   Strategy with a single
      *>> global step size mutated log-normally each generation
      *>>   (Rechenberg 1973, Schwefel
      *>> 1981). This is the pre-CMA-ES form -- no covariance matrix
      *>>   adaptation -- and is the
      *>> foundational lineage CMAES (also in this module) descends
      *>>   from. Derivative-free,
      *>> box-constrained.
       01 DM-EVOLUTION-STRATEGY-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-EVOLUTION-STRATEGY-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (EvolutionStrategyOptions = {}):
      *>>   EVOLUTION-STRATEGY-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-EVOLUTION-STRATEGY-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: EVOLUTION-STRATEGY handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-EVOLUTION-STRATEGY-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::EvolutionStrategy::optimize(ArbitraryFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double>
      *>>   & upper_bound) const -> double
