      *>   FIREFLY-ALGORITHM

      *>> datamunge::optim::FireflyAlgorithm::FireflyAlgorithm(FireflyAlgorithmOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> FIREFLY-ALGORITHM handle
      *>> CALL "dm_firefly_algorithm_new" USING DM-FIREFLY-ALGORITHM-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::FireflyAlgorithm. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> The Firefly Algorithm (Yang, 2008/2009): a population of
      *>>   fireflies is pairwise
      *>> attracted toward brighter (better) neighbors, with
      *>>   attractiveness decaying with
      *>> squared distance and a shrinking random-walk term for
      *>>   exploration. Derivative-free,
      *>> O(n^2) per iteration in the population size.
       01 DM-FIREFLY-ALGORITHM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-FIREFLY-ALGORITHM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (FireflyAlgorithmOptions = {}):
      *>>   FIREFLY-ALGORITHM-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-FIREFLY-ALGORITHM-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: FIREFLY-ALGORITHM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-FIREFLY-ALGORITHM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

