      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   FISTA

      *>> datamunge::optim::FISTA::FISTA(FISTAOptions options = {}) ->
      *>>   FISTA handle
      *>> CALL "dm_fista_new" USING DM-FISTA-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::FISTA. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> FISTA on the ProximalFunction callback interface.
      *>> Classical t recurrence (1+sqrt(1+4*t^2))/2 and extrapolated
      *>>   gradient points, followed by the supplied proximal map.
      *>>   Stops on successive accepted-coordinate displacement. No
      *>>   adaptive restart, backtracking or monotonicity safeguard.
      *>>   Supply the correct proximal dimensions and a rate at most
      *>>   1/L for the standard convex bound.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::FISTA optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - A. Beck and M. Teboulle (2009), A Fast Iterative
      *>>   Shrinkage-Thresholding Algorithm for Linear Inverse
      *>>   Problems, https://doi.org/10.1137/080716542
      *>>
      *>> See also: FISTAOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::FISTA optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-FISTA-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-FISTA-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (FISTAOptions = {}): FISTA-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   FISTAOptions.
          05 DM-FISTA-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: FISTA handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-FISTA-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::FISTA::optimize(ProximalFunction & function,
      *>>   std::vector<double> & coordinates) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_fista_optimize" USING DM-FISTA-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run FISTA from the supplied point using the configured finite
      *>>   budget.
      *>> Classical t recurrence (1+sqrt(1+4*t^2))/2 and extrapolated
      *>>   gradient points, followed by the supplied proximal map.
      *>>   Stops on successive accepted-coordinate displacement. No
      *>>   adaptive restart, backtracking or monotonicity safeguard.
      *>>   Supply the correct proximal dimensions and a rate at most
      *>>   1/L for the standard convex bound.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::L1LeastSquaresObjective f({{1}},{3},1);
      *>> dm::optim::FISTAOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0};
      *>> const auto value=dm::optim::FISTA(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: FISTA: step_size must be positive.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), FISTAOptions
       01 DM-FISTA-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the FISTA handle.
          05 DM-FISTA-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ProximalFunction &): PROXIMAL-FUNCTION handle.
      *>>   Borrowed ProximalFunction with matching finite output
      *>>   shapes.
          05 DM-FISTA-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-FISTA-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-FISTA-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::FISTA::options() const -> const FISTAOptions
      *>>   &
      *>> CALL "dm_fista_options" USING DM-FISTA-OPTIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
       01 DM-FISTA-OPTIONS.
      *>> Self: the FISTA handle.
          05 DM-FISTA-OPTIONS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const FISTAOptions &): FISTA-OPTIONS handle (new;
      *>>   refers into its owner, which it keeps alive). Const option
      *>>   reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
          05 DM-FISTA-OPTIONS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

