      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   GENETIC-ALGORITHM

      *>> datamunge::optim::GeneticAlgorithm::GeneticAlgorithm(GAOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> GENETIC-ALGORITHM handle
      *>> CALL "dm_genetic_algorithm_new" USING DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::GeneticAlgorithm. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> GeneticAlgorithm on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface.
      *>> Real-valued box-constrained selection, crossover, Gaussian
      *>>   mutation and optional elitism. Initial coordinates seed a
      *>>   clamped population member. Returns the best visited point
      *>>   and can stop after more than twenty small-best-improvement
      *>>   generations. O(population_size*p) storage; strategy/rate
      *>>   choices affect results, with no global certificate.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::GeneticAlgorithm optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - J. H. Holland (1992 reprint), Adaptation in Natural and
      *>>   Artificial Systems, MIT Press,
      *>>   https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262581110/adaptation-in-natural-and-artificial-systems/.
      *>>   This implementation uses real-valued operators, as specified
      *>>   above, rather than binary chromosomes.
      *>>
      *>> See also: GAOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::GeneticAlgorithm optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (GAOptions = {}): GA-OPTIONS handle. Method-specific
      *>>   controls; defaults are listed by GAOptions.
          05 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: GENETIC-ALGORITHM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::GeneticAlgorithm::optimize(ArbitraryFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double>
      *>>   & upper_bound) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_genetic_algorithm_optimize" USING
      *>>   DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run GeneticAlgorithm from the supplied point using the
      *>>   configured finite budget.
      *>> Real-valued box-constrained selection, crossover, Gaussian
      *>>   mutation and optional elitism. Initial coordinates seed a
      *>>   clamped population member. Returns the best visited point
      *>>   and can stop after more than twenty small-best-improvement
      *>>   generations. O(population_size*p) storage; strategy/rate
      *>>   choices affect results, with no global certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::GAOptions controls;controls.max_generations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto
      *>>   value=dm::optim::GeneticAlgorithm(controls).optimize(f,x,std::vector<double>{-3,-3},std::vector<double>{3,3});
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: GeneticAlgorithm::optimize:
      *>>   population_size must be at least 2.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), GAOptions
       01 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the GENETIC-ALGORITHM handle.
          05 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
      *>>   Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output
      *>>   shapes.
          05 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> lower_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Matching finite inclusive lower box limits.
          05 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-OPTIMIZE-LOWER-BOUND USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> upper_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Matching finite inclusive upper limits, greater than
      *>>   lower limits.
          05 DM-GENETIC-ALGORITHM-OPTIMIZE-UPPER-BOUND USAGE
