      *>> datamunge::optim::GreyWolfOptimizer::GreyWolfOptimizer(GreyWolfOptimizerOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> GREY-WOLF-OPTIMIZER handle
      *>> CALL "dm_grey_wolf_optimizer_new" USING
      *>>   DM-GREY-WOLF-OPTIMIZER-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::GreyWolfOptimizer. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Grey Wolf Optimizer (GWO) on an ArbitraryFunction within a box
      *>>   constraint: a
      *>> population of wolves is guided each iteration by its three
      *>>   best members (alpha,
      *>> beta, delta), moving every wolf to the elementwise average of
      *>>   three independently
      *>> randomized pulls toward those leaders. Derivative-free.
      *>>   Mirjalili, Mirjalili &
      *>> Lewis (2014), "Grey wolf optimizer", Advances in Engineering
      *>>   Software, 69, 46-61.
       01 DM-GREY-WOLF-OPTIMIZER-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-GREY-WOLF-OPTIMIZER-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (GreyWolfOptimizerOptions = {}):
      *>>   GREY-WOLF-OPTIMIZER-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-GREY-WOLF-OPTIMIZER-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: GREY-WOLF-OPTIMIZER handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-GREY-WOLF-OPTIMIZER-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::GreyWolfOptimizer::optimize(ArbitraryFunction
