      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   INTERIOR-POINT

      *>> datamunge::optim::InteriorPoint::InteriorPoint(InteriorPointOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> INTERIOR-POINT handle
      *>> CALL "dm_interior_point_new" USING DM-INTERIOR-POINT-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::InteriorPoint. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> InteriorPoint on the InequalityConstrainedFunction callback
      *>>   interface.
      *>> Gradient steps on f-mu*sum(log(-c)) with c<0. Backtracks only
      *>>   for strict feasibility, not barrier-objective decrease, then
      *>>   decays mu after each fixed inner budget. Requires a strictly
      *>>   feasible start and can fail later when feasible steps
      *>>   underflow. No KKT or barrier-stationarity stop test; no
      *>>   phase-I feasibility search.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::InteriorPoint optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_outer_iterations);
      *>>   // 20
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - J. Nocedal and S. J. Wright (2006), Numerical Optimization,
      *>>   second edition, https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-387-40065-5.
      *>>   The implemented variant and stopping rules are specified
      *>>   above.
      *>>
      *>> See also: InteriorPointOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::InteriorPoint optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_outer_iterations);
      *>>   // 20
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-INTERIOR-POINT-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-INTERIOR-POINT-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              0.
      *>> options (InteriorPointOptions = {}): INTERIOR-POINT-OPTIONS
      *>>   handle. Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   InteriorPointOptions.
          05 DM-INTERIOR-POINT-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: INTERIOR-POINT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-INTERIOR-POINT-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::InteriorPoint::optimize(InequalityConstrainedFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const ->
      *>>   double
      *>> CALL "dm_interior_point_optimize" USING
      *>>   DM-INTERIOR-POINT-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run InteriorPoint from the supplied point using the configured
      *>>   finite budget.
      *>> Gradient steps on f-mu*sum(log(-c)) with c<0. Backtracks only
      *>>   for strict feasibility, not barrier-objective decrease, then
      *>>   decays mu after each fixed inner budget. Requires a strictly
      *>>   feasible start and can fail later when feasible steps
      *>>   underflow. No KKT or barrier-stationarity stop test; no
      *>>   phase-I feasibility search.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::NonnegativeQuadratic f({-1,2});
      *>> dm::optim::InteriorPointOptions
      *>>   controls;controls.max_outer_iterations=1;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{.5,.5};
      *>> const auto
      *>>   value=dm::optim::InteriorPoint(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: InteriorPoint: starting point must be
      *>>   strictly feasible.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: InteriorPoint: unable to find feasible
      *>>   step.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), InteriorPointOptions
       01 DM-INTERIOR-POINT-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the INTERIOR-POINT handle.
          05 DM-INTERIOR-POINT-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (InequalityConstrainedFunction &):
      *>>   INEQUALITY-CONSTRAINED-FUNCTION handle. Borrowed
      *>>   InequalityConstrainedFunction with matching finite output
      *>>   shapes.
          05 DM-INTERIOR-POINT-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-INTERIOR-POINT-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-INTERIOR-POINT-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::InteriorPoint::options() const -> const
