      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   NELDER-MEAD

      *>> datamunge::optim::NelderMead::NelderMead(NelderMeadOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> NELDER-MEAD handle
      *>> CALL "dm_nelder_mead_new" USING DM-NELDER-MEAD-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::NelderMead. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> NelderMead on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface.
      *>> Local simplex reflection, expansion, contraction and shrink
      *>>   search. Starts with per-coordinate displacements
      *>>   initial_simplex_scale and stops when simplex diameter and
      *>>   value spread are small. Those conditions do not prove
      *>>   stationarity or a global minimum. O(p^2) simplex storage.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::NelderMead optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 2000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - J. A. Nelder and R. Mead (1965), A Simplex Method for
      *>>   Function Minimization,
      *>>   https://doi.org/10.1093/comjnl/7.4.308
      *>>
      *>> See also: NelderMeadOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::NelderMead optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 2000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-NELDER-MEAD-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-NELDER-MEAD-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (NelderMeadOptions = {}): NELDER-MEAD-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   NelderMeadOptions.
          05 DM-NELDER-MEAD-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: NELDER-MEAD handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-NELDER-MEAD-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::NelderMead::optimize(ArbitraryFunction &
      *>>   function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_nelder_mead_optimize" USING DM-NELDER-MEAD-OPTIMIZE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run NelderMead from the supplied point using the configured
      *>>   finite budget.
      *>> Local simplex reflection, expansion, contraction and shrink
      *>>   search. Starts with per-coordinate displacements
      *>>   initial_simplex_scale and stops when simplex diameter and
      *>>   value spread are small. Those conditions do not prove
      *>>   stationarity or a global minimum. O(p^2) simplex storage.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::NelderMeadOptions
      *>>   controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto
      *>>   value=dm::optim::NelderMead(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: NelderMead: initial_simplex_scale
      *>>   must be positive; NelderMead: reflection must be positive;
      *>>   NelderMead: expansion must be greater than 1; NelderMead:
      *>>   contraction must be in (0, 1); NelderMead: shrink must be in
      *>>   (0, 1); NelderMead: tolerance must be non-negative.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), NelderMeadOptions
       01 DM-NELDER-MEAD-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the NELDER-MEAD handle.
          05 DM-NELDER-MEAD-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
      *>>   Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output
      *>>   shapes.
          05 DM-NELDER-MEAD-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-NELDER-MEAD-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-NELDER-MEAD-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::NelderMead::options() const -> const
