      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   NESTEROV-ACCELERATED-GRADIENT

      *>> datamunge::optim::NesterovAcceleratedGradient::NesterovAcceleratedGradient(NesterovAcceleratedGradientOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> NESTEROV-ACCELERATED-GRADIENT handle
      *>> CALL "dm_nesterov_accelerated_gradient_new" USING
      *>>   DM-NESTEROV-ACCELERATED-GRADIENT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::NesterovAcceleratedGradient. Close
      *>>   the handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> NesterovAcceleratedGradient on the DifferentiableFunction
      *>>   callback interface.
      *>> Evaluates the gradient at coordinates+momentum*velocity, then
      *>>   updates velocity and coordinates. Tests that look-ahead
      *>>   gradient after the update. Fixed momentum and rate do not
      *>>   implement every strongly-convex acceleration schedule. O(p)
      *>>   reset local state.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::NesterovAcceleratedGradient optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - J. Nocedal and S. J. Wright (2006), Numerical Optimization,
      *>>   second edition, https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-387-40065-5.
      *>>   The implemented variant and stopping rules are specified
      *>>   above.
      *>>
      *>> See also: NesterovAcceleratedGradientOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::NesterovAcceleratedGradient optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-NESTEROV-ACCELERATED-GRADIENT-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-NESTEROV-ACCELERATED-GRADIENT-NEW-GIVEN USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (NesterovAcceleratedGradientOptions = {}):
      *>>   NESTEROV-ACCELERATED-GRADIENT-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   NesterovAcceleratedGradientOptions.
          05 DM-NESTEROV-ACCELERATED-GRADIENT-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: NESTEROV-ACCELERATED-GRADIENT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-NESTEROV-ACCELERATED-GRADIENT-NEW-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

