      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   NADAM

      *>> datamunge::optim::Nadam::Nadam(NadamOptions options = {}) ->
      *>>   NADAM handle
      *>> CALL "dm_nadam_new" USING DM-NADAM-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::Nadam. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Nadam on the DifferentiableFunction callback interface.
      *>> Fixed-beta Nadam variant: direction
      *>>   beta1*m/(1-beta1^t)+(1-beta1)*g/(1-beta1^t), divided by
      *>>   sqrt(v/(1-beta2^t))+epsilon. Does not implement scheduled
      *>>   momentum products. Tests the gradient used after updating;
      *>>   O(p) reset state.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::Nadam optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - T. Dozat (2016), Incorporating Nesterov Momentum into Adam,
      *>>   https://openreview.net/pdf?id=OM0jvwB8jIp57ZJjtNEZ
      *>>
      *>> See also: NadamOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::Nadam optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-NADAM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-NADAM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (NadamOptions = {}): NADAM-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   NadamOptions.
          05 DM-NADAM-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: NADAM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-NADAM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::Nadam::optimize(DifferentiableFunction &
      *>>   function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_nadam_optimize" USING DM-NADAM-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run Nadam from the supplied point using the configured finite
      *>>   budget.
      *>> Fixed-beta Nadam variant: direction
      *>>   beta1*m/(1-beta1^t)+(1-beta1)*g/(1-beta1^t), divided by
      *>>   sqrt(v/(1-beta2^t))+epsilon. Does not implement scheduled
      *>>   momentum products. Tests the gradient used after updating;
      *>>   O(p) reset state.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::NadamOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto value=dm::optim::Nadam(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: Nadam: step_size must be positive;
      *>>   Nadam: beta1 must be in [0, 1); Nadam: beta2 must be in [0,
      *>>   1); Nadam: epsilon must be positive; Nadam: tolerance must
      *>>   be non-negative.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), NadamOptions
       01 DM-NADAM-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the NADAM handle.
          05 DM-NADAM-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (DifferentiableFunction &): DIFFERENTIABLE-FUNCTION
      *>>   handle. Borrowed DifferentiableFunction with matching finite
      *>>   output shapes.
          05 DM-NADAM-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-NADAM-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-NADAM-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

