      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   PARALLEL-TEMPERING

      *>> datamunge::optim::ParallelTempering::ParallelTempering(ParallelTemperingOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> PARALLEL-TEMPERING handle
      *>> CALL "dm_parallel_tempering_new" USING
      *>>   DM-PARALLEL-TEMPERING-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::ParallelTempering. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Parallel tempering (replica exchange Monte Carlo): the
      *>>   population-based generalization
      *>> of SimulatedAnnealing. Runs num_replicas Metropolis chains
      *>>   simultaneously, each held at
      *>> its own fixed temperature on a geometric ladder, and
      *>>   periodically proposes swapping
      *>> adjacent-temperature replicas' states so hot chains help cold
      *>>   chains escape local
      *>> minima. Derivative-free, unconstrained, suitable for
      *>>   non-differentiable/black-box
      *>> objectives -- like SimulatedAnnealing, requires nothing beyond
      *>>   evaluate().
       01 DM-PARALLEL-TEMPERING-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-PARALLEL-TEMPERING-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (ParallelTemperingOptions = {}):
      *>>   PARALLEL-TEMPERING-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-PARALLEL-TEMPERING-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: PARALLEL-TEMPERING handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-PARALLEL-TEMPERING-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

