      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   PSO

      *>> datamunge::optim::PSO::PSO(PSOOptions options = {}) -> PSO
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_pso_new" USING DM-PSO-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::PSO. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> PSO on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface.
      *>> Box-constrained particle swarm with global or ring attraction
      *>>   and constant or linearly decayed inertia. Coordinates seed
      *>>   one clamped particle; returns the best visited feasible
      *>>   point. Stops after more than twenty small-best-improvement
      *>>   iterations or its budget. O(population_size*p) storage; no
      *>>   global-optimality certificate.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::PSO optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 1000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - J. Kennedy and R. Eberhart (1995), Particle Swarm
      *>>   Optimization, https://doi.org/10.1109/ICNN.1995.488968. This
      *>>   implementation adds the documented inertia, topology and
      *>>   clamping controls.
      *>>
      *>> See also: PSOOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::PSO optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 1000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-PSO-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-PSO-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (PSOOptions = {}): PSO-OPTIONS handle. Method-specific
      *>>   controls; defaults are listed by PSOOptions.
          05 DM-PSO-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: PSO handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-PSO-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::PSO::optimize(ArbitraryFunction & function,
      *>>   std::vector<double> & coordinates, const std::vector<double>
      *>>   & lower_bound, const std::vector<double> & upper_bound)
      *>>   const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_pso_optimize" USING DM-PSO-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run PSO from the supplied point using the configured finite
      *>>   budget.
      *>> Box-constrained particle swarm with global or ring attraction
      *>>   and constant or linearly decayed inertia. Coordinates seed
      *>>   one clamped particle; returns the best visited feasible
      *>>   point. Stops after more than twenty small-best-improvement
      *>>   iterations or its budget. O(population_size*p) storage; no
      *>>   global-optimality certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::PSOOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto
      *>>   value=dm::optim::PSO(controls).optimize(f,x,std::vector<double>{-3,-3},std::vector<double>{3,3});
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: PSO::optimize: population_size must
      *>>   be at least 2; PSO::optimize: topology must be 'global' or
      *>>   'ring'; PSO::optimize: inertia_strategy must be 'constant'
      *>>   or 'linear_decay'.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), PSOOptions
       01 DM-PSO-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the PSO handle.
          05 DM-PSO-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (ArbitraryFunction &): ARBITRARY-FUNCTION handle.
      *>>   Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output
      *>>   shapes.
          05 DM-PSO-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-PSO-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> lower_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Matching finite inclusive lower box limits.
          05 DM-PSO-OPTIMIZE-LOWER-BOUND USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> upper_bound (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Matching finite inclusive upper limits, greater than
      *>>   lower limits.
          05 DM-PSO-OPTIMIZE-UPPER-BOUND USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-PSO-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::PSO::options() const -> const PSOOptions &
      *>> CALL "dm_pso_options" USING DM-PSO-OPTIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
       01 DM-PSO-OPTIONS.
      *>> Self: the PSO handle.
          05 DM-PSO-OPTIONS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const PSOOptions &): PSO-OPTIONS handle (new; refers
      *>>   into its owner, which it keeps alive). Const option
      *>>   reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
          05 DM-PSO-OPTIONS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

