      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT

      *>> datamunge::optim::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent(RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescentOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT handle
      *>> CALL "dm_randomized_block_coordinate_descent_new" USING
      *>>   DM-RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent.
      *>>   Close the handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent on the DifferentiableFunction
      *>>   callback interface.
      *>> Randomly permutes coordinates each epoch and visits
      *>>   consecutive blocks once. Full-gradient block directions use
      *>>   Armijo backtracking and restore a failed block. This is
      *>>   random reshuffling, not independent coordinate draws. Stops
      *>>   on the full epoch-end gradient norm; O(p) local storage.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 1000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - S. J. Wright (2015), Coordinate descent algorithms,
      *>>   https://doi.org/10.1007/s10107-015-0892-3. This
      *>>   implementation uses the stated full-gradient
      *>>   coordinate/block steps.
      *>>
      *>> See also: RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescentOptions,
      *>>   trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 1000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-NEW-GIVEN USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescentOptions = {}):
      *>>   RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescentOptions.
          05 DM-RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT handle (new; close
      *>>   it).
          05 DM-RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-NEW-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent::optimize(DifferentiableFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const ->
      *>>   double
      *>> CALL "dm_randomized_block_coordinate_descent_optimize" USING
      *>>   DM-RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent from the supplied point
      *>>   using the configured finite budget.
      *>> Randomly permutes coordinates each epoch and visits
      *>>   consecutive blocks once. Full-gradient block directions use
      *>>   Armijo backtracking and restore a failed block. This is
      *>>   random reshuffling, not independent coordinate draws. Stops
      *>>   on the full epoch-end gradient norm; O(p) local storage.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescentOptions
      *>>   controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto
      *>>   value=dm::optim::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent:
      *>>   block_size must be positive;
      *>>   RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent: step_size must be
      *>>   positive; RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent: tolerance must
      *>>   be non-negative; RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent: armijo_c1
      *>>   must be in (0, 1); RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent:
      *>>   backtracking_factor must be in (0, 1).
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(),
      *>>   RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescentOptions
       01 DM-RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT handle.
          05 DM-RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (DifferentiableFunction &): DIFFERENTIABLE-FUNCTION
      *>>   handle. Borrowed DifferentiableFunction with matching finite
      *>>   output shapes.
          05 DM-RNDMZD-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-RNDMZD-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-RANDOMIZED-BLOCK-COORDINATE-DESCENT-OPTIMIZE-RESULT
              USAGE COMP-2.

