      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   RMS-PROP

      *>> datamunge::optim::RMSProp::RMSProp(RMSPropOptions options =
      *>>   {}) -> RMS-PROP handle
      *>> CALL "dm_rms_prop_new" USING DM-RMS-PROP-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::RMSProp. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> RMSProp on the DifferentiableFunction callback interface.
      *>> Uses an exponential squared-gradient average with decay_rate,
      *>>   dividing by sqrt(average)+epsilon. Tests the pre-update
      *>>   gradient norm after updating. Fixed rates can oscillate.
      *>>   O(p) local state, reset on every call.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::RMSProp optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - G. Hinton (2012), lecture 6e,
      *>>   https://www.cs.utoronto.ca/~hinton/coursera_lectures.html
      *>>
      *>> See also: RMSPropOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::RMSProp optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-RMS-PROP-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-RMS-PROP-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (RMSPropOptions = {}): RMS-PROP-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   RMSPropOptions.
          05 DM-RMS-PROP-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: RMS-PROP handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-RMS-PROP-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::RMSProp::optimize(DifferentiableFunction &
      *>>   function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_rms_prop_optimize" USING DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIMIZE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run RMSProp from the supplied point using the configured
      *>>   finite budget.
      *>> Uses an exponential squared-gradient average with decay_rate,
      *>>   dividing by sqrt(average)+epsilon. Tests the pre-update
      *>>   gradient norm after updating. Fixed rates can oscillate.
      *>>   O(p) local state, reset on every call.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::RMSPropOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto value=dm::optim::RMSProp(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: RMSProp: step_size must be positive;
      *>>   RMSProp: decay_rate must be in [0, 1); RMSProp: epsilon must
      *>>   be positive; RMSProp: tolerance must be non-negative.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), RMSPropOptions
       01 DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the RMS-PROP handle.
          05 DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (DifferentiableFunction &): DIFFERENTIABLE-FUNCTION
      *>>   handle. Borrowed DifferentiableFunction with matching finite
      *>>   output shapes.
          05 DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::RMSProp::options() const -> const
      *>>   RMSPropOptions &
      *>> CALL "dm_rms_prop_options" USING DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
       01 DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIONS.
      *>> Self: the RMS-PROP handle.
          05 DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIONS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const RMSPropOptions &): RMS-PROP-OPTIONS handle (new;
      *>>   refers into its owner, which it keeps alive). Const option
      *>>   reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
          05 DM-RMS-PROP-OPTIONS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

