      *>>   L^{-1}k_*\rVert^2`.
      *>>
      *>> The two-argument constructor keeps the original fixed setup:
      *>>   zero prior mean, unit signal
      *>> variance, no normalisation or fitting, expected improvement.
      *>>   The options constructor adds
      *>> value normalisation, marginal-likelihood fitting of the
      *>>   hyperparameters and other acquisitions.
      *>> The kernel is isotropic, so the inputs should be on comparable
      *>>   scales.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
