      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   SGD-OPTIONS

      *>> datamunge::optim::SGDOptions::SGDOptions() -> SGD-OPTIONS
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_sgd_options_new" USING DM-SGD-OPTIONS-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::SGDOptions. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Configuration for SGD; fields retain their documented native
      *>>   defaults.
      *>> Supply finite values in the supported ranges. Controls are
      *>>   copied at construction;
      *>> validation, stopping and loss scaling belong to optimize().
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::SGDOptions o;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",o.max_epochs); // 100
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: SGD
