      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   SGD

      *>> datamunge::optim::SGD::SGD(SGDOptions options = {}) -> SGD
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_sgd_new" USING DM-SGD-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::SGD. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SGD on the DifferentiableSeparableFunction callback interface.
      *>> Uses the mean gradient of each mini-batch, reshuffling
      *>>   component indices each epoch when enabled. Full objective
      *>>   remains the sum of components. Stops on absolute
      *>>   full-objective change per epoch. Nonempty components and
      *>>   positive batch_size are required; seeds reproduce the same
      *>>   build, not a cross-library shuffle transcript.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::SGD optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_epochs); // 100
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - H. Robbins and S. Monro (1951), A Stochastic Approximation
      *>>   Method, https://doi.org/10.1214/aoms/1177729586. The
      *>>   fixed-rate reshuffling variant here differs from their
      *>>   decreasing-step stochastic approximation.
      *>>
      *>> See also: SGDOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::SGD optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_epochs); // 100
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-SGD-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-SGD-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (SGDOptions = {}): SGD-OPTIONS handle. Method-specific
      *>>   controls; defaults are listed by SGDOptions.
          05 DM-SGD-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: SGD handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-SGD-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::SGD::optimize(DifferentiableSeparableFunction
      *>>   & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const ->
      *>>   double
      *>> CALL "dm_sgd_optimize" USING DM-SGD-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run SGD from the supplied point using the configured finite
      *>>   budget.
      *>> Uses the mean gradient of each mini-batch, reshuffling
      *>>   component indices each epoch when enabled. Full objective
      *>>   remains the sum of components. Stops on absolute
      *>>   full-objective change per epoch. Nonempty components and
      *>>   positive batch_size are required; seeds reproduce the same
      *>>   build, not a cross-library shuffle transcript.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::LeastSquaresObjective f({{1},{1}},{1,3});
      *>> dm::optim::SGDOptions controls;controls.max_epochs=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0};
      *>> const auto value=dm::optim::SGD(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: SGD: batch_size must be positive;
      *>>   SGD::optimize: function has zero terms.
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), SGDOptions
       01 DM-SGD-OPTIMIZE.
      *>> Self: the SGD handle.
          05 DM-SGD-OPTIMIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> function (DifferentiableSeparableFunction &):
      *>>   DIFFERENTIABLE-SEPARABLE-FUNCTION handle. Borrowed
      *>>   DifferentiableSeparableFunction with matching finite output
      *>>   shapes.
          05 DM-SGD-OPTIMIZE-FUNCTION USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> coordinates (std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native
      *>>   returned point.
          05 DM-SGD-OPTIMIZE-COORDINATES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. Objective at the native returned
      *>>   coordinates; not a stop-status code.
          05 DM-SGD-OPTIMIZE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::optim::SGD::options() const -> const SGDOptions &
      *>> CALL "dm_sgd_options" USING DM-SGD-OPTIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
       01 DM-SGD-OPTIONS.
      *>> Self: the SGD handle.
          05 DM-SGD-OPTIONS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const SGDOptions &): SGD-OPTIONS handle (new; refers
      *>>   into its owner, which it keeps alive). Const option
      *>>   reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
          05 DM-SGD-OPTIONS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

