      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   SIMULATED-ANNEALING

      *>> datamunge::optim::SimulatedAnnealing::SimulatedAnnealing(SimulatedAnnealingOptions
      *>>   options = {}) -> SIMULATED-ANNEALING handle
      *>> CALL "dm_simulated_annealing_new" USING
      *>>   DM-SIMULATED-ANNEALING-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::SimulatedAnnealing. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SimulatedAnnealing on the ArbitraryFunction callback
      *>>   interface.
      *>> Gaussian random-walk proposals with geometrically decaying
      *>>   temperature and Metropolis acceptance of worse values.
      *>>   Returns the best visited point, not the last accepted state.
      *>>   A finite cooling schedule does not certify a global optimum;
      *>>   O(p) storage.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::SimulatedAnnealing optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - S. Kirkpatrick, C. D. Gelatt and M. P. Vecchi (1983),
      *>>   Optimization by Simulated Annealing,
      *>>   https://doi.org/10.1126/science.220.4598.671. Finite
      *>>   geometric cooling here supplies no global guarantee.
      *>>
      *>> See also: SimulatedAnnealingOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::SimulatedAnnealing optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); //
      *>>   10000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-SIMULATED-ANNEALING-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-SIMULATED-ANNEALING-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.
      *>> options (SimulatedAnnealingOptions = {}):
      *>>   SIMULATED-ANNEALING-OPTIONS handle. Method-specific
      *>>   controls; defaults are listed by SimulatedAnnealingOptions.
          05 DM-SIMULATED-ANNEALING-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: SIMULATED-ANNEALING handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-SIMULATED-ANNEALING-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::SimulatedAnnealing::optimize(ArbitraryFunction
