      *>>   double
      *>> CALL "dm_simulated_annealing_optimize" USING
      *>>   DM-SIMULATED-ANNEALING-OPTIMIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Run SimulatedAnnealing from the supplied point using the
      *>>   configured finite budget.
      *>> Gaussian random-walk proposals with geometrically decaying
      *>>   temperature and Metropolis acceptance of worse values.
      *>>   Returns the best visited point, not the last accepted state.
      *>>   A finite cooling schedule does not certify a global optimum;
      *>>   O(p) storage.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
      *>> dm::optim::SimulatedAnnealingOptions
      *>>   controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
      *>> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
      *>> const auto
      *>>   value=dm::optim::SimulatedAnnealing(controls).optimize(f,x);
      *>> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::exception: Exceptions from supplied callbacks
      *>>   propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite
      *>>   inputs.
      *>>
      *>> See also: trace_optimize(), SimulatedAnnealingOptions
       01 DM-SIMULATED-ANNEALING-OPTIMIZE.
