      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   SVRG

      *>> datamunge::optim::SVRG::SVRG(SVRGOptions options = {}) -> SVRG
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_svrg_new" USING DM-SVRG-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::optim::SVRG. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SVRG on the DifferentiableSeparableFunction callback
      *>>   interface.
      *>> Uses mean component gradients:
      *>>   current_i-snapshot_i+full_snapshot_gradient/n. The division
      *>>   by n is essential for an unbiased mean-loss estimator and
      *>>   matches SGD/SAGA scale. Earlier code omitted it. Stops on
      *>>   absolute full-sum objective change per epoch. O(p) snapshot
      *>>   state, two component-gradient calls per inner update plus
      *>>   one full gradient per epoch.
      *>> The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
      *>>   callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
      *>> coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if
      *>>   a callback throws.
      *>> Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback
      *>>   exceptions; sharing a mutable
      *>> objective across threads requires external synchronisation.
      *>>   Normal return alone
      *>> is not a uniform convergence certificate.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::SVRG optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_epochs); // 100
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - R. Johnson and T. Zhang (2013), Accelerating Stochastic
      *>>   Gradient Descent using Predictive Variance Reduction,
      *>>   https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2013/hash/ac1dd209cbcc5e5d1c6e28598e8cbbe8-Abstract.html
      *>>
      *>> See also: SVRGOptions, trace_optimize()
      *>>
      *>> Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::optim::SVRG optimizer;
      *>> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_epochs); // 100
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: optimize()
       01 DM-SVRG-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-SVRG-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> options (SVRGOptions = {}): SVRG-OPTIONS handle.
      *>>   Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by
      *>>   SVRGOptions.
          05 DM-SVRG-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: SVRG handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-SVRG-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::optim::SVRG::optimize(DifferentiableSeparableFunction
