      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   HYPOTHESIS-TEST-RESULT

      *>> datamunge::stats::HypothesisTestResult::HypothesisTestResult()
      *>>   -> HYPOTHESIS-TEST-RESULT handle
      *>> CALL "dm_hypothesis_test_result_new" USING
      *>>   DM-HYPOTHESIS-TEST-RESULT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::stats::HypothesisTestResult. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Owned hypothesis-test result, analogous to R's htest list.
      *>> Each test documents which fields it populates and what its
      *>>   interval estimates.
      *>> Unused numeric fields retain zero; this default is storage,
      *>>   not a claim of zero effect.
      *>> Read bounds only when has_conf_int is true; one-sided
      *>>   intervals may be unbounded.
      *>> p_value is a null-model tail probability, not a posterior
      *>>   probability of the null.
      *>> Objects own their method string and contain no borrowed
      *>>   references or shared state.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto t=dm::stats::t_test_one_sample({1,2,3,4});
      *>> std::print("{}\n",t.has_conf_int); // true
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> -
      *>>   https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/t.test.html
      *>>
      *>> See also: Alternative, hypothesis_test_table()
       01 DM-HYPOTHESIS-TEST-RESULT-NEW.
      *>> Result: HYPOTHESIS-TEST-RESULT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-HYPOTHESIS-TEST-RESULT-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

