      *>> datamunge::stats::ARIMA::psi_weights(std::size_t count) const
      *>>   -> std::vector<double>
      *>> CALL "dm_arima_psi_weights" USING DM-ARIMA-PSI-WEIGHTS
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The first `count`
      *>>
      *>> `\psi`-weights of the full model, differencing included:
      *>> `y_t=\sum_{j\ge0}\psi_j\varepsilon_{t-j}` formally, with
      *>>   `\psi_0=1`.
      *>>
      *>> The h-step forecast error is
      *>>   `\sum_{j<h}\psi_j\varepsilon_{t+h-j}`, so its variance is
      *>> `\sigma^2\sum_{j<h}\psi_j^2`; forecast_with_intervals() uses
      *>>   exactly these weights.
      *>>
      *>> `\psi_0,\dots,\psi_{count-1}`.
       01 DM-ARIMA-PSI-WEIGHTS.
      *>> Self: the ARIMA handle.
          05 DM-ARIMA-PSI-WEIGHTS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> count (std::size_t): unsigned long. Number of weights.
          05 DM-ARIMA-PSI-WEIGHTS-COUNT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; close
      *>>   it).
          05 DM-ARIMA-PSI-WEIGHTS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

