      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING

      *>> datamunge::stats::ExponentialSmoothing::ExponentialSmoothing(const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & y, ExponentialSmoothingOptions options
      *>>   = {}) -> EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING handle
      *>> CALL "dm_exponential_smoothing_new" USING
      *>>   DM-EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::stats::ExponentialSmoothing. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Exponential smoothing (Holt-Winters family): simple
      *>>   exponential smoothing (no
      *>> trend, no seasonality), Holt linear trend (with optional
      *>>   damping), and seasonal
      *>> Holt-Winters (additive or multiplicative), unified under one
      *>>   class the way R's
      *>> HoltWinters() and statsmodels' ExponentialSmoothing() are --
      *>>   which components are
      *>> active is controlled entirely by
      *>>   ExponentialSmoothingOptions::trend/seasonal.
      *>>
      *>> Initial level/trend/seasonal-index states are set once from a
      *>>   simple classical
      *>> decomposition of the first one or two seasonal cycles and then
      *>>   held fixed; only
      *>> the smoothing parameters (alpha, beta, gamma, phi) are fit, by
      *>>   minimizing
      *>> one-step-ahead sum of squared errors with
      *>>   DifferentialEvolution.
       01 DM-EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 2 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 1.
      *>> y (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
          05 DM-EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING-NEW-Y USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> options (ExponentialSmoothingOptions = {}):
      *>>   EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING-OPTIONS handle.
          05 DM-EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING-NEW-OPTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-EXPONENTIAL-SMOOTHING-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::stats::ExponentialSmoothing::options() const ->
      *>>   const ExponentialSmoothingOptions &
