      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   BSPLINE

      *>> datamunge::Bspline::Bspline(double lower, double upper, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & knots, std::size_t degree = 3, bool
      *>>   intercept = false) -> BSPLINE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_bspline_new" USING DM-BSPLINE-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::Bspline. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> B-spline design factory, analogous to R's splines::bs().
      *>> Owns a clamped basis on fixed boundaries, reused for training
      *>>   and prediction.
      *>> By default the first basis column is omitted, so a formula's
      *>>   intercept does
      *>> not duplicate the partition of unity. No fitting or smoothing
      *>>   is performed.
      *>> Const evaluations are independent and safe to run
      *>>   concurrently.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::Bspline basis(0, 1, {0, 0.5, 1});
      *>> const auto design = basis.eval({0, 0.5, 1});
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n", design.rows(), design.cols()); // 3 4
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - C. de Boor (1972). "On calculating with B-splines". Journal
      *>>   of Approximation
      *>>   Theory 6(1), 50-62. doi:10.1016/0021-9045(72)90080-9.
      *>>
      *>> See also: bs(), fda::BSplineBasis, stats::LM
      *>>
      *>> Build a clamped basis from strictly increasing knot
      *>>   breakpoints.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::Bspline full(0, 1, {}, 1, true);
      *>> std::print("{:.1f}\n", full.eval({0.5})(0, 0)); // 0.5
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For invalid boundaries/knots or
      *>>   overflowing degree.
       01 DM-BSPLINE-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 3 to 5 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 3.
          05 DM-BSPLINE-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 3.
      *>> lower (double): double. Finite left boundary, strictly below
      *>>   upper.
          05 DM-BSPLINE-NEW-LOWER USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> upper (double): double. Finite right boundary.
          05 DM-BSPLINE-NEW-UPPER USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> knots (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Finite increasing breakpoints inside [lower, upper];
      *>>   boundary entries are optional and ignored when building
      *>>   interior knots. May be empty.
          05 DM-BSPLINE-NEW-KNOTS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> degree (std::size_t = 3): unsigned long. Polynomial degree,
      *>>   default 3 (cubic).
          05 DM-BSPLINE-NEW-DEGREE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> intercept (bool = false): 0 or 1. Include the first basis
      *>>   column, default false; use a no-intercept formula when true.
      *>>   Column count is interior knots + degree + (intercept ? 1 :
      *>>   0).
          05 DM-BSPLINE-NEW-INTERCEPT USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: BSPLINE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-BSPLINE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

