      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   CSV-READER

      *>> datamunge::CsvReader::CsvReader(const std::string & path, int
      *>>   batch_size = 1000, char delimiter = ',') -> CSV-READER
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_csv_reader_new" USING DM-CSV-READER-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::CsvReader. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly streaming CSV reader: returns a big file as
      *>>   DataFrames of at most
      *>> batch_size() rows each, so only one chunk is in memory at a
      *>>   time.
      *>>
      *>> Wraps datasets::CsvReader; column types are fixed from the
      *>>   first 1000 rows.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::CsvReader reader(dm::datasets::fetch("diamonds"), 10000);
      *>> while (reader.has_next()) {
      *>>   std::unique_ptr<dm::DataFrame> chunk(reader.next());
      *>>   // ... use chunk ...
      *>> }
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Opens `path` and infers its column types.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: if batch_size is not positive.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: if the file cannot be opened or is
      *>>   malformed.
       01 DM-CSV-READER-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> path (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. The CSV file.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-NEW-PATH PIC X(256).
          05 DM-CSV-READER-NEW-PATH-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> batch_size (int = 1000): int. Rows per chunk; must be
      *>>   positive.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-NEW-BATCH-SIZE USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> delimiter (char = ','): a character. The field separator.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-NEW-DELIMITER PIC X.
      *>> Result: CSV-READER handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-CSV-READER-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::CsvReader::has_next() -> bool
      *>> CALL "dm_csv_reader_has_next" USING DM-CSV-READER-HAS-NEXT
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> true while rows remain.
       01 DM-CSV-READER-HAS-NEXT.
      *>> Self: the CSV-READER handle.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-HAS-NEXT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (bool): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-HAS-NEXT-RESULT USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::CsvReader::next() -> DataFrame *
      *>> CALL "dm_csv_reader_next" USING DM-CSV-READER-NEXT DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The next chunk (caller owns it).
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: when no rows remain.
       01 DM-CSV-READER-NEXT.
      *>> Self: the CSV-READER handle.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-NEXT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (DataFrame *): DATA-FRAME handle (new; refers into its
      *>>   owner, which it keeps alive).
          05 DM-CSV-READER-NEXT-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::CsvReader::reset() -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_csv_reader_reset" USING DM-CSV-READER-RESET DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Rewinds to the first data row.
       01 DM-CSV-READER-RESET.
      *>> Self: the CSV-READER handle.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-RESET-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::CsvReader::batch_size() const -> int
      *>> CALL "dm_csv_reader_batch_size" USING DM-CSV-READER-BATCH-SIZE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Rows per chunk.
       01 DM-CSV-READER-BATCH-SIZE.
      *>> Self: the CSV-READER handle.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-BATCH-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (int): int.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-BATCH-SIZE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::CsvReader::set_batch_size(int rows) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_csv_reader_set_batch_size" USING
      *>>   DM-CSV-READER-SET-BATCH-SIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Changes the rows per chunk.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: if `rows` is not positive.
       01 DM-CSV-READER-SET-BATCH-SIZE.
      *>> Self: the CSV-READER handle.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-SET-BATCH-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> rows (int): int.
          05 DM-CSV-READER-SET-BATCH-SIZE-ROWS USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::CsvReader::column_names() const ->
      *>>   std::vector<std::string>
