      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   GG-PLOT

      *>> datamunge::GGPlot::GGPlot(const DataFrame & data, const
      *>>   std::string & x_column, const std::string & y_column = "",
      *>>   const std::string & color_column = "", const std::string &
      *>>   fill_column = "", const std::string & group_column = "") ->
      *>>   GG-PLOT handle
      *>> CALL "dm_gg_plot_new" USING DM-GG-PLOT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::GGPlot. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::graphics::GGPlot — a
      *>>   ggplot2-style grammar-of-graphics
      *>> builder. Geom/theme/scale/facet calls are chainable, mirroring
      *>>   ggplot2's own layered
      *>> `ggplot(df, aes(...)) + geom_point() + ...` style as closely
      *>>   as C++ method chaining allows.
       01 DM-GG-PLOT-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 6 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-GG-PLOT-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-GG-PLOT-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> x_column (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-GG-PLOT-NEW-X-COLUMN PIC X(256).
          05 DM-GG-PLOT-NEW-X-COLUMN-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> y_column (const std::string & = ""): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-GG-PLOT-NEW-Y-COLUMN PIC X(256).
          05 DM-GG-PLOT-NEW-Y-COLUMN-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
