      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   SPLOM

      *>> datamunge::Splom::Splom(const DataFrame & data, const
      *>>   std::vector<std::string> & columns = {}) -> SPLOM handle
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_new" USING DM-SPLOM-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::Splom. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A scatterplot matrix (R's `pairs()`, GGally's `ggpairs()`)
      *>>   over the columns of a
      *>> data frame, with chainable setters; the SWIG-friendly facade
      *>>   for graphics::Splom.
      *>>
      *>> Panel (row i, column j) puts variable j on x and variable i on
      *>>   y. The panel type follows
      *>> the two variables' kinds (numeric columns are quantitative,
      *>>   string columns categorical):
      *>> - diagonal: kernel density curves, one per group_by() group
      *>>   (numeric), or a stacked bar of
      *>>   level counts (string), titled with the variable name;
      *>> - numeric vs numeric above the diagonal: the points with a
      *>>   local linear smooth of the mean and
      *>>   a 95% prediction band, one per group; point colors follow
      *>>     set_col() or group_by();
      *>> - numeric vs numeric below the diagonal: bivariate kernel
      *>>   density contours, one set per group;
      *>> - string vs numeric: one violin per level with the median and
      *>>   interquartile range marked;
      *>> - string vs string: a mosaic shaded by chi-squared Pearson
      *>>   residuals, with its p-value.
      *>>
      *>> Values are copied at construction, so the frame need not
      *>>   outlive the matrix. Rows with a
      *>> missing value in either variable are dropped from that panel
      *>>   only. Setters return
      *>> `Splom&` for chaining; nothing is drawn until to_svg(),
      *>>   save(), or show(). The default
      *>> figure is 960 by 960 pixels with blue `{37, 99, 235}` points
      *>>   of radius 2.5.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto iris = dm::datasets::iris();
      *>> const auto species =
      *>>   dm::factor(dm::c(iris.get_column<std::string>("Species").values()));
      *>> const auto palette = dm::c(dm::RGB{255, 255, 80}, dm::RGB{100,
      *>>   255, 255},
      *>>                            dm::RGB{220, 100, 255});
      *>> auto pairs = dm::Splom(iris).set_title("Iris
      *>>   Pairs").set_col(species, palette);
      *>> pairs.show(); // or pairs.save("iris_pairs.svg") without a
      *>>   display
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: dm::splom(), dm::Plot, graphics::Splom
      *>>
      *>> Builds the matrix from a facade DataFrame (the overload SWIG
      *>>   bindings use).
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For a missing column, or fewer than
      *>>   two variables.
      *>>
      *>> See also: Splom(const dstruct::DataFrame&, const
      *>>   std::vector<std::string>&)
       01 DM-SPLOM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 2 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-SPLOM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle. Source frame; its
      *>>   values are copied.
          05 DM-SPLOM-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> columns (const std::vector<std::string> & = {}): VECTOR-STRING
      *>>   handle. Columns to include in order; empty selects every
      *>>   numeric column plus every string column with at most
      *>>   graphics::Splom::max_default_levels distinct values.
          05 DM-SPLOM-NEW-COLUMNS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: SPLOM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-SPLOM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::set_col(datamunge::graphics::RGB color) ->
      *>>   Splom &
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_set_col" USING DM-SPLOM-SET-COL DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Sets one color for every scatter point; same as color().
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto pairs =
      *>>   dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).set_col(dm::RGBA{220, 38,
      *>>   38, 0.5});
      *>> ```
       01 DM-SPLOM-SET-COL.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SET-COL-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> color (datamunge::graphics::RGB): RGB handle. Point color,
      *>>   alpha included; also used for bars without grouping.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SET-COL-COLOR USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (Splom &): SPLOM handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This matrix, for chaining.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SET-COL-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::set_title(const std::string & value) ->
      *>>   Splom &
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_set_title" USING DM-SPLOM-SET-TITLE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Same as title(), matching the `set_*` style of dm::Plot.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto pairs = dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).set_title("Iris
      *>>   Pairs");
      *>> ```
       01 DM-SPLOM-SET-TITLE.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SET-TITLE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Figure heading; empty removes the
      *>>   heading band.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SET-TITLE-VALUE PIC X(256).
          05 DM-SPLOM-SET-TITLE-VALUE-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> Result (Splom &): SPLOM handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This matrix, for chaining.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SET-TITLE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::title(const std::string & value) -> Splom &
