      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If either dimension is zero.
       01 DM-SPLOM-SIZE.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> width (std::size_t): unsigned long. Figure width in pixels.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SIZE-WIDTH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> height (std::size_t): unsigned long. Figure height in pixels.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SIZE-HEIGHT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (Splom &): SPLOM handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This matrix, for chaining.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SIZE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::color(datamunge::graphics::RGB value) ->
      *>>   Splom &
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_color" USING DM-SPLOM-COLOR DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Uses one color for all points and clears any grouping.
      *>>
      *>> Clears group_by(), point_colors(), and the factor form of
      *>>   set_col().
      *>>
      *>> See also: set_col(datamunge::graphics::RGB)
       01 DM-SPLOM-COLOR.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-COLOR-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (datamunge::graphics::RGB): RGB handle. Point color
      *>>   (default `{37, 99, 235}`).
          05 DM-SPLOM-COLOR-VALUE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (Splom &): SPLOM handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This matrix, for chaining.
          05 DM-SPLOM-COLOR-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::group_by(const std::string & column, const
      *>>   std::vector<datamunge::graphics::RGB> & palette = {}) ->
      *>>   Splom &
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_group_by" USING DM-SPLOM-GROUP-BY DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Splits every numeric panel by the groups of string column
      *>>   `column` (GGally's
      *>> `ggpairs(aes(colour = group))`); an empty palette uses the
      *>>   default level palette.
      *>>
      *>> The column need not be a panel variable but must be a string
      *>>   column of the source
      *>> frame. Groups are its sorted distinct non-missing values, and
      *>>   group k takes
      *>> `palette[k % palette.size()]`. Each group gets its own points,
      *>>   diagonal density, smooth
      *>> and prediction band, and density contours; rows with a missing
      *>>   group are left out of
      *>> those panels. When the column is also a panel variable its
      *>>   violins, bars, and mosaic axis
      *>> share the colors. Pass "" to clear the grouping. Clears
      *>>   point_colors().
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto pairs =
      *>>   dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).group_by("Species");
      *>> std::print("{}\n", pairs.groups()); // ["setosa",
      *>>   "versicolor", "virginica"]
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If `column` is not a string column of
      *>>   the source frame.
      *>>
      *>> See also: groups(), set_col()
       01 DM-SPLOM-GROUP-BY.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-GROUP-BY-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 2 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-SPLOM-GROUP-BY-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> column (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. String column to group by, or "" to
      *>>   clear.
          05 DM-SPLOM-GROUP-BY-COLUMN PIC X(256).
          05 DM-SPLOM-GROUP-BY-COLUMN-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> palette (const std::vector<datamunge::graphics::RGB> & = {}):
      *>>   VECTOR-RGB handle. Group colors in sorted-group order; empty
      *>>   uses the default.
          05 DM-SPLOM-GROUP-BY-PALETTE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (Splom &): SPLOM handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This matrix, for chaining.
          05 DM-SPLOM-GROUP-BY-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::point_colors(const
      *>>   std::vector<datamunge::graphics::RGB> & colors) -> Splom &
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_point_colors" USING DM-SPLOM-POINT-COLORS
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Sets one color per data row for the points (recycled); clears
      *>>   group_by().
      *>>
      *>> Same as set_col(const Vector<RGB>&) for callers holding a
      *>>   std::vector; an empty vector
      *>> restores the single color().
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto pairs = dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris())
      *>>                  .point_colors({dm::RGB{0, 0, 0}, dm::RGB{255,
      *>>                    0, 0}}); // alternate rows
      *>> ```
       01 DM-SPLOM-POINT-COLORS.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-POINT-COLORS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> colors (const std::vector<datamunge::graphics::RGB> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-RGB handle. Per-row colors, recycled when shorter
      *>>   than the frame.
          05 DM-SPLOM-POINT-COLORS-COLORS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (Splom &): SPLOM handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This matrix, for chaining.
          05 DM-SPLOM-POINT-COLORS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::level_palette(const
