      *>> datamunge::Splom::span(double value) -> Splom &
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_span" USING DM-SPLOM-SPAN DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Sets the fraction of each group's points used in each local
      *>>   fit of the smooths
      *>> above the diagonal (R's `loess(span =)`, default 0.75).
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto pairs =
      *>>   dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).group_by("Species").span(0.5).prediction_level(0.9);
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If `value` is not in (0, 1].
       01 DM-SPLOM-SPAN.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SPAN-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (double): double. Span in (0, 1]; smaller values follow
      *>>   the data more closely.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SPAN-VALUE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result (Splom &): SPLOM handle (new; refers into its owner,
      *>>   which it keeps alive). This matrix, for chaining.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SPAN-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

