      *>> datamunge::Splom::panel(std::size_t row, std::size_t col)
      *>>   const -> datamunge::graphics::RPlot
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_panel" USING DM-SPLOM-PANEL DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Builds the panel with variable `col` on x and variable `row`
      *>>   on y.
      *>>
      *>> The panel is a standalone dm::Plot sized to one grid cell,
      *>>   useful for inspecting or
      *>> saving a single pair. Indices are zero-based positions in
      *>>   variables().
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto pairs = dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris(),
      *>>   {"Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width"});
      *>> pairs.panel(1, 0).save("sepal_scatter.svg"); // Sepal.Length
      *>>   on x, Sepal.Width on y
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: If either index is not below
      *>>   variables().size().
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the panel has no complete rows to
      *>>   draw.
       01 DM-SPLOM-PANEL.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-PANEL-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> row (std::size_t): unsigned long. Zero-based index of the y
      *>>   variable.
          05 DM-SPLOM-PANEL-ROW USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> col (std::size_t): unsigned long. Zero-based index of the x
      *>>   variable; equal to `row` gives the diagonal panel.
          05 DM-SPLOM-PANEL-COL USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (datamunge::graphics::RPlot): R-PLOT handle (new; close
      *>>   it). The rendered-on-demand panel plot.
          05 DM-SPLOM-PANEL-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::to_svg() const -> std::string
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_to_svg" USING DM-SPLOM-TO-SVG DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Renders the matrix as a standalone SVG document and returns it
      *>>   as a string.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto svg =
      *>>   dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).set_title("Iris
      *>>   Pairs").to_svg();
      *>> std::print("{}\n", svg.contains("Iris Pairs")); // true
      *>> ```
       01 DM-SPLOM-TO-SVG.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-TO-SVG-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::string): text in PIC X(16384); -LENGTH is its
      *>>   length in bytes. The complete SVG text of the full grid,
      *>>   including the title band.
          05 DM-SPLOM-TO-SVG-RESULT PIC X(16384).
          05 DM-SPLOM-TO-SVG-RESULT-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::save(const std::string & path) const -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_save" USING DM-SPLOM-SAVE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Writes the matrix to `path`, choosing the format from the
      *>>   extension.
      *>>
      *>> `.svg` or no extension writes to_svg(); `.png` and `.pdf`
      *>>   write the tiled raster the
      *>> viewer shows. Needs no display.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const auto pairs =
      *>>   dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).group_by("Species");
      *>> pairs.save("iris_pairs.svg");
      *>> pairs.save("iris_pairs.png");
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: For any other extension.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the file cannot be written.
       01 DM-SPLOM-SAVE.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SAVE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> path (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Destination file; an existing file is
      *>>   overwritten.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SAVE-PATH PIC X(256).
          05 DM-SPLOM-SAVE-PATH-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::save_svg(const std::string & path) const ->
      *>>   void
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_save_svg" USING DM-SPLOM-SAVE-SVG DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Writes to_svg() to `path` regardless of its extension.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the file cannot be opened for
      *>>   writing.
       01 DM-SPLOM-SAVE-SVG.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SAVE-SVG-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> path (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Destination file; an existing file is
      *>>   overwritten.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SAVE-SVG-PATH PIC X(256).
          05 DM-SPLOM-SAVE-SVG-PATH-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.

      *>> datamunge::Splom::show(const std::string & title_hint = "")
      *>>   const -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_splom_show" USING DM-SPLOM-SHOW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Opens the matrix in the interactive X11 viewer and blocks
      *>>   until the window closes.
      *>>
      *>> Zoom and pan act on every panel at once; q or Escape closes
      *>>   the window. Requires an
      *>> X11-enabled build and a reachable display; use save() in
      *>>   headless code.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).set_title("Iris
      *>>   Pairs").group_by("Species").show();
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If X11 is unavailable or the display
      *>>   cannot be opened.
       01 DM-SPLOM-SHOW.
      *>> Self: the SPLOM handle.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SHOW-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-SPLOM-SHOW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> title_hint (const std::string & = ""): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. Window title; empty uses
      *>>   the figure title, or "datamunge splom".
          05 DM-SPLOM-SHOW-TITLE-HINT PIC X(256).
          05 DM-SPLOM-SHOW-TITLE-HINT-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.

      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   LM

      *>> datamunge::LM::LM(const DataFrame & data, const std::string &
      *>>   formula, const std::string & weights_column = "") -> LM
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_lm_new" USING DM-LM-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::LM. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::LM —
      *>>   R-`lm()`-style linear models fit from a DataFrame.
       01 DM-LM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-LM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-LM-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-LM-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-LM-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> weights_column (const std::string & = ""): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. Optional column name
      *>>   enabling weighted least squares; pass "" (the default) for
      *>>   OLS.
          05 DM-LM-NEW-WEIGHTS-COLUMN PIC X(256).
          05 DM-LM-NEW-WEIGHTS-COLUMN-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> Result: LM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-LM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

