          05 DM-LM-PRINT-SUMMARY-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::LM::predict(const DataFrame & newdata) const ->
      *>>   std::vector<double>
      *>> CALL "dm_lm_predict" USING DM-LM-PREDICT DM-STATUS
       01 DM-LM-PREDICT.
      *>> Self: the LM handle.
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> newdata (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-NEWDATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; close
      *>>   it).
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::LM::predict_frame(const DataFrame & newdata, const
      *>>   std::string & interval_kind = "none", double level =
      *>>   0.94999999999999996) const -> DataFrame *
      *>> CALL "dm_lm_predict_frame" USING DM-LM-PREDICT-FRAME DM-STATUS
       01 DM-LM-PREDICT-FRAME.
      *>> Self: the LM handle.
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-FRAME-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-FRAME-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> newdata (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-FRAME-NEWDATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> interval_kind (const std::string & = "none"): text in PIC
      *>>   X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. One of "none",
      *>>   "confidence", "prediction". Returned DataFrame has a "fit"
      *>>   column, plus "se_fit"/"lwr"/"upr" when an interval is
      *>>   requested.
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-FRAME-INTERVAL-KIND PIC X(256).
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-FRAME-INTERVAL-KIND-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> level (double = 0.94999999999999996): double.
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-FRAME-LEVEL USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result (DataFrame *): DATA-FRAME handle (new; refers into its
      *>>   owner, which it keeps alive).
          05 DM-LM-PREDICT-FRAME-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

