      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   LMM

      *>> datamunge::LMM::LMM(const DataFrame & data, const std::string
      *>>   & formula, bool reml = true, std::size_t de_population_size
      *>>   = 40, std::size_t de_max_generations = 300, double
      *>>   theta_bound = 5.0, std::size_t seed = 42) -> LMM handle
      *>> CALL "dm_lmm_new" USING DM-LMM-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::LMM. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::LMM — a linear
      *>>   mixed model fit by
      *>> (RE)ML, with a single grouping factor, e.g. "score ~ x1 + (1 +
      *>>   x1 | school)".
       01 DM-LMM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 7 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> reml (bool = true): 0 or 1. REML (default) or maximum
      *>>   likelihood.
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-REML USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> de_population_size (std::size_t = 40): unsigned long.
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-DE-POPULATION-SIZE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> de_max_generations (std::size_t = 300): unsigned long.
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-DE-MAX-GENERATIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> theta_bound (double = 5.0): double. Box-constraint magnitude
      *>>   (relative to the residual SD) for the DifferentialEvolution
      *>>   search over variance-component parameters.
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-THETA-BOUND USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> seed (std::size_t = 42): unsigned long.
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-SEED USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: LMM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-LMM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::LMM::formula_text() const -> std::string
      *>> CALL "dm_lmm_formula_text" USING DM-LMM-FORMULA-TEXT DM-STATUS
       01 DM-LMM-FORMULA-TEXT.
      *>> Self: the LMM handle.
          05 DM-LMM-FORMULA-TEXT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::string): text in PIC X(16384); -LENGTH is its
      *>>   length in bytes.
          05 DM-LMM-FORMULA-TEXT-RESULT PIC X(16384).
          05 DM-LMM-FORMULA-TEXT-RESULT-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 0.

