      *>> datamunge::GLMM::GLMM(const DataFrame & data, const
      *>>   std::string & formula, const std::string & family =
      *>>   "binomial", std::size_t max_iterations = 20, double tol =
      *>>   9.9999999999999995E-7, std::size_t de_population_size = 30,
      *>>   std::size_t de_max_generations = 150, double theta_bound =
      *>>   5.0, std::size_t seed = 42) -> GLMM handle
      *>> CALL "dm_glmm_new" USING DM-GLMM-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::GLMM. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::GLMM — a
      *>>   generalized linear mixed model
      *>> fit by penalized quasi-likelihood, with a single grouping
      *>>   factor, e.g.
      *>> "success ~ x1 + (1 | school)" with family="binomial".
       01 DM-GLMM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 9 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> family (const std::string & = "binomial"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. One of "binomial" (logit
      *>>   link) or "poisson" (log link).
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-FAMILY PIC X(256).
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-FAMILY-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> max_iterations (std::size_t = 20): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-MAX-ITERATIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> tol (double = 9.9999999999999995E-7): double.
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-TOL USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> de_population_size (std::size_t = 30): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-DE-POPULATION-SIZE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> de_max_generations (std::size_t = 150): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-DE-MAX-GENERATIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> theta_bound (double = 5.0): double.
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-THETA-BOUND USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> seed (std::size_t = 42): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-SEED USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: GLMM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-GLMM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

