      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   INLA-MIXED-MODEL

      *>> datamunge::INLAMixedModel::INLAMixedModel(const DataFrame &
      *>>   data, const std::string & formula, const std::string &
      *>>   family = "gaussian", const std::string & strategy = "grid",
      *>>   double fixed_effect_prior_sd = 1000.0, std::size_t
      *>>   grid_points_per_dim = 7, double grid_span = 4.0, std::size_t
      *>>   mode_population_size = 40, std::size_t mode_max_generations
      *>>   = 200, std::size_t seed = 42) -> INLA-MIXED-MODEL handle
      *>> CALL "dm_inla_mixed_model_new" USING DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::INLAMixedModel. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::INLAMixedModel —
      *>>   a mixed model (same
      *>> formula grammar as GLMM/LMM) fit by Integrated Nested Laplace
      *>>   Approximation instead
      *>> of penalized quasi-likelihood/REML: a genuinely Bayesian
      *>>   alternative returning real
      *>> posterior means/sds (including for the variance components)
      *>>   rather than point
      *>> estimates + asymptotic standard errors. See
      *>>   datamunge::bayes::INLA (C++-only, not
      *>> exposed to bindings -- same reasoning as AutodiffModel) for
      *>>   the underlying algorithm.
       01 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 10 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> family (const std::string & = "gaussian"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. One of "gaussian"
      *>>   (identity link), "binomial" (logit link), or "poisson" (log
      *>>   link).
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-FAMILY PIC X(256).
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-FAMILY-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> strategy (const std::string & = "grid"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. One of "grid" (integrate
      *>>   over hyperparameter uncertainty) or "eb" (empirical Bayes:
      *>>   fix hyperparameters at their posterior mode).
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-STRATEGY PIC X(256).
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-STRATEGY-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> fixed_effect_prior_sd (double = 1000.0): double.
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-FIXED-EFFECT-PRIOR-SD USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> grid_points_per_dim (std::size_t = 7): unsigned long.
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-GRID-POINTS-PER-DIM USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> grid_span (double = 4.0): double.
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-GRID-SPAN USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> mode_population_size (std::size_t = 40): unsigned long.
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-MODE-POPULATION-SIZE USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> mode_max_generations (std::size_t = 200): unsigned long.
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-MODE-MAX-GENERATIONS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> seed (std::size_t = 42): unsigned long.
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-SEED USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: INLA-MIXED-MODEL handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-INLA-MIXED-MODEL-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

