      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   SVM

      *>> datamunge::SVM::SVM(const DataFrame & data, const std::string
      *>>   & formula, const std::string & kernel = "radial", double
      *>>   cost = 1.0, double gamma = -1.0, double coef0 = 0.0, int
      *>>   degree = 3, bool scale = true) -> SVM handle
      *>> CALL "dm_svm_new" USING DM-SVM-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::SVM. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::SVM —
      *>>   R-`e1071::svm()`-style multi-class SVM classification.
       01 DM-SVM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 8 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> kernel (const std::string & = "radial"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. One of "linear",
      *>>   "polynomial", "radial" (default), "sigmoid".
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-KERNEL PIC X(256).
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-KERNEL-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> cost (double = 1.0): double.
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-COST USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> gamma (double = -1.0): double. <= 0 means "auto" = 1 / number
      *>>   of predictors.
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-GAMMA USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> coef0 (double = 0.0): double.
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-COEF0 USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> degree (int = 3): int.
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-DEGREE USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> scale (bool = true): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-SCALE USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: SVM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-SVM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

