      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER

      *>> datamunge::RandomForestClassifier::RandomForestClassifier(const
      *>>   DataFrame & data, const std::string & formula, std::size_t
      *>>   n_trees = 100, std::size_t max_depth = 10, std::size_t
      *>>   min_samples_split = 2, std::size_t min_samples_leaf = 1,
      *>>   std::size_t max_features = 0, const std::string & criterion
      *>>   = "gini", bool bootstrap = true, double sample_fraction =
      *>>   1.0, std::uint64_t seed = 42) -> RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_random_forest_classifier_new" USING
      *>>   DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::RandomForestClassifier. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for
      *>>   datamunge::stats::RandomForestClassifier — a bagged
      *>>   ensemble of CART trees,
      *>> each fit on a bootstrap sample with a random subset of
      *>>   predictors considered at every split.
       01 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 11 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> n_trees (std::size_t = 100): unsigned long.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-N-TREES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> max_depth (std::size_t = 10): unsigned long.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-MAX-DEPTH USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> min_samples_split (std::size_t = 2): unsigned long.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-MIN-SAMPLES-SPLIT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> min_samples_leaf (std::size_t = 1): unsigned long.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-MIN-SAMPLES-LEAF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> max_features (std::size_t = 0): unsigned long. 0 = auto
      *>>   (floor(sqrt(number of predictors))).
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-MAX-FEATURES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> criterion (const std::string & = "gini"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. "gini" (default) or
      *>>   "entropy".
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-CRITERION PIC X(256).
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-CRITERION-LENGTH USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> bootstrap (bool = true): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-BOOTSTRAP USAGE BINARY-CHAR
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> sample_fraction (double = 1.0): double.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-SAMPLE-FRACTION USAGE
              COMP-2.
      *>> seed (std::uint64_t = 42): unsigned long.
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-SEED USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::RandomForestClassifier::classes() const ->
      *>>   std::vector<std::string>
      *>> CALL "dm_random_forest_classifier_classes" USING
      *>>   DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-CLASSES DM-STATUS
       01 DM-RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER-CLASSES.
      *>> Self: the RANDOM-FOREST-CLASSIFIER handle.
