      *>> datamunge::ElasticNet::ElasticNet(const DataFrame & data,
      *>>   const std::string & formula, double alpha = 0.5, double
      *>>   lambda = -1.0, std::size_t n_lambda = 100, std::size_t
      *>>   cv_folds = 5, bool standardize = true, std::uint64_t seed =
      *>>   42) -> ELASTIC-NET handle
      *>> CALL "dm_elastic_net_new" USING DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::ElasticNet. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::ElasticNet —
      *>>   regularized linear regression fit by
      *>> coordinate descent (alpha=0 is ridge, alpha=1 is lasso); see
      *>>   also the Ridge and Lasso convenience
      *>> facades below.
       01 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 8 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> alpha (double = 0.5): double. L1/L2 mixing: 0 = ridge, 1 =
      *>>   lasso, in between = elastic net.
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-ALPHA USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> lambda (double = -1.0): double. Regularization strength; pass
      *>>   a negative value (the default) to select it automatically
      *>>   via cross-validation.
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-LAMBDA USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> n_lambda (std::size_t = 100): unsigned long.
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-N-LAMBDA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> cv_folds (std::size_t = 5): unsigned long.
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-CV-FOLDS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> standardize (bool = true): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-STANDARDIZE USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> seed (std::uint64_t = 42): unsigned long.
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-SEED USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: ELASTIC-NET handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-ELASTIC-NET-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

