      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   LASSO

      *>> datamunge::Lasso::Lasso(const DataFrame & data, const
      *>>   std::string & formula, double lambda = -1.0, std::size_t
      *>>   n_lambda = 100, std::size_t cv_folds = 5, bool standardize =
      *>>   true, std::uint64_t seed = 42) -> LASSO handle
      *>> CALL "dm_lasso_new" USING DM-LASSO-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::Lasso. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::Lasso — pure
      *>>   L1-penalized ("lasso") regression, a special
      *>> case of ElasticNet with alpha fixed to 1. Can shrink
      *>>   coefficients exactly to zero, performing
      *>> variable selection.
       01 DM-LASSO-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 7 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-LASSO-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-LASSO-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-LASSO-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-LASSO-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> lambda (double = -1.0): double.
          05 DM-LASSO-NEW-LAMBDA USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> n_lambda (std::size_t = 100): unsigned long.
          05 DM-LASSO-NEW-N-LAMBDA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> cv_folds (std::size_t = 5): unsigned long.
          05 DM-LASSO-NEW-CV-FOLDS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> standardize (bool = true): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-LASSO-NEW-STANDARDIZE USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> seed (std::uint64_t = 42): unsigned long.
          05 DM-LASSO-NEW-SEED USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: LASSO handle (new; close it).
