      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   PCA

      *>> datamunge::PCA::PCA(const DataFrame & data, const
      *>>   std::vector<std::string> & feature_columns, bool center =
      *>>   true, bool scale = true) -> PCA handle
      *>> CALL "dm_pca_new" USING DM-PCA-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::PCA. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::PCA — principal
      *>>   component analysis fit
      *>> from a DataFrame and a list of numeric feature columns via
      *>>   eigendecomposition of the
      *>> correlation (default) or covariance matrix.
       01 DM-PCA-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-PCA-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-PCA-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> feature_columns (const std::vector<std::string> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-STRING handle.
          05 DM-PCA-NEW-FEATURE-COLUMNS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> center (bool = true): 0 or 1. Mean-center each feature before
      *>>   fitting; almost always left true.
          05 DM-PCA-NEW-CENTER USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> scale (bool = true): 0 or 1. Standardize each feature to unit
      *>>   variance before fitting (i.e. fit on the correlation matrix
      *>>   rather than the covariance matrix); recommended whenever
      *>>   features are on different scales, and the default here.
          05 DM-PCA-NEW-SCALE USAGE BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: PCA handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-PCA-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::PCA::PCA(const DataFrame & data, const std::string
      *>>   & encoded_feature_columns, bool center = true, bool scale =
      *>>   true) -> PCA handle
      *>> CALL "dm_pca_new_data_frame_string_bool_bool" USING
      *>>   DM-PCA-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-BOOL-BOOL DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::PCA. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::PCA — principal
      *>>   component analysis fit
      *>> from a DataFrame and a list of numeric feature columns via
      *>>   eigendecomposition of the
      *>> correlation (default) or covariance matrix.
      *>>
      *>> Same as the vector<string> constructor, but feature_columns is
      *>>   a single "<count>
      *>> col1..."-encoded string -- see KMeans's encoded constructor
      *>>   for why.
       01 DM-PCA-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-BOOL-BOOL.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-PCA-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-BOOL-BOOL-GIVEN USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-PCA-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-BOOL-BOOL-DATA USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> encoded_feature_columns (const std::string &): text in PIC
      *>>   X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces.
