      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   MDS

      *>> datamunge::MDS::MDS(const DataFrame & data, const
      *>>   std::vector<std::string> & feature_columns, std::size_t
      *>>   n_components = 2, const std::string & metric = "euclidean")
      *>>   -> MDS handle
      *>> CALL "dm_mds_new" USING DM-MDS-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::MDS. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::MDS — classical
      *>>   (metric/Torgerson)
      *>> multidimensional scaling fit from a DataFrame and a list of
      *>>   numeric feature columns:
      *>> embeds the rows in a low-dimensional space that best
      *>>   reproduces their original
      *>> pairwise distances.
       01 DM-MDS-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> feature_columns (const std::vector<std::string> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-STRING handle.
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-FEATURE-COLUMNS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> n_components (std::size_t = 2): unsigned long.
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-N-COMPONENTS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> metric (const std::string & = "euclidean"): text in PIC
      *>>   X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. One of "euclidean"
      *>>   (default) or "manhattan".
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-METRIC PIC X(256).
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-METRIC-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> Result: MDS handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::MDS::MDS(const DataFrame & data, const std::string
      *>>   & encoded_feature_columns, std::size_t n_components = 2,
      *>>   const std::string & metric = "euclidean") -> MDS handle
      *>> CALL "dm_mds_new_data_frame_string_ulong_string" USING
      *>>   DM-MDS-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-ULONG-STRING DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::MDS. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::MDS — classical
      *>>   (metric/Torgerson)
      *>> multidimensional scaling fit from a DataFrame and a list of
      *>>   numeric feature columns:
      *>> embeds the rows in a low-dimensional space that best
      *>>   reproduces their original
      *>> pairwise distances.
      *>>
      *>> Same as the vector<string> constructor, but feature_columns is
      *>>   a single "<count>
      *>> col1..."-encoded string -- see KMeans's encoded constructor
      *>>   for why.
       01 DM-MDS-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-ULONG-STRING.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-ULONG-STRING-GIVEN USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-ULONG-STRING-DATA USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> encoded_feature_columns (const std::string &): text in PIC
      *>>   X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-DATA-FRM-STRNG-ULNG-STRNG-ENCDD-FTR-COLUMNS PIC
              X(256).
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-DAT-FRM-STR-ULNG-STRNG-ENCDD-FTR-CLMNS-LNGTH
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> n_components (std::size_t = 2): unsigned long.
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-ULONG-STRING-N-COMPONENTS
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> metric (const std::string & = "euclidean"): text in PIC
      *>>   X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-ULONG-STRING-METRIC PIC
              X(256).
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-ULONG-STRING-METRIC-LENGTH
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> Result: MDS handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-MDS-NEW-DATA-FRAME-STRING-ULONG-STRING-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::MDS::feature_names() const ->
