      *>> datamunge::DiffusionMaps::DiffusionMaps(const DataFrame &
      *>>   data, const std::vector<std::string> & feature_columns,
      *>>   std::size_t n_components = 2, double heat_kernel_epsilon =
      *>>   1.0, double alpha = 0.5, double diffusion_time = 1.0) ->
      *>>   DIFFUSION-MAPS handle
      *>> CALL "dm_diffusion_maps_new" USING DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::DiffusionMaps. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::DiffusionMaps —
      *>>   embeds points via the
      *>> leading eigenvectors of a dense, alpha-normalized heat-kernel
      *>>   Markov transition matrix,
      *>> scaled by eigenvalue^diffusion_time. Distinct from
      *>>   LaplacianEigenmaps (sparse k-NN
      *>> graph Laplacian, no density normalization).
       01 DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 6 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> feature_columns (const std::vector<std::string> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-STRING handle.
          05 DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW-FEATURE-COLUMNS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> n_components (std::size_t = 2): unsigned long.
          05 DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW-N-COMPONENTS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> heat_kernel_epsilon (double = 1.0): double.
          05 DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW-HEAT-KERNEL-EPSILON USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> alpha (double = 0.5): double.
          05 DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW-ALPHA USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> diffusion_time (double = 1.0): double.
          05 DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW-DIFFUSION-TIME USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result: DIFFUSION-MAPS handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-DIFFUSION-MAPS-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::DiffusionMaps::DiffusionMaps(const DataFrame &
      *>>   data, const std::string & encoded_feature_columns,
