      *>>   DIFFUSION-MAPS handle
      *>> CALL "dm_dffsn_mps_new_data_frm_strng_ulng_dbl_double_double"
      *>>   USING DM-DFFSN-MPS-NEW-DATA-FRM-STRNG-ULNG-DBL-DOUBLE-DOUBLE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::DiffusionMaps. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::DiffusionMaps —
      *>>   embeds points via the
      *>> leading eigenvectors of a dense, alpha-normalized heat-kernel
      *>>   Markov transition matrix,
      *>> scaled by eigenvalue^diffusion_time. Distinct from
      *>>   LaplacianEigenmaps (sparse k-NN
      *>> graph Laplacian, no density normalization).
      *>>
      *>> Same as the vector<string> constructor, but feature_columns is
      *>>   a single "<count>
      *>> col1..."-encoded string -- see KMeans's encoded constructor
      *>>   for why.
       01 DM-DFFSN-MPS-NEW-DATA-FRM-STRNG-ULNG-DBL-DOUBLE-DOUBLE.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 6 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-DFFSN-MPS-NEW-DATA-FRM-STRNG-ULNG-DBL-DBL-DBL-GIVEN
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-DFFSN-MPS-NEW-DATA-FRM-STRNG-ULNG-DBL-DBL-DBL-DATA USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> encoded_feature_columns (const std::string &): text in PIC
      *>>   X(256); -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-DFF-MPS-NEW-DAT-FRM-STR-ULN-DBL-DBL-DBL-ENC-FTR-CLMN PIC
              X(256).
