      *>   GBM-REGRESSOR

      *>> datamunge::GBMRegressor::GBMRegressor(const DataFrame & data,
      *>>   const std::string & formula, std::size_t n_trees = 100,
      *>>   double learning_rate = 0.10000000000000001, std::size_t
      *>>   max_depth = 3, std::size_t min_samples_split = 2,
      *>>   std::size_t min_samples_leaf = 1, double subsample = 1.0,
      *>>   std::uint64_t seed = 42) -> GBM-REGRESSOR handle
      *>> CALL "dm_gbm_regressor_new" USING DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::GBMRegressor. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::GBMRegressor — a
      *>>   sequence of shallow regression trees,
      *>> each fit to the residuals of the current ensemble (gradient
      *>>   boosting on squared error).
       01 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 9 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> n_trees (std::size_t = 100): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-N-TREES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> learning_rate (double = 0.10000000000000001): double.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-LEARNING-RATE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> max_depth (std::size_t = 3): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-MAX-DEPTH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> min_samples_split (std::size_t = 2): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-MIN-SAMPLES-SPLIT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> min_samples_leaf (std::size_t = 1): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-MIN-SAMPLES-LEAF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> subsample (double = 1.0): double.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-SUBSAMPLE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> seed (std::uint64_t = 42): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-SEED USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: GBM-REGRESSOR handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-GBM-REGRESSOR-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

