      *>> datamunge::KernelRegression::KernelRegression(const DataFrame
      *>>   & data, const std::string & formula, const std::string &
      *>>   kernel = "gaussian", double bandwidth = -1.0, std::size_t
      *>>   n_bandwidth = 50, bool standardize = true) ->
      *>>   KERNEL-REGRESSION handle
      *>> CALL "dm_kernel_regression_new" USING DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::KernelRegression. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::KernelRegression
      *>>   — Nadaraya-Watson kernel regression, a
      *>> nonparametric fit where each prediction is a kernel-weighted
      *>>   average of training responses.
       01 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 6 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> kernel (const std::string & = "gaussian"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. "gaussian" (default),
      *>>   "epanechnikov", "uniform", or "triangular".
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-KERNEL PIC X(256).
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-KERNEL-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> bandwidth (double = -1.0): double. Bandwidth in
      *>>   standardized-predictor units; pass a negative value (the
      *>>   default) to select it automatically via leave-one-out
      *>>   cross-validation.
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-BANDWIDTH USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> n_bandwidth (std::size_t = 50): unsigned long.
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-N-BANDWIDTH USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> standardize (bool = true): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-STANDARDIZE USAGE BINARY-CHAR
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: KERNEL-REGRESSION handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-KERNEL-REGRESSION-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

