      *>   GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION

      *>> datamunge::GaussianProcessRegression::GaussianProcessRegression(const
      *>>   DataFrame & data, const std::string & formula, double
      *>>   length_scale = -1.0, double noise_ratio = -1.0, std::size_t
      *>>   n_length_scale_grid = 20, std::size_t n_noise_grid = 15,
      *>>   bool standardize = true) -> GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_gaussian_process_regression_new" USING
      *>>   DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::GaussianProcessRegression. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for
      *>>   datamunge::stats::GaussianProcessRegression — exact
      *>>   Gaussian process
      *>> regression with an RBF kernel, fit via Cholesky decomposition.
      *>>   Unlike every other regressor here,
      *>> predictions come with a principled posterior confidence
      *>>   interval; see predict_frame().
       01 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 7 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> length_scale (double = -1.0): double. RBF kernel length scale
      *>>   in standardized-predictor units; pass a negative value (the
      *>>   default) to select it automatically by maximizing the log
      *>>   marginal likelihood.
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-LENGTH-SCALE USAGE
              COMP-2.
      *>> noise_ratio (double = -1.0): double. noise_variance /
      *>>   signal_variance; pass a negative value (the default) to
      *>>   select it automatically the same way (0 is a legal fixed
      *>>   value: a noiseless/interpolating GP).
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-NOISE-RATIO USAGE
              COMP-2.
      *>> n_length_scale_grid (std::size_t = 20): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-N-LENGTH-SCALE-GRID
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> n_noise_grid (std::size_t = 15): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-N-NOISE-GRID USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> standardize (bool = true): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-STANDARDIZE USAGE
              BINARY-CHAR UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-PROCESS-REGRESSION-NEW-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

