      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER

      *>> datamunge::NaiveBayesClassifier::NaiveBayesClassifier(const
      *>>   DataFrame & data, const std::string & formula, double
      *>>   laplace_smoothing = 1.0, double var_smoothing =
      *>>   1.0000000000000001E-9) -> NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER handle
      *>> CALL "dm_naive_bayes_classifier_new" USING
      *>>   DM-NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::NaiveBayesClassifier. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for
      *>>   datamunge::stats::NaiveBayesClassifier — a Naive Bayes
      *>>   classifier that
      *>> models numeric predictors with per-class Gaussians and
      *>>   categorical predictors with per-class
      *>> frequency tables (each categorical predictor's levels modeled
      *>>   jointly as one variable, not as
      *>> separate independent dummy features).
       01 DM-NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> laplace_smoothing (double = 1.0): double.
          05 DM-NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER-NEW-LAPLACE-SMOOTHING USAGE
              COMP-2.
      *>> var_smoothing (double = 1.0000000000000001E-9): double.
          05 DM-NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER-NEW-VAR-SMOOTHING USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result: NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-NAIVE-BAYES-CLASSIFIER-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

