      *>   GLM

      *>> datamunge::GLM::GLM(const DataFrame & data, const std::string
      *>>   & formula, const std::string & family = "gaussian", const
      *>>   std::string & weights_column = "", std::size_t max_iter =
      *>>   25, double tol = 1.0E-8) -> GLM handle
      *>> CALL "dm_glm_new" USING DM-GLM-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::GLM. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::GLM — a
      *>>   generalized linear model (gaussian, binomial,
      *>> poisson, or Gamma family with its canonical link, matching R's
      *>>   glm() defaults) fit by iteratively
      *>> reweighted least squares.
       01 DM-GLM-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 6 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> data (const DataFrame &): DATA-FRAME handle.
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-DATA USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> formula (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-FORMULA PIC X(256).
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-FORMULA-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> family (const std::string & = "gaussian"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. One of "gaussian"
      *>>   (identity link), "binomial" (logit link), "poisson" (log
      *>>   link), or "Gamma" (inverse link).
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-FAMILY PIC X(256).
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-FAMILY-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> weights_column (const std::string & = ""): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. Optional column name
      *>>   enabling prior weights; pass "" (the default) for none.
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-WEIGHTS-COLUMN PIC X(256).
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-WEIGHTS-COLUMN-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> max_iter (std::size_t = 25): unsigned long.
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-MAX-ITER USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> tol (double = 1.0E-8): double.
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-TOL USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result: GLM handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-GLM-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

