      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   DUAL

      *>> datamunge::Dual::Dual(double value, double derivative = 0.0)
      *>>   -> DUAL handle
      *>> CALL "dm_dual_new" USING DM-DUAL-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::Dual. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::autodiff::Dual -- a
      *>>   first-order forward-mode
      *>> dual number. Build an expression out of named operations
      *>>   (starting from a seed
      *>> with derivative=1) to read off an exact derivative alongside
      *>>   the value.
      *>>
      *>> A dual number value + derivative·ε (ε² = 0).
      *>>
      *>> Seed the variable you differentiate with derivative 1 and
      *>>   constants with 0; every
      *>> operation then carries the exact derivative with respect to
      *>>   that seed.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::Dual x(2.0, 1.0); // seed d/dx
      *>> std::print("{}\n", x.multiply(x).derivative()); // 4
      *>> ```
       01 DM-DUAL-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 2 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-DUAL-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> Value (double): double. Real part, the function value.
          05 DM-DUAL-NEW-VALUE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> derivative (double = 0.0): double. Dual part, the derivative
      *>>   with respect to the seed (default 0).
          05 DM-DUAL-NEW-DERIVATIVE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result: DUAL handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-DUAL-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Dual::value() const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_dual_value" USING DM-DUAL-VALUE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The real part: the function value.
       01 DM-DUAL-VALUE.
      *>> Self: the DUAL handle.
          05 DM-DUAL-VALUE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double.
          05 DM-DUAL-VALUE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::Dual::derivative() const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_dual_derivative" USING DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The dual part: the exact derivative with respect to the seed.
       01 DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE.
      *>> Self: the DUAL handle.
          05 DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double.
          05 DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::Dual::add(const Dual & other) const -> Dual
      *>> CALL "dm_dual_add" USING DM-DUAL-ADD DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Sum: this + `other`, with derivative a' + b'.
