      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   HYPER-DUAL

      *>> datamunge::HyperDual::HyperDual(double value, double eps1 =
      *>>   0.0, double eps2 = 0.0, double eps1eps2 = 0.0) -> HYPER-DUAL
      *>>   handle
      *>> CALL "dm_hyper_dual_new" USING DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::HyperDual. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::autodiff::HyperDual -- a
      *>>   second-order
      *>> forward-mode dual number carrying two independent derivative
      *>>   directions plus
      *>> their exact mixed second partial, for computing Hessian
      *>>   entries.
      *>>
      *>> A hyper-dual number value + eps1·ε₁ + eps2·ε₂ +
      *>>   eps1eps2·ε₁ε₂ (ε₁² = ε₂² = 0).
      *>>
      *>> Seed input i with eps1 = 1 and input j with eps2 = 1 (both on
      *>>   the same input for a
      *>> diagonal entry); the result's eps1eps2() is then the exact
      *>>   ∂²f/∂xᵢ∂xⱼ.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> const dm::HyperDual x(3.0, 1.0, 1.0);
      *>> std::print("{}\n", x.multiply(x).eps1eps2()); // d²(x²)/dx²
      *>>   = 2
      *>> ```
       01 DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> Value (double): double. Real part, the function value.
          05 DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-VALUE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> eps1 (double = 0.0): double. First derivative along the first
      *>>   seed direction (default 0).
          05 DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-EPS1 USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> eps2 (double = 0.0): double. First derivative along the second
      *>>   seed direction (default 0).
          05 DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-EPS2 USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> eps1eps2 (double = 0.0): double. Mixed second derivative part
      *>>   (default 0; leave 0 for inputs).
          05 DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-EPS1EPS2 USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result: HYPER-DUAL handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::HyperDual::value() const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_hyper_dual_value" USING DM-HYPER-DUAL-VALUE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The real part: the function value.
       01 DM-HYPER-DUAL-VALUE.
      *>> Self: the HYPER-DUAL handle.
          05 DM-HYPER-DUAL-VALUE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double.
          05 DM-HYPER-DUAL-VALUE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::HyperDual::eps1() const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_hyper_dual_eps1" USING DM-HYPER-DUAL-EPS1 DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Derivative along the first seed direction (ε₁ part).
       01 DM-HYPER-DUAL-EPS1.
      *>> Self: the HYPER-DUAL handle.
