      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   TAPE

      *>> datamunge::Tape::Tape() -> TAPE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_tape_new" USING DM-TAPE-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::Tape. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::autodiff::Tape -- a
      *>>   reverse-mode
      *>> ("backpropagation") computation tape. Create leaf Vars against
      *>>   a Tape, build an
      *>> expression out of named Var operations, then call backward()
      *>>   on the output Var
      *>> to get the derivative of that output with respect to every
      *>>   node on the tape
      *>> (index a leaf's own index() into the result to read its
      *>>   gradient).
      *>>
      *>> An empty tape; create leaf Vars against it with Var(tape,
      *>>   value).
       01 DM-TAPE-NEW.
      *>> Result: TAPE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-TAPE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Tape::size() const -> std::size_t
      *>> CALL "dm_tape_size" USING DM-TAPE-SIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Number of recorded nodes (leaves plus operation results).
       01 DM-TAPE-SIZE.
      *>> Self: the TAPE handle.
          05 DM-TAPE-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::size_t): unsigned long.
          05 DM-TAPE-SIZE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::Tape::value_at(std::size_t index) const -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_tape_value_at" USING DM-TAPE-VALUE-AT DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The value recorded at node `index`.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: When `index` >= size().
       01 DM-TAPE-VALUE-AT.
      *>> Self: the TAPE handle.
          05 DM-TAPE-VALUE-AT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> index (std::size_t): unsigned long. Node index, as returned by
      *>>   Var::index().
          05 DM-TAPE-VALUE-AT-INDEX USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. The node's value.
          05 DM-TAPE-VALUE-AT-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::Tape::backward(const Var & output) const ->
      *>>   std::vector<double>
      *>> CALL "dm_tape_backward" USING DM-TAPE-BACKWARD DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Reverse sweep from `output`: d(output)/d(node) for every node
      *>>   on the tape.
      *>>
      *>> The tape is unchanged, so backward() may be called again for
      *>>   other outputs.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::Tape tape;
      *>> const dm::Var a(tape, 2.0), b(tape, 3.0);
      *>> const auto grad = tape.backward(a.multiply(b));
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n", grad[a.index()], grad[b.index()]); // 3
      *>>   2
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: When `output` is not a node of this tape.
       01 DM-TAPE-BACKWARD.
      *>> Self: the TAPE handle.
          05 DM-TAPE-BACKWARD-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> output (const Var &): VAR handle. A Var recorded on this tape
      *>>   (usually the final expression).
          05 DM-TAPE-BACKWARD-OUTPUT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; close
      *>>   it). One adjoint per node, indexed by Var::index() (0-based;
      *>>   add 1 in R and Lua).
          05 DM-TAPE-BACKWARD-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

