      *>> datamunge::cad::View::View() -> CAD-SCENE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_cad_scene_new" USING DM-CAD-SCENE-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::cad::View. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A small code-driven scene facade, exposed as CadScene in
      *>>   Python/R.
      *>> Owns scene/camera/render controls. All operations delegate to
      *>>   the canonical
      *>> CAD, polygon and renderer APIs; copying retains independent
      *>>   scene state.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::cad::View view;
      *>> view.add(dm::cad::Solid::box(2, 3, 4), "#3b82f6", "block");
      *>> view.size(640, 480); view.render("block.png");
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Create an empty scene with automatic camera framing.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> See the class example.
       01 DM-CAD-SCENE-NEW.
      *>> Result: CAD-SCENE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::cad::View::from_file(const std::string &
      *>>   path) -> View
      *>> CALL "dm_cad_scene_from_file" USING DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-FILE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Import any format supported by load_scene().
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto view = dm::cad::View::from_file("part.step");
      *>> view.render("part.png");
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: Unsupported format.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: Import/I/O failure.
       01 DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-FILE.
      *>> path (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. Input filename.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-FILE-PATH PIC X(256).
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-FILE-PATH-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> Result (View): CAD-SCENE handle (new; close it). Owned view
      *>>   with automatic framing.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-FILE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> static datamunge::cad::View::from_urdf(const std::string &
      *>>   path) -> View
      *>> CALL "dm_cad_scene_from_urdf" USING DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-URDF
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Load an articulated URDF visual model and its asset files.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto view = dm::cad::View::from_urdf("robot.urdf");
      *>> view.set_joint("joint2", -.6); view.render("robot.png");
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: Invalid URDF/joint data.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: Import failure.
       01 DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-URDF.
      *>> path (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces. URDF file; relative meshes resolve
      *>>   beside it.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-URDF-PATH PIC X(256).
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-URDF-PATH-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> Result (View): CAD-SCENE handle (new; close it). Owned view at
      *>>   the loader's initial joint coordinates.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-FROM-URDF-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::cad::View::set_joint(const std::string & name,
      *>>   double value) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_cad_scene_set_joint" USING DM-CAD-SCENE-SET-JOINT
