      *>> datamunge::cad::View::add(const Solid & solid, const
      *>>   std::string & color = "#4080d9", const std::string & name =
      *>>   "Solid") -> int
      *>> CALL "dm_cad_scene_add" USING DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Tessellate a solid and append it as a scene object.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> See the class example.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: Invalid color.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: Tessellation failure.
       01 DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD.
      *>> Self: the CAD-SCENE handle.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> solid (const Solid &): CAD-SOLID handle. Borrowed source,
      *>>   unchanged.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD-SOLID USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> color (const std::string & = "#4080d9"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. Hex RGB/RGBA tint, default
      *>>   #4080d9.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD-COLOR PIC X(256).
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD-COLOR-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> name (const std::string & = "Solid"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces. Object name, default
      *>>   Solid.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD-NAME PIC X(256).
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD-NAME-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> Result (int): int. New object ID.
          05 DM-CAD-SCENE-ADD-RESULT USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.

