      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT

      *>> datamunge::fda::BSplineRefinement::BSplineRefinement() ->
      *>>   B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT handle
      *>> CALL "dm_b_spline_refinement_new" USING
      *>>   DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fda::BSplineRefinement. Close the handle
      *>>   with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A refined B-spline basis together with the operator that maps
      *>>   coarse
      *>> coefficients onto it.
      *>>
      *>> For any coefficient vector c on the coarse basis, `matrix * c`
      *>>   (equivalently apply())
      *>> gives coefficients on the refined basis that represent exactly
      *>>   the same spline.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto coarse = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(2, 4);
      *>> auto refined = dm::fda::dyadic_refine(coarse);
      *>> std::print("{}\n", refined.basis.basis_size()); // 6
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> See also: refine_basis(), dyadic_refine()
       01 DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-NEW.
      *>> Result: B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::BSplineRefinement::apply(const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & coefficients) const ->
      *>>   std::vector<double>
      *>> CALL "dm_b_spline_refinement_apply" USING
      *>>   DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-APPLY DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Maps coarse coefficients to the refined basis.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto r =
      *>>   dm::fda::dyadic_refine(dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1,
      *>>   2));
      *>> std::print("{}\n", r.apply({0.0, 2.0})); // [0, 1, 2]
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If `coefficients` does not match the
      *>>   coarse basis size.
       01 DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-APPLY.
      *>> Self: the B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT handle.
          05 DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-APPLY-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> coefficients (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. One coefficient per coarse basis function.
          05 DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-APPLY-COEFFICIENTS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; close
      *>>   it). One coefficient per refined basis function,
      *>>   representing the same spline.
          05 DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-APPLY-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> BSplineBasis datamunge::fda::BSplineRefinement::basis
      *>> CALL "dm_b_spline_refinement_basis_get" USING
      *>>   DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-BASIS DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_b_spline_refinement_basis_set" USING
      *>>   DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-BASIS DM-STATUS (writes -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Refined basis (same degree and domain).
       01 DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-BASIS.
      *>> Self: the B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT handle.
          05 DM-B-SPLINE-REFINEMENT-BASIS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (BSplineBasis): B-SPLINE-BASIS handle (new; refers into
