      *>> datamunge::fda::TensorBSpline::evaluate_grid(const
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> & axes) const ->
      *>>   std::vector<double>
      *>> CALL "dm_tensor_b_spline_evaluate_grid" USING
      *>>   DM-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-EVALUATE-GRID DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Evaluates on the Cartesian product of per-axis sample values.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
      *>> dm::fda::TensorBSpline f({b, b}, {0, 1, 1, 2});
      *>> std::print("{}\n", f.evaluate_grid({{0, 1}, {0, 1}})); // [0,
      *>>   1, 1, 2]
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If axes.size() != dimensions() or an
      *>>   axis is empty.
       01 DM-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-EVALUATE-GRID.
      *>> Self: the TENSOR-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-EVALUATE-GRID-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> axes (const std::vector<std::vector<double>> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. d non-empty coordinate lists.
          05 DM-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-EVALUATE-GRID-AXES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; close
      *>>   it). Row-major grid of values (axis 0 slowest, last axis
      *>>   fastest).
          05 DM-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-EVALUATE-GRID-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::TensorBSpline::dyadic_refine() const ->
      *>>   TensorBSpline
      *>> CALL "dm_tensor_b_spline_dyadic_refine" USING
      *>>   DM-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-DYADIC-REFINE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Dyadically refines every axis and maps the coefficients,
      *>>   giving an identical
      *>> function on the finer, nested tensor basis.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::TensorBSpline
      *>>   f(dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(2, 4), {0, 1, 3, 2});
      *>> auto g = f.dyadic_refine();
      *>> std::print("{} {:.6f}\n", g.coefficient_count(),
      *>>   g.evaluate(0.3) - f.evaluate(0.3)); // 6 0.000000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If some axis basis is not clamped.
      *>>
      *>> See also: dyadic_refine(const BSplineBasis&)
       01 DM-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-DYADIC-REFINE.
      *>> Self: the TENSOR-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-DYADIC-REFINE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (TensorBSpline): TENSOR-B-SPLINE handle (new; close
      *>>   it). The refined spline.
          05 DM-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-DYADIC-REFINE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   ORTHANT-CELL-TREE

      *>> datamunge::fda::detail::OrthantCellTree::OrthantCellTree(std::vector<double>
      *>>   lo, std::vector<double> hi) -> ORTHANT-CELL-TREE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_orthant_cell_tree_new" USING DM-ORTHANT-CELL-TREE-NEW
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fda::detail::OrthantCellTree. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Dyadic 2^d-ary tree of axis-aligned boxes shared by the
      *>>   hierarchical splines.
      *>>
      *>> Cells live in a flat vector and are addressed by id (root 0).
      *>>   Children are created on
      *>> demand by halving every axis; slot bit k selects the upper
      *>>   half of axis k.
      *>>
      *>> Creates the root cell [lo, hi].
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: On empty/mismatched/non-finite
      *>>   bounds, lo >= hi, or more than 20 dimensions.
       01 DM-ORTHANT-CELL-TREE-NEW.
      *>> lo (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Lower corner.
          05 DM-ORTHANT-CELL-TREE-NEW-LO USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> hi (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Upper corner,
      *>>   with lo[k] < hi[k].
          05 DM-ORTHANT-CELL-TREE-NEW-HI USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: ORTHANT-CELL-TREE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-ORTHANT-CELL-TREE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

