      *>> CALL "dm_axis_refinement_cols_get" USING
      *>>   DM-AXIS-REFINEMENT-COLS DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_axis_refinement_cols_set" USING
      *>>   DM-AXIS-REFINEMENT-COLS DM-STATUS (writes -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> cols[j]: (refined i, R(i, j)) for coarse index j.
       01 DM-AXIS-REFINEMENT-COLS.
      *>> Self: the AXIS-REFINEMENT handle.
          05 DM-AXIS-REFINEMENT-COLS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (RefinementRows): VECTOR-VECTOR-PAIR-INT-DOUBLE handle
      *>>   (new; refers into its owner, which it keeps alive).
          05 DM-AXIS-REFINEMENT-COLS-VALUE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::HierarchicalBSpline(std::vector<double>
      *>>   domain_min, std::vector<double> domain_max) ->
      *>>   HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_new" USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline. Close the
      *>>   handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Classical (overlay) hierarchical B-spline in the style of
      *>>   Forsey and Bartels:
      *>> every cell of a dyadic tree may carry its own local "detail"
      *>>   TensorBSpline.
      *>>
      *>> evaluate(x) sums the patch of every cell on the root-to-leaf
      *>>   path containing x. Each
      *>> patch is evaluated in its cell's local coordinates, (x -
      *>>   cell_min) / (cell_max -
      *>> cell_min) in [0, 1]^d, so patch bases should span [0, 1].
      *>>   Patches are independent
      *>> (no shared nested basis and no truncation); see
      *>>   TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline for the
      *>> THB-spline construction. Cells are identified by integer ids
      *>>   (root 0).
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(0, 1); //
      *>>   constant patch
      *>> h.set_spline(h.root(), dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {1.0}));
      *>> h.refine(h.root(), 1, dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {2.0})); //
      *>>   upper half
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n", h.evaluate({0.25}), h.evaluate({0.75}));
      *>>   // 1 3
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - D. R. Forsey and R. H. Bartels (1988). Hierarchical B-spline
      *>>   refinement. ACM SIGGRAPH
      *>>   Computer Graphics 22(4), 205-212.
      *>>     https://doi.org/10.1145/378456.378512
      *>>
      *>> See also: TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline
      *>>
      *>> Creates a hierarchy whose root cell is [domain_min,
      *>>   domain_max], with no patches.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 2.0});
      *>> std::print("{} {}\n", h.dimensions(), h.cell_count()); // 2 1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: On empty, mismatched or non-finite
      *>>   bounds, min >= max, or more than 20 dimensions.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-NEW.
      *>> domain_min (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Lower
      *>>   corner (length d >= 1).
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-NEW-DOMAIN-MIN USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> domain_max (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Upper
      *>>   corner, with domain_min[k] < domain_max[k].
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-NEW-DOMAIN-MAX USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::dimensions() const ->
      *>>   std::size_t
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_dimensions" USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-DIMENSIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Number of dimensions d.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-DIMENSIONS.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-DIMENSIONS-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::size_t): unsigned long. d.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-DIMENSIONS-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::cell_count() const -> int
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_cell_count" USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-CELL-COUNT DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Number of cells created so far.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-CELL-COUNT.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-CELL-COUNT-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (int): int. Cell count.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-CELL-COUNT-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::root() const -> int
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_root" USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-ROOT DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Root cell id.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-ROOT.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-ROOT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (int): int. Always 0.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-ROOT-RESULT USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::parent(int cell) const ->
