      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::subdivide(int cell) ->
      *>>   std::vector<int>
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_subdivide" USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-SUBDIVIDE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Creates all 2^d children of `cell` (existing ones are kept),
      *>>   without patches.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 1.0});
      *>> std::print("{}\n", h.subdivide(h.root()).size()); // 4
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: For an invalid id.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-SUBDIVIDE.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-SUBDIVIDE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> cell (int): int. Cell id.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-SUBDIVIDE-CELL USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<int>): VECTOR-INT handle (new; close it).
      *>>   The 2^d child ids in slot order.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-SUBDIVIDE-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::refine(int cell, int
      *>>   slot) -> int
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_refine" USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Creates (if needed) only the child of `cell` at `slot`.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
      *>> int c = h.refine(h.root(), 0);
      *>> std::print("{}\n", h.cell_max(c)); // [0.5]
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: For an invalid id or slot.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> cell (int): int. Cell id.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-CELL USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED.
      *>> slot (int): int. Child slot; bit k selects the upper half of
      *>>   axis k.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-SLOT USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED.
      *>> Result (int): int. The child id.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::refine(int cell, int
      *>>   slot, TensorBSpline spline) -> int
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_refine_int_int_tensor_b_spline"
      *>>   USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-INT-INT-TENSOR-B-SPLINE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Creates (if needed) the child at `slot` and installs `spline`
      *>>   on it.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> See the class example.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: For an invalid id or slot.
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the patch dimension differs from
      *>>   dimensions().
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-INT-INT-TENSOR-B-SPLINE.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-INT-INT-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-SELF
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> cell (int): int. Cell id.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-INT-INT-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-CELL
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> slot (int): int. Child slot.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-INT-INT-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-SLOT
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> spline (TensorBSpline): TENSOR-B-SPLINE handle. Patch for the
      *>>   child.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLN-REFINE-INT-INT-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-SPLINE
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (int): int. The child id.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLN-REFINE-INT-INT-TENSOR-B-SPLINE-RESULT
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::refine_region(const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & region_min, const std::vector<double>
      *>>   & region_max, int depth) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_refine_region" USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-REGION DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Subdivides, down to depth `depth`, every cell overlapping the
      *>>   open box
      *>> (region_min, region_max).
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
      *>> h.refine_region({0.0}, {0.3}, 2);
      *>> std::print("{}\n", h.cell_count()); // 4
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: On mismatched sizes or min >= max.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-REGION.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-REGION-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> region_min (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Lower corner.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-REGION-REGION-MIN USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> region_max (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Upper corner (min < max per axis).
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-REGION-REGION-MAX USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> depth (int): int. Deepest depth to create (cells already
      *>>   deeper are untouched).
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-REGION-DEPTH USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::refine_region(const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & region_min, const std::vector<double>
      *>>   & region_max, int depth, const SplineFactory & factory) ->
      *>>   void
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_refine_region_vector_dou_pvm8l"
      *>>   USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-REGION-VECTOR-DOU-PVM8L
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Like refine_region(region_min, region_max, depth) but calls
      *>>   `factory` on every
      *>> touched cell (new or existing) and installs any patch it
      *>>   returns.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(0, 1);
      *>> h.refine_region({0.0}, {0.3}, 1, [&](auto&, auto&) { return
      *>>   dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {1.0}); });
      *>> std::print("{}\n", h.evaluate({0.1})); // 1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: On invalid bounds or a patch of the
      *>>   wrong dimension.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-REGION-VECTOR-DOU-PVM8L.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLINE-REFINE-REGION-VECTOR-DOU-PVM8L-SELF
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> region_min (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Lower corner.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLN-RFN-RGN-VECTOR-DOU-PVM8L-REGION-MIN USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> region_max (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE
      *>>   handle. Upper corner.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLN-RFN-RGN-VECTOR-DOU-PVM8L-REGION-MAX USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> depth (int): int. Deepest depth.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLN-REFINE-REGION-VECTOR-DOU-PVM8L-DEPTH
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> factory (const SplineFactory &): PROGRAM-POINTER (SET it TO
      *>>   ENTRY "PROGRAM-ID"), or NULL. Patch callback; std::nullopt
      *>>   leaves a cell unchanged.
          05 DM-HRRCHCL-B-SPLN-RFN-REGION-VECTOR-DOU-PVM8L-FACTORY USAGE
              PROGRAM-POINTER.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::fit_cell(int cell,
      *>>   std::vector<BSplineBasis> bases, const
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & values, const SplineSolveOptions &
      *>>   options = {}) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_fit_cell" USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Least-squares fits a new patch on `cell` so the whole
      *>>   hierarchy matches
      *>> `values` at `points`.
      *>>
      *>> The patch explains only what is left after every other patch
      *>>   on the path (the
      *>> residual values - evaluate(points)), in the spirit of
      *>>   Forsey-Bartels editing, so pass
      *>> raw data values rather than residuals. Points are global
      *>>   coordinates inside the cell.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
      *>> h.fit_cell(h.root(), {b}, {{0.0}, {1.0}}, {1.0, 3.0});
      *>> std::print("{}\n", h.evaluate({0.5})); // 2
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: For an invalid id.
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If the cell has a patch, inputs are
      *>>   empty/mismatched, or a point lies outside the cell.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the local normal equations are
      *>>   singular.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 4 to 5 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 4.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE 4.
      *>> cell (int): int. Cell id; must not already have a patch
      *>>   (clear_spline() first to refit).
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-CELL USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED.
      *>> bases (std::vector<BSplineBasis>): VECTOR-B-SPLINE-BASIS
      *>>   handle. Patch bases on [0, 1], one per dimension.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-BASES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> points (const std::vector<std::vector<double>> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Sample locations inside the
      *>>   cell.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-POINTS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> values (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   One raw data value per point.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-VALUES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> options (const SplineSolveOptions & = {}):
      *>>   SPLINE-SOLVE-OPTIONS handle. Solver settings.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-OPTIONS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::fit_cell_penalized(int
      *>>   cell, std::vector<BSplineBasis> bases, const
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & values, const std::vector<double> &
      *>>   lambdas, int order = 2, const SplineSolveOptions & options =
      *>>   {}) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_hierarchical_b_spline_fit_cell_penalized" USING
      *>>   DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Penalized (P-spline) variant of fit_cell() with per-axis
      *>>   `lambdas` and
      *>> difference `order`; all-zero lambdas give fit_cell().
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(3, 10);
      *>> h.fit_cell_penalized(h.root(), {b}, {{0.0}, {1.0}}, {0.0,
      *>>   2.0}, {1e3});
      *>> std::print("{:.3f}\n", h.evaluate({0.5})); // 1.000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: For an invalid id.
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: As for fit_cell() and
      *>>   fit_tensor_pspline().
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the penalized normal equations are
      *>>   singular.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 5 to 7 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 5.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED-GIVEN USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 5.
      *>> cell (int): int. Cell id without a patch.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED-CELL USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> bases (std::vector<BSplineBasis>): VECTOR-B-SPLINE-BASIS
      *>>   handle. Patch bases on [0, 1].
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED-BASES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> points (const std::vector<std::vector<double>> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Sample locations inside the
      *>>   cell.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED-POINTS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> values (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Raw data values.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED-VALUES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> lambdas (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Nonnegative per-axis weights.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED-LAMBDAS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> order (int = 2): int. Difference order (default 2).
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED-ORDER USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> options (const SplineSolveOptions & = {}):
      *>>   SPLINE-SOLVE-OPTIONS handle. Solver settings.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-CELL-PENALIZED-OPTIONS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

