      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: On a dimension mismatch, empty axis,
      *>>   or outside point.
       01 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-EVALUATE-GRID.
      *>> Self: the HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-EVALUATE-GRID-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> axes (const std::vector<std::vector<double>> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. d non-empty coordinate lists.
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-EVALUATE-GRID-AXES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; close
      *>>   it). Row-major values (last axis fastest).
          05 DM-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-EVALUATE-GRID-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE

      *>> datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline(TensorBSpline
      *>>   base) -> TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle
      *>> CALL "dm_truncated_hierarchical_b_spline_new" USING
      *>>   DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline. Close
      *>>   the handle with CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Truncated hierarchical B-spline (THB-spline) of Giannelli,
      *>>   Juttler and Speleers.
      *>>
      *>> Level 0 is the caller's TensorBSpline; level l + 1 is the
      *>>   dyadic refinement of level l.
      *>> A dyadic cell tree defines the nested domains Omega^0 (whole
      *>>   domain) contains Omega^1
      *>> contains ..., where Omega^l is the union of cells of depth >=
      *>>   l. A level-l basis
      *>> function is active when its support lies in Omega^l but not in
      *>>   Omega^(l+1). The THB
      *>> basis consists of the active functions, each truncated: its
      *>>   representation on finer
      *>> levels drops the finer functions whose support lies in the
      *>>   finer refined domain. The
      *>> resulting basis is a partition of unity, preserves the
      *>>   continuity of the underlying
      *>> splines, and spans the hierarchical spline space.
      *>>
      *>> Internally each level stores a full coefficient net whose
      *>>   entries outside the next
      *>> level's refined domain always equal the refinement of the
      *>>   coarser level; coefficient
      *>> edits are pushed down through all finer levels with
      *>>   truncation, so evaluation needs
      *>> only the finest level covering a point. Refinement never
      *>>   changes the represented
      *>> function. Bases must be clamped. Cells are integer ids (root
      *>>   0).
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(2, 4);
      *>> dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline
      *>>   thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline({b, b}, std::vector<double>(16,
      *>>   1.0)));
      *>> thb.refine_region({0.0, 0.0}, {0.5, 0.5}, 1);
      *>> std::print("{} {:.3f}\n", thb.level_count(),
      *>>   thb.evaluate({0.2, 0.2})); // 2 1.000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> **References**
      *>>
      *>> - C. Giannelli, B. Juttler and H. Speleers (2012).
      *>>   THB-splines: The truncated basis for
      *>>   hierarchical splines. Computer Aided Geometric Design 29(7),
      *>>     485-498.
      *>>   https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cagd.2012.03.025
      *>> - D. R. Forsey and R. H. Bartels (1988). Hierarchical B-spline
      *>>   refinement.
      *>>   https://doi.org/10.1145/378456.378512
      *>>
      *>> See also: HierarchicalBSpline, dyadic_refine()
      *>>
      *>> Starts a hierarchy whose level 0 (and root cell / domain) is
      *>>   `base`.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> See the class example.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: If an axis basis is not clamped or d
      *>>   > 20.
       01 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-NEW.
      *>> base (TensorBSpline): TENSOR-B-SPLINE handle. Level-0 spline;
      *>>   every axis basis must be clamped.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-NEW-BASE USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle (new; close
      *>>   it).
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-NEW-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::dimensions()
      *>>   const -> std::size_t
      *>> CALL "dm_truncated_hierarchical_b_spline_dimensions" USING
      *>>   DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-DIMENSIONS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Number of dimensions d.
       01 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-DIMENSIONS.
      *>> Self: the TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-DIMENSIONS-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::size_t): unsigned long. d.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-DIMENSIONS-RESULT USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::level_count()
