      *>> datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::set_coefficient(int
      *>>   level, const std::vector<int> & index, double value) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_truncated_hierarchical_b_spline_set_coefficient"
      *>>   USING DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-SET-COEFFICIENT
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Sets the coefficient of an active function and propagates the
      *>>   change, with
      *>> truncation, to every finer level. The edit is local to the
      *>>   function's support.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
      *>> dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline
      *>>   thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {0.0, 0.0}));
      *>> thb.set_coefficient(0, {1}, 2.0);
      *>> std::print("{}\n", thb.evaluate({0.5})); // 1
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: For invalid levels/indices.
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: On a dimension mismatch or an
      *>>   inactive index.
       01 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-SET-COEFFICIENT.
