      *>> datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::fit_level(int
      *>>   level, const std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points,
      *>>   const std::vector<double> & values, const SplineSolveOptions
      *>>   & options = {}) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_truncated_hierarchical_b_spline_fit_level" USING
      *>>   DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-LEVEL DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Least-squares update of the active coefficients at `level`
      *>>   only.
      *>>
      *>> Solves for the change of the level's active coefficients that
      *>>   best explains the
      *>> residual values - evaluate(points), using the exact truncated
      *>>   basis, so pass raw
      *>> data values. Points shallower than `level` are unaffected by
      *>>   these functions and
      *>> are ignored. Typical use is coarse-to-fine: fit level 0,
      *>>   refine where residuals are
      *>> large, then fit the new level.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
      *>> dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline
      *>>   thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {0.0, 0.0}));
      *>> thb.fit_level(0, {{0.0}, {1.0}}, {1.0, 3.0});
      *>> std::print("{}\n", thb.evaluate({0.5})); // 2
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: For an invalid level.
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: On empty/mismatched inputs, points
      *>>   outside the domain, or a level with no active functions.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the normal equations are singular.
       01 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-LEVEL.
      *>> Self: the TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-LEVEL-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 3 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 3.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-LEVEL-GIVEN USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 3.
      *>> level (int): int. Level with at least one active function.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-LEVEL-LEVEL USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
