      *>> datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::fit_level_penalized(int
      *>>   level, const std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points,
      *>>   const std::vector<double> & values, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & lambdas, int order = 2, const
      *>>   SplineSolveOptions & options = {}) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_truncated_hierarchical_b_spline_fit_level_penalized"
      *>>   USING DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-LEVEL-PENALIZED
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Penalized variant of fit_level(): adds the level's full-grid
      *>>   tensor difference
      *>> penalty restricted to its active functions, applied to the
      *>>   coefficient change.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(3, 8);
      *>> dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline
      *>>   thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, std::vector<double>(8, 0.0)));
      *>> thb.fit_level_penalized(0, {{0.0}, {1.0}}, {0.0, 1.0}, {1e3});
      *>> std::print("{:.3f}\n", thb.evaluate({0.5})); // 0.500
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::out_of_range: For an invalid level.
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: As for fit_level() and
      *>>   tensor_difference_penalty().
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the normal equations are singular.
       01 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-LEVEL-PENALIZED.
      *>> Self: the TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-TRNCTD-HRRCHCL-B-SPLINE-FIT-LEVEL-PENALIZED-SELF USAGE
