      *>> datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::fit(const
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & values, const SplineSolveOptions &
      *>>   options = {}) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_truncated_hierarchical_b_spline_fit" USING
      *>>   DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Least-squares fit of every active coefficient on every level
      *>>   at once
      *>> (replaces the current function).
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
      *>> dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline
      *>>   thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {0.0, 0.0}));
      *>> thb.refine(thb.root(), 1); // adds a knot at 0.5
      *>> thb.fit({{0.0}, {0.25}, {0.5}, {0.75}, {1.0}}, {1.0, 0.5, 0.0,
      *>>   0.5, 1.0}); // |2x - 1|
      *>> std::print("{:.3f}\n", thb.evaluate({0.75})); // 0.500
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: On empty/mismatched inputs or points
      *>>   outside the domain.
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If some active function has too little
      *>>   data (singular).
       01 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT.
      *>> Self: the TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-GIVEN USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 2.
      *>> points (const std::vector<std::vector<double>> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Sample locations inside the
      *>>   domain.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-POINTS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> values (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   One value per point.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-VALUES USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> options (const SplineSolveOptions & = {}):
      *>>   SPLINE-SOLVE-OPTIONS handle. Solver settings.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-OPTIONS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::fit_penalized(const
      *>>   std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const
      *>>   std::vector<double> & values, const std::vector<double> &
      *>>   lambdas, int order = 2, const SplineSolveOptions & options =
      *>>   {}) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_truncated_hierarchical_b_spline_fit_penalized" USING
      *>>   DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-PENALIZED DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Penalized all-level fit: adds lambda_k times the squared
      *>>   order-q differences
      *>> along axis k of every run of q + 1 neighbouring active
      *>>   coefficients of a level.
      *>>
      *>> Differences that would involve an inactive coefficient are
      *>>   omitted, so for q >= 1
      *>> constant coefficients (and, generally, polynomials of degree <
      *>>   q in the coefficient
      *>> index on each level) are unpenalized; q = 0 is ridge
      *>>   regression on all coefficients.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(2, 6);
      *>> dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline
      *>>   thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, std::vector<double>(6, 0.0)));
      *>> thb.refine_region({0.0}, {0.5}, 1);
      *>> thb.fit_penalized({{0.0}, {1.0}}, {2.0, 2.0}, {1.0}, 1);
      *>> std::print("{:.3f}\n", thb.evaluate({0.3})); // 2.000
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: As for fit() and
      *>>   tensor_difference_penalty().
      *>> - std::runtime_error: If the normal equations are singular.
       01 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-PENALIZED.
      *>> Self: the TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE handle.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-PENALIZED-SELF USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 3 to 5 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 3.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-PENALIZED-GIVEN
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 3.
      *>> points (const std::vector<std::vector<double>> &):
      *>>   VECTOR-VECTOR-DOUBLE handle. Sample locations.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-PENALIZED-POINTS
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> values (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   One value per point.
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-PENALIZED-VALUES
              USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> lambdas (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Nonnegative per-axis weights.
          05 DM-TRNCTD-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-PENALIZED-LAMBDAS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> order (int = 2): int. Difference order (default 2).
          05 DM-TRUNCATED-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-PENALIZED-ORDER
              USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> options (const SplineSolveOptions & = {}):
      *>>   SPLINE-SOLVE-OPTIONS handle. Solver settings.
          05 DM-TRNCTD-HIERARCHICAL-B-SPLINE-FIT-PENALIZED-OPTIONS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

