      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   NN-MODEL

      *>> datamunge::nn::NnModel::NnModel(unsigned int seed = 0) ->
      *>>   NN-MODEL handle
      *>> CALL "dm_nn_model_new" USING DM-NN-MODEL-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::nn::NnModel. Close the handle with CALL
      *>>   "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> A sequential network. Layers are added by spec and own
      *>>   parameters named
      *>> "<kind><index>/..." (e.g. "dense0/W", "conv1/b"); batch-norm
      *>>   moving
      *>> statistics live in a second store. Parameters are created on
      *>>   the first
      *>> forward pass, when the input width is known.
       01 DM-NN-MODEL-NEW.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-NEW-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> seed (unsigned int = 0): unsigned int.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-NEW-SEED USAGE BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result: NN-MODEL handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::nn::NnModel::add_dense(int units, const std::string
      *>>   & activation = "none") -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_nn_model_add_dense" USING DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-DENSE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Fully connected layer; activation "none", "relu", "tanh",
      *>>   "sigmoid", "gelu", ...
       01 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-DENSE.
      *>> Self: the NN-MODEL handle.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-DENSE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 2 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-DENSE-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              1.
      *>> units (int): int.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-DENSE-UNITS USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> activation (const std::string & = "none"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-DENSE-ACTIVATION PIC X(256).
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-DENSE-ACTIVATION-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.

      *>> datamunge::nn::NnModel::add_conv2d(int filters, int kernel,
      *>>   int stride = 1, const std::string & padding = "same", const
      *>>   std::string & activation = "none") -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_nn_model_add_conv2d" USING DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> 2-D convolution on NHWC input; padding "same" or "valid".
       01 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D.
      *>> Self: the NN-MODEL handle.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 5 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              2.
      *>> filters (int): int.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D-FILTERS USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> kernel (int): int.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D-KERNEL USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> stride (int = 1): int.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D-STRIDE USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> padding (const std::string & = "same"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D-PADDING PIC X(256).
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D-PADDING-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.
      *>> activation (const std::string & = "none"): text in PIC X(256);
      *>>   -LENGTH -1 trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D-ACTIVATION PIC X(256).
          05 DM-NN-MODEL-ADD-CONV2D-ACTIVATION-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE -1.

      *>> datamunge::nn::NnModel::add_max_pool2d(int window, int stride,
      *>>   const std::string & padding = "valid") -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_nn_model_add_max_pool2d" USING
