      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   TASK-OUTPUT

      *>> datamunge::sim::TaskOutput::TaskOutput() -> TASK-OUTPUT handle
      *>> CALL "dm_task_output_new" USING DM-TASK-OUTPUT-NEW DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> C++ class datamunge::sim::TaskOutput. Close the handle with
      *>>   CALL "dm_close".
      *>>
      *>> Preallocated observations, rewards and independent episode-end
      *>>   flags.
      *>> Observations are row-major [environments,observation_size].
      *>>   Terminal observations
      *>> stay in final_observations until the next terminal transition
      *>>   for that index.
      *>> No auto-reset occurs. Masked-out rows keep all previous
      *>>   values.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::sim::TaskBatch task(dm::sim::Task::InvertedPendulum,2);
      *>> const auto& result=task.output();
      *>> ```
       01 DM-TASK-OUTPUT-NEW.
      *>> Result: TASK-OUTPUT handle (new; close it).
          05 DM-TASK-OUTPUT-NEW-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> std::vector<double> datamunge::sim::TaskOutput::observations
      *>> CALL "dm_task_output_observations_get" USING
      *>>   DM-TASK-OUTPUT-OBSERVATIONS DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Current observations, including terminal states.
       01 DM-TASK-OUTPUT-OBSERVATIONS.
      *>> Self: the TASK-OUTPUT handle.
          05 DM-TASK-OUTPUT-OBSERVATIONS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; refers
      *>>   into its owner, which it keeps alive).
          05 DM-TASK-OUTPUT-OBSERVATIONS-VALUE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> std::vector<double> datamunge::sim::TaskOutput::rewards
      *>> CALL "dm_task_output_rewards_get" USING DM-TASK-OUTPUT-REWARDS
      *>>   DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
      *>>
      *>> Reward from the last selected step, zero after reset.
       01 DM-TASK-OUTPUT-REWARDS.
      *>> Self: the TASK-OUTPUT handle.
          05 DM-TASK-OUTPUT-REWARDS-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Value (std::vector<double>): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new; refers
      *>>   into its owner, which it keeps alive).
          05 DM-TASK-OUTPUT-REWARDS-VALUE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> std::vector<std::uint8_t>
      *>>   datamunge::sim::TaskOutput::terminated
      *>> CALL "dm_task_output_terminated_get" USING
      *>>   DM-TASK-OUTPUT-TERMINATED DM-STATUS (reads -VALUE)
