      *>> Self: the TASK-BATCH handle.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-OBSERVATION-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::size_t): unsigned long. Four for InvertedPendulum
      *>>   or eleven for Hopper.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-OBSERVATION-SIZE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::action_size() const -> std::size_t
      *>> CALL "dm_task_batch_action_size" USING
      *>>   DM-TASK-BATCH-ACTION-SIZE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Read the continuous action width.
       01 DM-TASK-BATCH-ACTION-SIZE.
      *>> Self: the TASK-BATCH handle.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-ACTION-SIZE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::size_t): unsigned long. One for InvertedPendulum
      *>>   or three for Hopper.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-ACTION-SIZE-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::output() const -> const TaskOutput
      *>>   &
      *>> CALL "dm_task_batch_output" USING DM-TASK-BATCH-OUTPUT
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Borrow current rollout outputs without advancing the
      *>>   simulation.
       01 DM-TASK-BATCH-OUTPUT.
      *>> Self: the TASK-BATCH handle.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-OUTPUT-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const TaskOutput &): TASK-OUTPUT handle (new; close
      *>>   it). Internal reusable arrays, valid until destruction and
      *>>   modified by step/reset.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-OUTPUT-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::step(const std::vector<double> &
      *>>   actions, const std::vector<std::uint8_t> & mask = {}) ->
      *>>   const TaskOutput &
      *>> CALL "dm_task_batch_step" USING DM-TASK-BATCH-STEP DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Advance selected task rows and retain final observations on
      *>>   episode end.
      *>> Selected completed rows must be reset first. An unselected row
      *>>   remains unchanged.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::sim::TaskBatch task(dm::sim::Task::Hopper,1);
      *>> const auto& result=task.step({0,0,0});
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: Invalid action shape/value or mask,
      *>>   before mutation.
      *>> - std::logic_error: A selected row already finished.
      *>> - std::exception: Physics failure; explicit reset is required
      *>>   before retrying.
       01 DM-TASK-BATCH-STEP.
      *>> Self: the TASK-BATCH handle.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-STEP-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 2 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-STEP-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> actions (const std::vector<double> &): VECTOR-DOUBLE handle.
      *>>   Row-major [size(),action_size()] values in the documented
      *>>   action box.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-STEP-ACTIONS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> mask (const std::vector<std::uint8_t> & = {}): VECTOR-UCHAR
      *>>   handle. Empty selects all; otherwise size() binary bytes.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-STEP-MASK USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const TaskOutput &): TASK-OUTPUT handle (new; close
      *>>   it). Borrowed reusable rollout output; no automatic reset.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-STEP-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::reset(const
      *>>   std::vector<std::uint8_t> & mask = {}) -> const TaskOutput &
      *>> CALL "dm_task_batch_reset" USING DM-TASK-BATCH-RESET DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Restore and perturb selected rows; retain final observations
      *>>   for rollout collectors.
      *>> Clears rewards/end flags for selected rows. Random streams
      *>>   continue between episodes.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::sim::TaskBatch
      *>>   task(dm::sim::Task::InvertedPendulum,2);task.reset({0,1});
      *>> ```
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: Invalid mask.
       01 DM-TASK-BATCH-RESET.
      *>> Self: the TASK-BATCH handle.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-RESET-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Arguments to send: 0 to 1 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 0.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-RESET-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 0.
      *>> mask (const std::vector<std::uint8_t> & = {}): VECTOR-UCHAR
      *>>   handle. Empty selects all; otherwise size() binary bytes.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-RESET-MASK USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (const TaskOutput &): TASK-OUTPUT handle (new; close
      *>>   it). Borrowed reset observations and current unselected
      *>>   rows.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-RESET-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::seed(std::uint64_t seed) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_task_batch_seed" USING DM-TASK-BATCH-SEED DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Reproduce fresh reset draws after explicit reseeding; physics
      *>>   is unchanged until reset.
      *>>
      *>> **Example**
      *>>
      *>> ```cpp
      *>> dm::sim::TaskBatch
      *>>   task(dm::sim::Task::Hopper,1);task.seed(7);task.reset();
      *>> ```
       01 DM-TASK-BATCH-SEED.
      *>> Self: the TASK-BATCH handle.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-SEED-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> seed (std::uint64_t): unsigned long. New batch random seed.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-SEED-SEED USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::cobol_bindings::task_batch_create(datamunge::sim::Task
      *>>   task, std::size_t count, std::size_t workers = 1,
      *>>   std::uint64_t seed = 0, std::uint64_t time_limit = 1000) ->
      *>>   datamunge::sim::TaskBatch *
      *>> CALL "dm_task_batch_create" USING DM-TASK-BATCH-CREATE
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Create an owned native CPU task batch. task is
      *>>   InvertedPendulum or Hopper; count and workers
      *>> must be positive. seed defaults to zero and time_limit to 1000
      *>>   successful episode steps.
       01 DM-TASK-BATCH-CREATE.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 5 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-CREATE-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              2.
      *>> task (datamunge::sim::Task): TASK value (see the 88 levels).
          05 DM-TASK-BATCH-CREATE-TASK USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
             88 DM-TASK-BATCH-CREATE-TASK-INVERTED-PENDULUM VALUE 0.
             88 DM-TASK-BATCH-CREATE-TASK-HOPPER VALUE 1.
