      *>> datamunge::algebra::definite_integral(const Expr & f, const
      *>>   std::string & var, double a, double b, double tolerance =
      *>>   1.0000000000000001E-9, int max_depth = 50) -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_definite_integral" USING DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The definite integral of f (with every other name in f bound
      *>>   as usual by evaluate())
      *>> from a to b with respect to var, via adaptive Simpson's rule
      *>>   -- a numeric fallback/
      *>> complement to Expr::integrate() for cases outside that
      *>>   method's supported symbolic
      *>> forms (e.g. sin(x)*cos(x), or any other integrand it throws
      *>>   on), or simply to check
      *>> a symbolic result. Handles a > b by returning the negated
      *>>   integral over [b, a].
       01 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL.
      *>> Arguments to send: 4 to 6 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 4.
          05 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              4.
      *>> f (const Expr &): EXPR handle.
          05 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL-F USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> var (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL-VAR PIC X(256).
          05 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL-VAR-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE -1.
      *>> a (double): double.
          05 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL-A USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> b (double): double.
          05 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL-B USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> tolerance (double = 1.0000000000000001E-9): double. Target
      *>>   absolute error per the adaptive refinement's own error
      *>>   estimate; not a hard guarantee for a pathological (e.g.
      *>>   discontinuous or highly oscillatory) integrand.
          05 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL-TOLERANCE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> max_depth (int = 50): int. Hard cap on recursive bisection
      *>>   depth, bounding worst-case cost.
          05 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL-MAX-DEPTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double.
          05 DM-DEFINITE-INTEGRAL-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::algebra::taylor_series(const Expr & f, const
      *>>   std::string & var, double center, int order) -> Polynomial
      *>> CALL "dm_taylor_series" USING DM-TAYLOR-SERIES DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> The degree-`order` Taylor polynomial of f around var = center,
      *>>   built from `order`
      *>> repeated symbolic differentiations of f (each evaluated at
      *>>   center and divided by the
      *>> matching factorial) -- the returned polynomial q approximates
      *>>   f near center as
      *>> q.evaluate(x - center), NOT q.evaluate(x) directly (q's
      *>>   coefficients are for powers
      *>> of (x - center), matching the standard Taylor series form
      *>> f(x) ~= sum_k f^(k)(center)/k! * (x-center)^k).
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: if order is negative, or
      *>>   std::invalid_argument propagated from Expr::differentiate()
      *>>   if f contains a non-constant exponent.
       01 DM-TAYLOR-SERIES.
      *>> f (const Expr &): EXPR handle.
          05 DM-TAYLOR-SERIES-F USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> var (const std::string &): text in PIC X(256); -LENGTH -1
      *>>   trims trailing spaces.
          05 DM-TAYLOR-SERIES-VAR PIC X(256).
          05 DM-TAYLOR-SERIES-VAR-LENGTH USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              -1.
      *>> center (double): double.
          05 DM-TAYLOR-SERIES-CENTER USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> order (int): int.
          05 DM-TAYLOR-SERIES-ORDER USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> Result (Polynomial): POLYNOMIAL handle (new; close it).
