      *>> datamunge::algebra::detail::is_negligible_remainder(const
      *>>   Polynomial & r, const Polynomial & scale_reference, double
      *>>   relative_tolerance = 1.0000000000000001E-9) -> bool
      *>> CALL "dm_is_negligible_remainder" USING
      *>>   DM-IS-NEGLIGIBLE-REMAINDER DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> True when every coefficient of `r` is negligible relative to
      *>>   `scale_reference`'s
      *>> largest-magnitude coefficient. The classical Euclidean
      *>>   algorithm's termination test
      *>> (`remainder.is_zero()`) assumes a remainder that is
      *>>   mathematically zero comes back
      *>> as *exactly* zero -- true over an exact field, but not over
      *>>   doubles: a genuine
      *>> (e.g. repeated) common factor can leave a remainder like
      *>>   1.78e-15 instead of 0.0,
      *>> which Polynomial::is_zero()'s exact-equality check treats as a
      *>>   nonzero polynomial,
      *>> making the Euclidean algorithm take one more spurious step and
      *>>   converge on a
      *>> meaningless near-zero-constant "GCD" instead of the true,
      *>>   higher-degree one. Treating
      *>> such a remainder as zero (this function) fixes that without
      *>>   weakening
      *>> Polynomial::is_zero() itself, which is used elsewhere for
      *>>   genuine exact-zero checks
      *>> (e.g. rejecting division by the zero polynomial).
       01 DM-IS-NEGLIGIBLE-REMAINDER.
      *>> Arguments to send: 2 to 3 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 2.
          05 DM-IS-NEGLIGIBLE-REMAINDER-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED
              VALUE 2.
      *>> r (const Polynomial &): POLYNOMIAL handle.
          05 DM-IS-NEGLIGIBLE-REMAINDER-R USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> scale_reference (const Polynomial &): POLYNOMIAL handle.
          05 DM-IS-NEGLIGIBLE-REMAINDER-SCALE-REFERENCE USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> relative_tolerance (double = 1.0000000000000001E-9): double.
          05 DM-IS-NEGLIGIBLE-REMAINDER-RELATIVE-TOLERANCE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result (bool): 0 or 1.
          05 DM-IS-NEGLIGIBLE-REMAINDER-RESULT USAGE BINARY-CHAR
              UNSIGNED.

