          05 DM-SQUARE-FREE-FACTORIZATION-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::algebra::factor_over_reals(const Polynomial & p,
      *>>   double conjugate_tolerance = 9.9999999999999995E-7) ->
      *>>   RealFactorization
      *>> CALL "dm_factor_over_reals" USING DM-FACTOR-OVER-REALS
      *>>   DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Factors p over the reals: splits it into square-free pieces
      *>>   via
      *>> square_free_factorization() (each with its own multiplicity),
      *>>   then finds every root
      *>> of each piece via complex_roots() -- safe here since a
      *>>   square-free piece has, by
      *>> construction, only distinct roots, exactly the case
