      *>>   remainders, const std::vector<double> & moduli) -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_crt" USING DM-CRT DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Chinese Remainder Theorem: the unique x in [0,
      *>>   product(moduli)) such that
      *>> `x == remainders[i] (mod moduli[i])` for every i, given
      *>>   pairwise-coprime positive
      *>> moduli.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: if sizes disagree, are empty, a
      *>>   modulus is non-positive, the moduli aren't pairwise coprime,
      *>>   or the combined modulus would exceed 2^53 (past the point a
      *>>   double can represent every integer exactly).
