      *>> datamunge::bayes::leapfrog_gaussian_acceptance(double
      *>>   step_size, std::size_t num_steps, double sd, std::size_t
      *>>   angles = 4096) -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_leapfrog_gaussian_acceptance" USING
      *>>   DM-LEAPFROG-GAUSSIAN-ACCEPTANCE DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Exact expected Metropolis acceptance of one HMC proposal
      *>>   (fixed step size and
      *>> number of leapfrog steps, unit mass) on a one-dimensional
      *>>
      *>> `N(m,s^2)` target, started
      *>> in equilibrium.
      *>>
      *>> In scaled coordinates `x=((q-m)/s,\,p)` each leapfrog step is
      *>>   the linear map
      *>> `M=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\-h/2&1\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}1&h\\0&1\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\-h/2&1\end{pmatrix}`
      *>> with `h=\varepsilon/s`, `\det M=1` and
      *>>   `\operatorname{tr}M=2-h^2`, so it is stable
      *>> exactly when `\varepsilon<2s`. Writing
      *>>   `x_0=r(\cos\phi,\sin\phi)` the energy error is
      *>> `\Delta H=r^2f(\phi)` with
      *>>   `f=\tfrac12(|M^L(\cos\phi,\sin\phi)|^2-1)`, and because
      *>> `r^2/2\sim\text{Exp}(1)` the radial average of
      *>>   `\min(1,e^{-\Delta H})` is
      *>> `1/(1+2f)` for `f>0` and 1 otherwise. The angle is integrated
      *>>   numerically.
      *>>
      *>> `\varepsilon>0`.
      *>>
      *>> `L\geq1`.
      *>>
      *>> `s>0`.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: for non-positive arguments.
       01 DM-LEAPFROG-GAUSSIAN-ACCEPTANCE.
      *>> Arguments to send: 3 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 3.
          05 DM-LEAPFROG-GAUSSIAN-ACCEPTANCE-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG
              SIGNED VALUE 3.
      *>> step_size (double): double. Leapfrog step size
          05 DM-LEAPFROG-GAUSSIAN-ACCEPTANCE-STEP-SIZE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> num_steps (std::size_t): unsigned long. Number of leapfrog
      *>>   steps
          05 DM-LEAPFROG-GAUSSIAN-ACCEPTANCE-NUM-STEPS USAGE
              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> sd (double): double. Target standard deviation
          05 DM-LEAPFROG-GAUSSIAN-ACCEPTANCE-SD USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> angles (std::size_t = 4096): unsigned long. Number of
      *>>   quadrature angles (at least 8).
          05 DM-LEAPFROG-GAUSSIAN-ACCEPTANCE-ANGLES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE
              UNSIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. The expected acceptance probability.
          05 DM-LEAPFROG-GAUSSIAN-ACCEPTANCE-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> datamunge::bayes::gaussian_importance_efficiency(double scale,
      *>>   int dimension) -> double
      *>> CALL "dm_gaussian_importance_efficiency" USING
      *>>   DM-GAUSSIAN-IMPORTANCE-EFFICIENCY DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Asymptotic effective-sample-size fraction
      *>>
      *>> `N_{\text{eff}}/N` of importance sampling
      *>> a `d`-dimensional Gaussian target with a Gaussian proposal of
      *>>   the same mean and
      *>> covariance scaled by `k^2`.
      *>>
      *>> `N_{\text{eff}}/N\to1/E_q[w^2]` for weights `w=p/q` normalised
      *>>   to mean 1. In one
      *>> dimension `E_q[w^2]=\int p^2/q=k^2/\sqrt{2k^2-1}`, finite only
      *>>   for `k^2>1/2`, and the
      *>> dimensions multiply, giving `\bigl(\sqrt{2k^2-1}/k^2\bigr)^d`.
      *>>   It is 1 at `k=1` and
      *>> 0 (infinite weight variance) for `k\le1/\sqrt2`.
      *>>
      *>> `k>0`.
      *>>
      *>> `d\ge1`.
      *>>
      *>> Errors (a non-zero status):
      *>> - std::invalid_argument: for non-positive `scale` or
      *>>   `dimension`.
       01 DM-GAUSSIAN-IMPORTANCE-EFFICIENCY.
      *>> scale (double): double. Proposal scale factor
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-IMPORTANCE-EFFICIENCY-SCALE USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> dimension (int): int. Dimension
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-IMPORTANCE-EFFICIENCY-DIMENSION USAGE
              BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> Result (double): double. The efficiency in [0, 1].
          05 DM-GAUSSIAN-IMPORTANCE-EFFICIENCY-RESULT USAGE COMP-2.

