      *>> datamunge::cv::dog_blobs(const image::Image & img, int
      *>>   num_scales = 4, double sigma0 = 1.6000000000000001, double
      *>>   threshold = 3.0) -> std::vector<KeyPoint>
      *>> CALL "dm_dog_blobs" USING DM-DOG-BLOBS DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Difference-of-Gaussians blob detection (the detector SIFT
      *>>   keypoints are built on,
      *>> without the orientation/descriptor stages): builds
      *>>   `num_scales` + 1 Gaussian-
      *>> blurred copies of `img` at geometrically-spaced sigma_i =
      *>>   `sigma0` * 2^(i /
      *>> num_scales), subtracts consecutive pairs to get `num_scales`
      *>>   DoG images, then keeps
      *>> every point that is a strict extremum (min or max) among its
      *>>   26 neighbors in the
      *>> resulting (x, y, scale) volume -- 8 in its own DoG layer plus
      *>>   9 in each adjacent
      *>> layer -- and whose |response| exceeds `threshold`. A single
      *>>   octave only (no
      *>> image-halving between octaves like full SIFT) -- simpler, and
      *>>   sufficient for
      *>> detecting blobs across a single order-of-magnitude size range.
       01 DM-DOG-BLOBS.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-DOG-BLOBS-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> img (const image::Image &): IMAGE handle.
          05 DM-DOG-BLOBS-IMG USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> num_scales (int = 4): int.
          05 DM-DOG-BLOBS-NUM-SCALES USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> sigma0 (double = 1.6000000000000001): double.
          05 DM-DOG-BLOBS-SIGMA0 USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> threshold (double = 3.0): double.
          05 DM-DOG-BLOBS-THRESHOLD USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> Result (std::vector<KeyPoint>): VECTOR-KEY-POINT handle (new;
      *>>   close it).
          05 DM-DOG-BLOBS-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

