      *>>   5) -> std::vector<HoughLine>
      *>> CALL "dm_hough_lines" USING DM-HOUGH-LINES DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Standard Hough line transform: every pixel of `img` whose
      *>>   grayscale luma is >= `edge_threshold`
      *>> votes, in a rho-theta accumulator (theta stepped every degree
      *>>   over
      *>> [0, pi), rho stepped every pixel over the image's diagonal
      *>>   range), for every line
      *>> that could pass through it. Returns every accumulator cell
      *>>   with at least `min_votes`,
      *>> non-max-suppressed within a (2*nms_radius+1) rho-theta cell
      *>>   window so a
      *>> single real line doesn't produce a cluster of near-duplicate
      *>>   near-identical results.
      *>> Intended input is an edge map (e.g. image::sobel_edges()'s
      *>>   output), not a raw photo.
       01 DM-HOUGH-LINES.
      *>> Arguments to send: 1 to 4 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 1.
          05 DM-HOUGH-LINES-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> img (const image::Image &): IMAGE handle.
          05 DM-HOUGH-LINES-IMG USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> edge_threshold (int = 128): int.
          05 DM-HOUGH-LINES-EDGE-THRESHOLD USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> min_votes (int = 50): int.
          05 DM-HOUGH-LINES-MIN-VOTES USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> nms_radius (int = 5): int.
          05 DM-HOUGH-LINES-NMS-RADIUS USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<HoughLine>): VECTOR-HOUGH-LINE handle
      *>>   (new; close it).
          05 DM-HOUGH-LINES-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

      *>> datamunge::cv::hough_circles(const image::Image & img, int
      *>>   min_radius, int max_radius, double gradient_threshold =
      *>>   50.0, int min_votes = 20, int nms_radius = 10) ->
      *>>   std::vector<HoughCircle>
      *>> CALL "dm_hough_circles" USING DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Gradient-direction-guided Hough circle transform: for every
      *>>   edge pixel (Sobel
      *>> gradient magnitude >= `gradient_threshold` on `img's`
      *>>   grayscale conversion), and
      *>> for every candidate radius in [`min_radius`, `max_radius`],
      *>>   votes for the two
      *>> candidate centers at that distance along the pixel's gradient
      *>>   line (handles both
      *>> bright-disk-on-dark and dark-disk-on-bright edge polarity).
      *>>   Each radius gets an
      *>> independent 2D (cx, cy) accumulator and non-max suppression
      *>>   pass -- simpler to
      *>> reason about than a combined 3D (cx, cy, r) accumulator, at
      *>>   the cost of not
      *>> suppressing near-duplicate detections across adjacent radii.
       01 DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES.
      *>> Arguments to send: 3 to 6 (C++ defaults fill the rest);
      *>>   initially 3.
          05 DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES-GIVEN USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE 3.
      *>> img (const image::Image &): IMAGE handle.
          05 DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES-IMG USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> min_radius (int): int.
          05 DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES-MIN-RADIUS USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> max_radius (int): int.
          05 DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES-MAX-RADIUS USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> gradient_threshold (double = 50.0): double.
          05 DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES-GRADIENT-THRESHOLD USAGE COMP-2.
      *>> min_votes (int = 20): int.
          05 DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES-MIN-VOTES USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> nms_radius (int = 10): int.
          05 DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES-NMS-RADIUS USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED.
      *>> Result (std::vector<HoughCircle>): VECTOR-HOUGH-CIRCLE handle
      *>>   (new; close it).
          05 DM-HOUGH-CIRCLES-RESULT USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

