      *>> Triangulates a SIMPLE polygon (convex or not, but not
      *>>   self-intersecting) by ear
      *>> clipping: repeatedly finds a "ear" -- a convex vertex whose
      *>>   neighbor-triangle
      *>> contains no other polygon vertex -- clips it off as one output
      *>>   triangle, and
      *>> repeats on the remaining (n-1)-vertex polygon. O(n^3) worst
      *>>   case (each of the O(n)
      *>> clipped ears requires an O(n) scan to verify, each vertex
      *>>   check O(1)) -- unlike
      *>> delaunay_triangulation() (which only sees an unordered point
      *>>   SET), this respects
      *>> the polygon's actual boundary, so it correctly handles concave
      *>>   (non-convex) shapes.
      *>> Every triangle's vertices are indices into `polygon`. Works
      *>>   for any winding order
      *>> (detects and internally corrects clockwise input). Returns
      *>>   empty for fewer than 3
      *>> vertices; a triangle input returns itself unchanged.
