      *>> datamunge::image::write_png(const Image & img, const
      *>>   std::string & path) -> void
      *>> CALL "dm_write_png" USING DM-WRITE-PNG DM-STATUS
      *>>
      *>> Writes `img` as an 8-bit-depth, non-interlaced PNG, using its
      *>>   ImageMode directly as
      *>> the PNG color type (Grayscale/GrayscaleAlpha/RGB/RGBA all have
      *>>   a direct PNG
      *>> equivalent, so no conversion is ever needed). Every scanline
      *>>   is written with filter
      *>> type 0 (None) -- simpler and always correct, at the cost of a
      *>>   somewhat larger file
      *>> than a filter-optimizing encoder would produce; any standard
      *>>   PNG decoder still reads
      *>> the result correctly.
