      *> ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *>   containers and function values

      *>> C++ std::vector<double> (VECTOR-DOUBLE handles).
      *>> CALL "dm_vector_double_new" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
      *>>   (sets -SELF to a new, empty one)
      *>> CALL "dm_vector_double_size" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
      *>>   (sets -SIZE)
      *>> CALL "dm_vector_double_get" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
      *>>   (reads -VALUE at -INDEX)
      *>> CALL "dm_vector_double_set" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
      *>>   (writes -VALUE at -INDEX)
      *>> CALL "dm_vector_double_push" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
      *>>   (appends -VALUE)
      *>> CALL "dm_vector_double_clear" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
      *>>   (removes every element)
       01 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE.
      *>> The VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (new sets it).
          05 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> 1-based position for get and set.
          05 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-INDEX USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE SIGNED VALUE 1.
      *>> The element count (size sets it).
          05 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SIZE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> The element for get, set and push: double.
          05 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE USAGE COMP-2.

      *>> Copies VECTOR-DOUBLE elements to or from a COBOL table of up
      *>>   to 1000 entries.
      *>> CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING
      *>>   DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS (sets -SELF to a new one
      *>>   holding the -COUNT items)
      *>> CALL "dm_vector_double_append_table" USING
      *>>   DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS (adds the -COUNT items to
      *>>   -SELF)
      *>> CALL "dm_vector_double_to_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE
      *>>   DM-STATUS (copies elements from -START, as many as fit, and
      *>>   sets -COUNT)
       01 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE.
      *>> The VECTOR-DOUBLE handle (from_table sets it).
          05 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
      *>> to_table: the 1-based position of the first element to copy.
          05 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-START USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE SIGNED
              VALUE 1.
      *>> The number of -ITEM entries used (to_table sets it).
          05 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT USAGE BINARY-LONG SIGNED VALUE
              0.
          05 DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEMS OCCURS 0 TO 1000 TIMES
